password I gotta memorize.<br /> <br /> Plus Kickstarter\u2019s famous. They\u2019re like a pop culture reference. Comic strips in real newspapers mention Kickstarter and assume the reader knows what they\u2019re talking about. Nobody\u2019s ever heard of Indiegogo.<br /> <br /> Any chance if enough people express how upset they are that they\u2019ll cancel the deal and do it on Kickstarter instead? Or am I tilting at windmills? \ud83d\ude0a (Kinda being silly but I really am annoyed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T05:50:10-08:00","id":1435634,"title":"","content":"But yeah, cowboy mages would be kinda cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T10:41:47-08:00","id":1435671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1435633#post1435633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This means I have to create a whole new account and a whole new password I gotta memorize.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly perfect because of things like this, but better experiment with a supplement than a core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus Kickstarter\u2019s famous.<br /> ...<br /> Nobody\u2019s ever heard of Indiegogo. </div> </div> </div>That seems.... very unfair. Indiegogo is basically the 3rd largest crowdfunding site after KickStarter and GoFundMe. It's not some tiny small potatoes operation. It is smaller than KS, sure, but that's not everything. Indiegogo has around half the users as KS, but on average far more Indiegogo users fund multiple projects. Indiegogo has more payment options. Etc.<br /> <br /> I think it's also fair to say that Onyx Path isn't really getting a lot of new backers on KS just because KS is the biggest company in that market. The number of backers for OPP projects seems pretty baked in, and mostly come from OPP's social media presence. It's worth exploring if the giant number of users on KS (again, most of which only signed up for one thing and rarely back anything else) is actually better for a company with a fairly stable fan base that will probably follow them on a platform switch.<br /> <br /> Indiegogo also isn't a &quot;hit the magic number&quot; system. If a project is struggling, and gets 95% funding, it can still collect in the hopes of making the product and finding the rest through a different avenue, where KS fails your project if you're a cent short of goal (while hyperbole, a small % of KS campaigns that look like they're going to just get funded fail at the last minute because a few backers pull out suddenly at the end). This makes it harder to compare to KS on some metrics because while more KS projects meet funding (though neither site posts terribly great success rates), it's unclear how many in the difference on Indiegogo still succeed because they got close enough despite not hitting the projected target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any chance if enough people express how upset they are that they\u2019ll cancel the deal and do it on Kickstarter instead? Or am I tilting at windmills? </div> </div> </div>Considering it's a stated experiment with a fairly minor supplement? Tilting seems like the answer. If they want to try Indiegogo, some project is going to have to be the one to do it with. Asking OPP to never switch platforms unless forced by something like KS closing shop seems unlikely to be something they'd agree too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T12:28:54-08:00","id":1435687,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> sorry. I was in a bitchy mood when I posted that. Thank you for answering so intelligently. I feel better now after reading that and understanding why they might want to switch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T17:20:11-08:00","id":1435708,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Indiegogo so I'm just curious. What are the differences with KS that they are testing out? Because Victorian Mage is sure to be funded regardless of which site it uses. And even if most KS users only sign up to back one thing, OPP fans have usually backed several projects. Did they talk about their reasons in a Monday Meeting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-16T18:02:43-08:00","id":1435712,"title":"","content":"The MMN mostly mention that Indiegogo is easier on the backend of actually running the campaign. Indiegogo is generally regarded as the more flexible platform for the campaign creator<br /> <br /> I know one big feature for some users is the Indiegogo has native Paypal support, where Kickstarter doesn't. Some international fans live in places where credit cards aren't common, making Kickstarter's limited payment options a problem (this is something that came up in the past when it was clear crowdfunding was going to be an on-going part of OPP's strategy). Paypal integration alone could potential open things to some more people that would be regular backers but aren't now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":