ine to back the week follow the 15th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T18:29:38-08:00","id":1437066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437052#post1437052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's open for another 28 days, so you should be fine to back the week follow the 15th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you kindly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T18:32:39-08:00","id":1437067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437049#post1437049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long is this going to be open? I won't be able to back at the level I need/want until the 15th of March.</div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of time remaining is displayed to the right of the funding bar on the Indiegogo page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T08:45:23-08:00","id":1437240,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: previously published material stated that when the Union was founded, the Celestial Masters and Void Seekers combined to become the Explorators. The latest reveal lists them as still separate Conventions at the founding of the Union. Was the merger postponed a few years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T19:08:55-08:00","id":1437309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437240#post1437240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: previously published material stated that when the Union was founded, the Celestial Masters and Void Seekers combined to become the Explorators. The latest reveal lists them as still separate Conventions at the founding of the Union. Was the merger postponed a few years?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll see how that bears out in future updates. It's a &quot;well, no, but yes&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T02:50:41-08:00","id":1437335,"title":"","content":"Weird question: how is the book giving this much emphasis to Hollow Ones (named as such) when The Hollow Men, from which their name derives, was published in 1925, and the Tradbook for the Hollow Ones says the first cabals of Hollowers formed in the early 1900s? Surely it should all be &quot;precursors to the Hollow Ones&quot; or &quot;Romantic Orphans&quot; or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T08:43:28-08:00","id":1437357,"title":"","content":"They are the Sepulchrals, the Tenebrous in the XIX century. The Victorian Age is too the epoch of the Decadentism, a spirit present in the future Hollow Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T11:22:50-08:00","id":1437369,"title":"","content":"And I find it kind of suspect that the two chapters go a lot into how awful and racist the march of imperialism and colonialism was...and yet lists a work talking about about Madame Blavatasky, who herself propagated the incredibly racist Root Race stuff, to the point of being inspiration of Nazi ideology...and yet nothing is mentioned about that? Aside from a way too forgiving descriptor of &quot;eccentric&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nvm that this is a factoid no unknown to past OPP freelancers, considering even that was mentioned in the CofD Dark Era &quot;Lifting the Veil&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T11:53:42-08:00","id":1437373,"title":"","content":"So with today's reveal, the mystery of the Explorators has been revealed: from 1851 to 1897, the Union consists of Blocs of multiple Conventions each, with the Explorers Society encompassing the Celestial Masters and Void Seekers while the Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers form a separate Bloc of their own. <br /> <br /> The remaining Blocs appear to be the Grand Faculty (the \u00c6sculapean Order and\u2026), the League of Constructors (Brotherhood of Mechanicians and\u2026), and the Ivory Tower (the Lightkeepers and\u2026)<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong, and the Electrodyne Engineers and Analytical Reckoners are folded into these Bolcs. Given their focus on information, I could maybe see the Analytical Reckoners in the Ivory Tower; and the League of Constructors sounds like a group that the Electrodyne Engineers might be a part of. <br /> <br /> I think it's likely, though, that the Invisible Exchequers are in the Ivory Tower. There's also mention of a Golden Guild, which I was thinking was a synonym; but the reveal today says that there's a rivalry between the two. <br /> <br /> More thoughts later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T12:36:40-08:00","id":1437379,"title":"","content":"Also, as I read the preview manuscript, I keep seeing things that seem to wildly violate previous Mage canon, for example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world of the Awakened is vast. The horizons of Earth give way to the distant stars and the depths of the spirit worlds. In times before, the Mystick Traditions could dominate the world seemingly on a whim as magick elevated them above and beyond mortals. The Council of Nine stood at the heart of the Traditions, offering unity of magical practices and so mighty as to seem beyond challenge. Hubris walks hand in hand with power. <br /> <br /> The impossible happened; a Tradition fell, the Nine became Eight, the mystical significance shattered \u2014 and none of the great and powerful on the Council knew what to do. Though engaged in a rabid flurry of activity, proclamations and arguments about the tragedy that had befallen them for months and then years, they did nothing. What had been legendary became disconnected. They ignored and neglected growing threats. </div> </div> </div>The Council of Nine could never seem &quot;beyond challenge&quot; when they formed because everyone was panicking about the nascent Order of Reason. And a Tradition fell like...20 minutes later. The Council wasn't ever really &quot;great and powerful&quot; Is this an intentional retcon? If so, what's the new history of the formation of the Council? Or is this an error that needs to be corrected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T13:34:00-08:00","id":1437385,"title":"","content":"We had an entire gameline (<b>Sorcerers Crusade</b>) that featured a strong Council of Nine. So at the very least, \u201cone Tradition fell like...20 minutes later\u201d is vastly overstating things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T13:58:55-08:00","id":1437386,"title":"","content":"I don't know that I'd call an organization that lost 1 of it's nine groups after executing one of it's leaders after four years strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T14:02:17-08:00","id":1437387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437385#post1437385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had an entire gameline (<b>Sorcerers Crusade</b>) that featured a strong Council of Nine. So at the very least, \u201cone Tradition fell like...20 minutes later\u201d is vastly overstating things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't mind them retconning the Sorcerer's crusade to have lasted more than 4 years...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T14:17:53-08:00","id":1437389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janothar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437386#post1437386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that I'd call an organization that lost 1 of it's nine groups after executing one of it's leaders after four years strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Four years is fairly short, yes; but it's not much shorter than the ten years that the Order of Reason went between its founding and the Solificati abandoning <i>them</i>, roughly a century earlier. <br /> <br /> To me, the loss of a Tradition so soon after the Council was formed said more about the Solificati than about the Council of Nine. Take note, Disparate Alliance; the Children of Knowledge already have two strikes against them\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T15:10:46-08:00","id":1437395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437389#post1437389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Four years is fairly short, yes; but it's not much shorter than the ten years that the Order of Reason went between its founding and the Solificati abandoning <i>them</i>, roughly a century earlier.<br /> <br /> To me, the loss of a Tradition so soon after the Council was formed said more about the Solificati than about the Council of Nine. Take note, Disparate Alliance; the Children of Knowledge already have two strikes against them\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Its about time for them to leave the Disparate Alliance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T15:11:49-08:00","id":1437396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janothar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437379#post1437379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as I read the preview manuscript, I keep seeing things that seem to wildly violate previous Mage canon, for example:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Council of Nine could never seem &quot;beyond challenge&quot; when they formed because everyone was panicking about the nascent Order of Reason. And a Tradition fell like...20 minutes later. The Council wasn't ever really &quot;great and powerful&quot; Is this an intentional retcon? If so, what's the new history of the formation of the Council? Or is this an error that needs to be corrected?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flowery subjective characterization you disagree with does not \u201cwildly violating previous Mage canon\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T16:23:14-08:00","id":1437402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437396#post1437396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flowery subjective characterization you disagree with does not \u201cwildly violating previous Mage canon\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not exactly the first nor the last time that we've had an OPP book that goes overboard on flowery prose that it muddies the water on if it's actually trying to say something about the setting or if it's just a metaphor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:14:54-08:00","id":1437481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janothar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437379#post1437379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as I read the preview manuscript, I keep seeing things that seem to wildly violate previous Mage canon, for example:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Council of Nine could never seem &quot;beyond challenge&quot; when they formed because everyone was panicking about the nascent Order of Reason. And a Tradition fell like...20 minutes later. The Council wasn't ever really &quot;great and powerful&quot; Is this an intentional retcon? If so, what's the new history of the formation of the Council? Or is this an error that needs to be corrected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you're misreading that. The passage says 'and none of the great and powerful <u><i><b>on</b></i></u> the Council knew what to do'. It's not talking about the 'great and powerful' Traditions, it's talking about the mages that sat on the Council who would be powerful elder members of their Traditions, powerful leaders and mages in their own right.<br /> <br /> As for the paragraph before that, it's rather flowery but it is worth noting that when the Nine Traditions came together while it was in response to the rise of the Order of Reason, the Order was only at the dawn of it's ascendancy. There was no guarantee that they would become so dominant. It's also worth noting that before the rise of the Order, the Fellowships that became the Traditions were the dominant force in the World of Mages.<br /> <br /> With that one could make the argument that their failure to properly unite in those early days, leading to the tragedy of the First Cabal and the leaving of the Solificati was the deathknell of their power and dominance, allowing the Order to rise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 03-01-2021, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:18:32-08:00","id":1437483,"title":"","content":"Are the Acharne still CoE, or did they fall in the 18th century?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:56:22-08:00","id":1437491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437483#post1437483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Acharne still CoE, or did they fall in the 18th century?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not brought up. The Cultus Ecstasis are using hellfire clubs though, via the Phantasmagoria cult, who focus on sex and mind-expanding drugs rather than the Acharne's torments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T09:44:50-08:00","id":1437496,"title":"","content":"I've had a very focused idea for a chronicle centered around the modernization/industrialization of agriculture. I am thinking of the main conflict being between the Verbena and various parts of the Technocratic Union. This would be a generational game and the characters can try and keep the industrialization at bay and keep regenerative practices in use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T10:14:04-08:00","id":1437501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437496#post1437496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a very focused idea for a chronicle centered around the modernization/industrialization of agriculture. I am thinking of the main conflict being between the Verbena and various parts of the Technocratic Union. This would be a generational game and the characters can try and keep the industrialization at bay and keep regenerative practices in use.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you haven't already, I recommend reading <i>Seeing Like A State</i> by James C. Scott. It examines the role that authoritarian motivations had in central planning, as it pertains to things like agriculture, the layout of cities, and other avenues.<br /> <br /> Slate Star Codex wrote a <a href=\"https://slatestarcodex.com/2017/03/16/book-review-seeing-like-a-state/\" target=\"_blank\">comprehensive review</a> of the book a while back.<br /> <br /> For multiple reasons, it is apropos to your premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:45:46-08:00","id":1437516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437501#post1437501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't already, I recommend reading <i>Seeing Like A State</i> by James C. Scott. It examines the role that authoritarian motivations had in central planning, as it pertains to things like agriculture, the layout of cities, and other avenues.<br /> <br /> Slate Star Codex wrote a <a href=\"https://slatestarcodex.com/2017/03/16/book-review-seeing-like-a-state/\" target=\"_blank\">comprehensive review</a> of the book a while back.<br /> <br /> For multiple reasons, it is apropos to your premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the recommendation. I'll freely admit my knowledge of the Victorian period is limited to very specific topics, so this will definitely help broaden my knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T13:23:07-08:00","id":1437527,"title":"","content":"I will say this about what I've read with the Traditions chapter, specifically with the two page splats: sub-factions (something that was missing in their M20 core write-ups) that provide a lot more nuanced and morally grey depiction of the Traditions. Even in the CC splat it finally relents with it going \u201cok, no, not everyone in the CC thinks imperialism is Great-for-Everyone\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T13:39:15-08:00","id":1437528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437516#post1437516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the recommendation. I'll freely admit my knowledge of the Victorian period is limited to very specific topics, so this will definitely help broaden my knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Victorian Era is pretty damn big with lots of fascinating events and rapid changes to society. Even if you focus in on a single nation, you're going to see a lot of things going on. Multiple revolutions happened that changed the world. New ideas and philosophies born of the Enlightenment and the revolutions of the late 1700s. Industrialization pushing the world away from the last vestiges of it's Feudal past. Prussia united the German states into an Empire, beating what was seen as Great Land Power of Europe in the process. This is age where the Opium Wars signaled the start of the death spiral of the Qing and Imperial China in general and the rapid industrialization of Japan. This is the age of the American Civil War and the Crimean War, wars that would foreshadow the horrors industrialized war in World War I. Of the British Empire reaching it's greatest heights.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of how that world could deviate and change depending on your game.<br /> <br /> It is an expansive, fascinating era with countless possibilities for players and Storytellers alike, whether playing as Traditionalist, Order or Craft characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T14:02:08-08:00","id":1437532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437527#post1437527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say this about what I've read with the Traditions chapter, specifically with the two page splats: sub-factions (something that was missing in their M20 core write-ups) that provide a lot more nuanced and morally grey depiction of the Traditions. Even in the CC splat it finally relents with it going \u201cok, no, not everyone in the CC thinks imperialism is Great-for-Everyone\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, M20 was missing them because of page count. Technocracy Reloaded will be bringing back the Methodologies for each Convention; so if White Wolf authorizes equivalent books for the Traditions and Disparates (and they might, despite having rejected them once), we can expect that the factions will be in there, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T16:21:09-08:00","id":1437546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437532#post1437532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear, M20 was missing them because of page count.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sentiment I still disagree with... considering I\u2019m sitting over here with Wr20 core, which does list off all the Guild sub-factions and almost all of the Legion sub-factions.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s a book with a much smaller page count then M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T16:37:34-08:00","id":1437549,"title":"","content":"What was originally intended to go into M20 core ended up getting split between M20, Book of Secrets, and Gods and Monsters (and arguably HDYDT) \u2014 and even that wasn't enough, as seen by the fact that faction material for the modern groups still hasn't been published. Wr20 managed with a smaller page count because it had less material that it was trying to cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T17:39:17-08:00","id":1437560,"title":"","content":"I still maintain that M20 probably would have been at least marginally shorter if Phil Brucato had been less verbose. Not to rag on him too much - he's one of Mage's most hard-working advocates - but the writing itself could have been significantly tighter.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, verbosity is very on-brand for Mage, a game about big ideas and deliberate contradictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T17:47:20-08:00","id":1437561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437496#post1437496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a very focused idea for a chronicle centered around the modernization/industrialization of agriculture. I am thinking of the main conflict being between the Verbena and various parts of the Technocratic Union. This would be a generational game and the characters can try and keep the industrialization at bay and keep regenerative practices in use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Captain Swing is a Verbena then? I was certain he was CoX.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T23:55:04-08:00","id":1437583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437549#post1437549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was originally intended to go into M20 core ended up getting split between M20, Book of Secrets, and Gods and Monsters (and arguably HDYDT) \u2014 and even that wasn't enough, as seen by the fact that faction material for the modern groups still hasn't been published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then that's not a good sign of a well put together corebook if necessary material needs to be put into supplements and not in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wr20 managed with a smaller page count because it had less material that it was trying to cover. </div> </div> </div>Not really, considering that it even added new material that wasn't in previous Wraith books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437560#post1437560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still maintain that M20 probably would have been at least marginally shorter if Phil Brucato had been less verbose. Not to rag on him too much - he's one of Mage's most hard-working advocates - but the writing itself could have been significantly tighter.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, verbosity is very on-brand for Mage, a game about big ideas and deliberate contradictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it is, and should have been a lot shorter.<br /> <br /> But no, it shouldn't be too &quot;verbose&quot; if it means creating confusing and contradicting setting and rules that makes the game harder to parse, and in the worse way possible that it drives away players and STs from ever touching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T01:10:02-08:00","id":1437594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437560#post1437560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still maintain that M20 probably would have been at least marginally shorter if Phil Brucato had been less verbose. Not to rag on him too much - he's one of Mage's most hard-working advocates - but the writing itself could have been significantly tighter.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, verbosity is very on-brand for Mage, a game about big ideas and deliberate contradictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he'd be able to do it differently, and it does look like he had a lot of fun and put a lot of passion into it. It's still a solid version of Mage and embodies his vision well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T01:26:12-08:00","id":1437596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437583#post1437583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then that's not a good sign of a well put together corebook if necessary material needs to be put into supplements and not in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not really, considering that it even added new material that wasn't in previous Wraith books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Wraith was drawing on a smaller library than Mage was.<br /> <br /> But perhaps we should take this to another thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T05:08:09-08:00","id":1437612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437561#post1437561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Captain Swing is a Verbena then? I was certain he was CoX.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to look that one up, and based on my in depth Wikipedia reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can easily see &quot;him&quot; as Verbena, along with General Ludd. I could also see both of them as something constructed by entire cabals, to use as a cover story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T08:56:35-08:00","id":1437639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437596#post1437596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that Wraith was drawing on a smaller library than Mage was.<br /> <br /> But perhaps we should take this to another thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems unnecessary to make a whole other thread on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T10:11:20-08:00","id":1437647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437491#post1437491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not brought up. The Cultus Ecstasis are using hellfire clubs though, via the Phantasmagoria cult, who focus on sex and mind-expanding drugs rather than the Acharne's torments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess what I'd do at my table then is establish the Acharne already fell, and that in turn leads to the Phantasmagoria being eyed with suspicion by scandalized fellow Mages, as befits Hellfire Clubs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:42:15-08:00","id":1437666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437647#post1437647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess what I'd do at my table then is establish the Acharne already fell, and that in turn leads to the Phantasmagoria being eyed with suspicion by scandalized fellow Mages, as befits Hellfire Clubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Order of Reason is targeting the Phantasmagoria for their acts of sexual freedom, including persecuting hellfire clubs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:14:14-08:00","id":1437671,"title":"","content":"New set of stretch goals are up.<br /> <br /> -$63k: Digital Wallpaper<br /> -$66k: Jumpstart<br /> -$70k: Companion<br /> <br /> For the companion specifically...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At $70,000 in funding \u2013 Bizarre Tales &amp; Unusual Characters \u2013 A small companion book with playable stories and intriguing ne\u2019er-do-wells will be created and released in a supplemental PDF, which will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the Victorian Mage PDF. </div> </div> </div>Which...to be honest is a bit disappointing if that's what they're starting with for the Companion book if it's just plot/chronicle hooks and NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:20:23-08:00","id":1437675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437671#post1437671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New set of stretch goals are up.<br /> <br /> -$63k: Digital Wallpaper<br /> -$66k: Jumpstart<br /> -$70k: Companion<br /> <br /> For the companion specifically...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which...to be honest is a bit disappointing if that's what they're starting with for the Companion book if it's just plot/chronicle hooks and NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well they mentioned in the Onyx Pathcast there isn't going to be a lot in terms of new mechanics (there wasn't for Victorian Age Vampire either!). A guess a lot more Artifacts/Devices could be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T12:31:19-08:00","id":1437677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437675#post1437675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well they mentioned in the Onyx Pathcast there isn't going to be a lot in terms of new mechanics (there wasn't for Victorian Age Vampire either!). A guess a lot more Artifacts/Devices could be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they? Because I think Watson's interview on Mage: the Podcast suggested the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T13:51:19-08:00","id":1437692,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting to see what they do with the Magick chapter in the manuscript. I know an early draft had something about every Tradition having a \u201cminor Sphere\u201d (a notion that was last seen on the MRev Storyteller's Handbook, which was all about optional rules to change the feel of the game); and while I <i>suspect</i> that's been dropped, I'm not going to 100% rule it out as a possibility. <br /> <br /> Still, it's possible that there's enough room on the core book to fit whatever new mechanics they have in mind for Victorian Mage, leaving nothing for the Companion. We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T16:19:45-08:00","id":1437714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437647#post1437647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I'd do at my table then is establish the Acharne already fell, and that in turn leads to the Phantasmagoria being eyed with suspicion by scandalized fellow Mages, as befits Hellfire Clubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd run it that the Acharne was in the process of falling. That way, the players are allowed to get involved in it.<br /> <br /> There's no wasted opportunity more frustrating than being told about a potentially interesting plot development that the Storytellers and Players are not invited to participate in.<br /> <br /> (Note I said &quot;invited&quot;. The ST can obviously do whatever they want. My issue is that the books that describe the events in question don't give any help to STs for doing so. The writers didn't think to include the ST and Players, because they didn't want to spend the time, or because they wanted it a forgone conclusion, rather than something the Players could interfere with.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T19:09:22-08:00","id":1437729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437677#post1437677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they? Because I think Watson's interview on Mage: the Podcast suggested the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>My name is Ian.<br /> <br /> I don't recall speaking overmuch about mechanics other than a few Victorian-flavoured versions of things we already have, like the Straits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T20:07:49-08:00","id":1437739,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-02-2021, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T20:27:35-08:00","id":1437741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437714#post1437714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd run it that the Acharne was in the process of falling. That way, the players are allowed to get involved in it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>true but we do have the Black Willow Society to do roughly the same story with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T08:17:52-08:00","id":1437814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437369#post1437369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I find it kind of suspect that the two chapters go a lot into how awful and racist the march of imperialism and colonialism was...and yet lists a work talking about about Madame Blavatasky, who herself propagated the incredibly racist Root Race stuff, to the point of being inspiration of Nazi ideology...and yet nothing is mentioned about that? Aside from a way too forgiving descriptor of &quot;eccentric&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nvm that this is a factoid no unknown to past OPP freelancers, considering even that was mentioned in the CofD Dark Era &quot;Lifting the Veil&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blavatsky's not given a pass, it turns out; there's a faction of Theosophical Hollow Ones, and their racism (and Blavatsky's) is called out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 03-03-2021, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T12:40:20-08:00","id":1437849,"title":"","content":"I was really impressed with the write-ups for the Order of Reason and the Crafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T19:30:51-08:00","id":1437903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437729#post1437729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My name is Ian.<br /> <br /> I don't recall speaking overmuch about mechanics other than a few Victorian-flavoured versions of things we already have, like the Straits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, noted. Guess we'll have to wait on that chapter getting released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T20:34:57-08:00","id":1437910,"title":"","content":"*reads through the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...why? Why are we going all the way back to the 1e take of &quot;The Technocracy/Order of Reason are Objectively Evil&quot;? To the point of the sidebar ending with &quot;if you try to have OoR PCs depicted as heroic and sympathetic, you're playing them Wrong&quot;. If that's the case then...why even have them as a playable option? Why not just relegate them to the Antagonists chapter and only as NPCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T22:01:43-08:00","id":1437916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437910#post1437910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads through the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...why? Why are we going all the way back to the 1e take of &quot;The Technocracy/Order of Reason are Objectively Evil&quot;? To the point of the sidebar ending with &quot;if you try to have OoR PCs depicted as heroic and sympathetic, you're playing them Wrong&quot;. If that's the case then...why even have them as a playable option? Why not just relegate them to the Antagonists chapter and only as NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e\u2019s evil Technocrats were cartoon villains. These evil Technocrats are just the accurate representation of European Imperialists. There is no way to pretend they aren\u2019t evil without making a book of imperialist-apologist lies (which I\u2019m aware a good portion of steampunk and similar imperial fetishist settings do, even if they are lies of omission). They are mass starving Ireland and India on purpose due to the \u201crationalist\u201d theories of Malthus to make a better world. Any \u201cbut they also do good thing [X]\u201d is just \u201cHitler loved dogs\u201d level of irrelevant after that threshold.<br /> <br /> you can play members of an Imperialist faction without white-washing Imperialism. That\u2019s literally the second most played and supported option in Exalted for example.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to play upper class English high society, you already wanted to play members of a evil genocidal institution, the Union reflecting that is just being honest about this era of world history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-04-2021, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T22:23:52-08:00","id":1437917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437910#post1437910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads through the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...why? Why are we going all the way back to the 1e take of &quot;The Technocracy/Order of Reason are Objectively Evil&quot;? To the point of the sidebar ending with &quot;if you try to have OoR PCs depicted as heroic and sympathetic, you're playing them Wrong&quot;. If that's the case then...why even have them as a playable option? Why not just relegate them to the Antagonists chapter and only as NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Victorian Age is a grim time, and the Chorus Celestial and Order of Hermes (at the very least) are given just as much grief for thier complicity in European Imperialism. <br /> <br /> The Order/Union of this era as a whole represents probably the absolute nadir of their morality. No matter how you slice it, the dominant powers of the age were definitely in bed with industry and finance, and were busy committing probably the highest density of wanton atrocity against civilians ever seen in human history. <br /> <br /> Reading the writeups for the Blocs and Conventions, the Celestial Masters, Electrodyne Engineers, Analytical Reckoners, International Brotherhood of Machinists, and Hippocratic Circle are all portrayed as having several great virtues and ways in which they could actually start *fighting* oppression, besides contributing largely to benign pursuits like infrastructure and medicine, instead of the bloody-handed Void Seekers or the rapacious Invisible Exchequers. Not to mention the Blue Cog Cognate and the contacts of the Children of Kabezya-Mpungu, which paint a picture of the Order containing quite a bit more ethical complexity than one might initially assume.<br /> <br /> Individuals and even whole groups can do real good, and the book acknowledged this, but the Order as a larger entity has grown cruel and monstrous. You can give in and become a monster, you can fight from within, or you can break away, but you simply cannot remain ignorant forever. This isn't a moratorium on PC's from the Conventions, it's an ultimatum: if you want to rescue the dreams of True Science from the jaws of Empire, you're probably gonna have to kill the management. And that's something Union fans have been well aware of since 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T23:28:42-08:00","id":1437920,"title":"","content":"Wait: the Affinity Spheres of the Analytical Reckoners <i>don't include Correspondence</i>? That's <i>got</i> to be an oversight, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T23:37:39-08:00","id":1437921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437920#post1437920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait: the Affinity Spheres of the Analytical Reckoners <i>don't include Correspondence</i>? That's <i>got</i> to be an oversight, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe, but keep in mind that the Digital Web was unknown to them at the time. The idea of telecommunications tech being able to functionally collapse distances was just a twinkle in an Electrodyne's eye, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T23:48:11-08:00","id":1437922,"title":"","content":"I'm not thinking of the Digital Web. I'm thinking more about Geometry. And bear in mind that telegraphs <i>are</i> a thing in the Victorian Age; though you have a point about it being an Electrodyne Engineer innovation. That said, I can definitely see the Analytical Reckoners latching into it, through the likes of Morse Code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T00:10:05-08:00","id":1437928,"title":"","content":"The Chorus Celestial writeup really presents a solely Christian European framework. That's worth addressing OR EMBRACING. If the latter, it would be interesting to cover the Vishnudharadhara and other non-Christian future Chorusters and not considering themselves party to the same tradition in this era because of the aggressive missionary work and are effectively Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T00:11:38-08:00","id":1437929,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that when we get to the chapter on Magick, it will address the Technocratic Variants. Specifically, when did they emerge? I'd peg Dimensional Science to Tychoides' surgery of the Solar System and the emergence of Tychoidean Cosmology, in 1897; Data <i>may</i> originate as late as the discovery of the Digital Web in the early 20th century; but I could possibly see it emerge considerably earlier, maybe as early as the founding of the Analytical Reckoners (thought probably not quite <i>that</i> really). And Primal Utility? No idea when that one emerged. It may even predate the Victorian Age, for all I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T00:20:18-08:00","id":1437930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437928#post1437928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chorus Celestial writeup really presents a solely Christian European framework. That's worth addressing OR EMBRACING. If the latter, it would be interesting to cover the Vishnudharadhara and other non-Christian future Chorusters and not considering themselves party to the same tradition in this era because of the aggressive missionary work and are effectively Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're not yet part of the Choir Celestial, it poses the question of when they join and why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T01:01:04-08:00","id":1437931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437930#post1437930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not yet part of the Choir Celestial, it poses the question of when they join and why.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would assume the strengthening Union on one side, and the ascent of more tolerant universalist Chorusters over the Septarians meaning that non-Christian theurgists could take positions of power in the tradition.<br /> <br /> Oh, another thing that may be worth examining is if the reason the Septarians are so powerful in this era is if they got an influx of Gabrielites in after the Albertan Reformation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T01:21:26-08:00","id":1437933,"title":"","content":"I wish there were more crafts with an alternative timeline of one of the Technocrafts Joining the council and the &quot;Mad Science&quot; tradition basically is MUCH more diverse to start..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T01:41:06-08:00","id":1437935,"title":"","content":"I want to recommend &quot;Foragers, Farmers, and Fossil Fuels&quot; a fascinating book on the evolution of values. The author admits his argument is reductionist, but fairly explains why it has to be reductionist. The relevance is that the Victorian period was a time of transition as our own time is. Their actions made our present changes in values possible. The book I'm recommending will help you see some of the long sweep of what happened and is still happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T09:06:17-08:00","id":1437966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437910#post1437910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads through the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...why? Why are we going all the way back to the 1e take of &quot;The Technocracy/Order of Reason are Objectively Evil&quot;? To the point of the sidebar ending with &quot;if you try to have OoR PCs depicted as heroic and sympathetic, you're playing them Wrong&quot;. If that's the case then...why even have them as a playable option? Why not just relegate them to the Antagonists chapter and only as NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the sidebar is <b><i>not</i> </b>&quot;The Order of Reason is objectively evil.&quot; The point of the sidebar is &quot;19th-century imperialism was objectively harmful to nearly everyone outside a narrowly defined political-economic elite, and the real-world objectives and tactics of 19th-century imperialists cannot be plausibly separated from those of the fictional Order of Reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:38:36-08:00","id":1437976,"title":"","content":"Six toMAYtoes, half a dozen toMAHtoes. I'm not saying that the point about imperialism is wrong; it isn't. But the effect is the same: the box in question \u2014 and the general tone of the book, for that matter \u2014 ends up saying \u201cVictorian Mage is <i>about</i> the evils of imperialism, and the Technocracy embodies that.\u201d In fact, the box in question goes the extra step of stripping away the usual \u201cread between the lines of a biased narrator\u201d approach that's traditionally been used for the Technocracy, and flat-out lectures the reader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T11:07:42-08:00","id":1437985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437976#post1437976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six toMAYtoes, half a dozen toMAHtoes. I'm not saying that the point about imperialism is wrong; it isn't. But the effect is the same: the box in question \u2014 and the general tone of the book, for that matter \u2014 ends up saying \u201cVictorian Mage is <i>about</i> the evils of imperialism, and the Technocracy embodies that.\u201d In fact, the box in question goes the extra step of stripping away the usual \u201cread between the lines of a biased narrator\u201d approach that's traditionally been used for the Technocracy, and flat-out lectures the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently that's necessary since people habitually fall for the biased narration when it comes the Union in particular, and in this book that would mean marketing Imperialist apologism, which not being absolute monsters, they don't want to do.<br /> <br /> The average Western audience member watches Temple of Doom without realizing it's a bunch of lies defending real historic genocide (I mean they know the specific events are fiction of course, but I mean the presentation of the backwards Indians and the enlightened heroic British who come in is the cavalry at the end of the film, or people starving in India at the time period in question being the fault of other Indians rather than the British). British mainstream society still won't recognize the genocides their nation's comparative affluence is built on as genocides. Hell I'm not even sure the majority of people in the anglosphere outside Ireland realize the Great Famine was intentional British policy and not just a natural disaster. The Russo brothers legit thought Thanos was a tragic fanatic with understandable motivation but unacceptable actions toward those ends - despite being an objectively wrong Malthusian. The Human Geography teacher I replaced in my current job literally had a unit dedicated to overpopulation LIKE IT WAS A REAL THING! The last President Bush literally said on live television that &quot;the US has never been at nation of conquerers&quot; - which resulted in every social studies teacher I know having to lie down for an hour. Since Imperial apologism for the West and Malthusianism is still believed in the mainstream, they can't really expect most of the audience to read between the lines on those.<br /> <br /> I'm not opposed to White Man's Burden dialogue samples to better understand how atrocities get rationalized (I love me some Rudyard Kippling!), but in the context of the book also stating the actual reality clearly and explicitly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T11:45:41-08:00","id":1437991,"title":"","content":"Note: Overpopulation can be real. It just isn't what they used to worry about. When the Medieval Climate Anomaly suddenly went away, the Inuit suffered brutally, but the Norse Greenlanders suddenly found that they could no longer feed themselves or their cattle. They experienced overpopulation relative to their resources. Many cultures have experienced environmental changes that collapsed their ability to feed themselves. The higher the population, the more brutal the collapse. Imperialism has several times caused this type of overpopulation by forcing improper farming methods on the people (many late 19th century Indian famines,) or by warping the local society and economy ( Ireland in the 1840s and after).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:30:23-08:00","id":1438010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437910#post1437910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*reads through the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure but the title also calls this to mind (this is from a British comedy show) <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hn1VxaMEjRU\" data-code=\"hn1VxaMEjRU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hn1VxaMEjRU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:44:20-08:00","id":1438014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437916#post1437916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to play upper class English high society, you already wanted to play members of a evil genocidal institution, the Union reflecting that is just being honest about this era of world history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are they a playable option at all?<br /> <br /> Frankly if this is the stance the book is going to take about the Order of Reason, and if the developers were that concerned about OoR being used by bad faith players...<br /> <br /> They shouldn't be a playable option. Period.<br /> <br /> Remove their chapter and stick it in the Antagonists section, remove that choice period from players completely, and make it a Traditions and Crafts only time period.<br /> <br /> Otherwise as is, it's sending mixed messages on what the intent of playable OoR are. And at face value saying that &quot;only play OoR if your table agrees to play Evil Mages&quot; from OOC point of view restricts the kind of chronicles and stories that could be told at individual tables, which frankly is bad for everyone.<br /> <br /> (going to put a pin on OoR for now, since I'm not done reading this chapter)<br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> I HAVE, however, finished reading the Traditions chapter and....it's a mixed bag.<br /> <br /> -<b>Ahl-i-Batin</b>: So right off the bat...the write-up mentions that Batini are heavily involved with the Ottoman Empire...and considering how much they shit talk Western Imperialism that's kind of an issue since Ottomans were engaged in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantinople_massacre_of_1821\" target=\"_blank\">their own atrocities</a> before and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamidian_massacres\" target=\"_blank\">during this time period</a> (nvm the ones that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_Genocide\" target=\"_blank\">they're going to do after the Victorian era...</a>) Some of these atrocities that should be the kind to get Choristors and Greek Euthanatoi to stick the Batini on their Shit List.<br /> <br /> So either this is inconsistent writing, or the Batini are in denial that the Ottomans are failing and refuse to acknowledge their crimes.<br /> <br /> ...but apart from that, the rest of the write up is actually pretty solid. Particularly the sub-faction listed that sounds like a proto-version of the Paradise Garden. That the way how they describe interacting with Ottoman politics, using Mind Effects to either influence particular politicians or flush out corrupt ones, describing their use of Corr Effects by comparing it to telegrams, and even saying that they're leaning to learning technomancy...it makes them sound like mystical-NWO. Which is actually a far more interesting take then just M20 core's &quot;wandering ascetics that believe in Unity&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's honestly to the point that it makes me consider playing one, clicking with me in a way that the M20 write-up didn't.<br /> <br /> (and more justification for me on the &quot;sub-factions should have been mentioned in M20 core&quot;)<br /> <br /> -<b>Akashics</b>: Very amused at painting them as folk heroes which in the context of this era...yeah, sure I'd be up for some Drunken Master 2 and Ip Man shenanigans (yes I'm aware the Ip Man movies take place decades after the Victorian Era, hush now. It's still about a folk hero taking on imperialist forces, just a different one). Also, am glad for at least the mention of Akashics operating in Asian immigrant communities.<br /> <br /> Although I am weirded out how the Boxer Rebellion Future Fates sidebar...seems to be trying to downplay it which is odd.<br /> <br /> -<b>Celestial Chorus</b>: As I said further upthread, yeah I'm digging how their actual splat write-up gives them more nuance and doesn't say that ALL of the Choristors are up for converting the &quot;&quot;&quot;savages&quot;&quot;&quot; to a more civilized way of belief. And even then, it is at least grounded in the Choristor's fear of their Paradigm being eroded away, and doing whatever it takes to preserve it.<br /> <br /> -<b>Dreamspeakers</b>: I'm...mixed on the Dreamspeakers.On the one hand, their write up does highlight other animist cultures and takes more step to distance itself as &quot;the Native American group&quot;. But that not only have all Dreamspeakers across the world have been in communication with each other, but all of them mutually agree to be united against colonialism seems...way too clean.<br /> <br /> Especially since DSs have always been depicted as having the loosest/non-existent organization of all the Traditions, but they all agreed to the same thing.<br /> <br /> I get what the write-up is going for: that out of all the Traditions the DSs would be impacted the most by colonialism. And that they would try to make a unified front to combat it...I think it's just stretching credibility way too much that they all unanimously agree on it, and with the Tradition known for being the least organized. And at worse it dips into problematic race color-blinding.<br /> <br /> -<b>Ecstatics/Sahajiya</b>: A bit whelmed. Feels about the same as they are in modern day Mage. Not much to say, honestly. I get the angle of wanting people to break free from stuffy and constricting Victorian social norms, it's just that context isn't drastically different enough from how they are in a present day game.<br /> <br /> -<b>Euthanatoi/Chakravanti</b>: This actually makes a bigger effort to clearly thread the needle on the relationship between the Death and Fate aspects of the Entropy sphere in how the Euthanatoi view it and it's great. The bit about them taking on the role of anti-heroes and vigilantes...like the classic Western gunslinger. It's not bad by any stretch, just surprising. Like, it's definitely a strange association to imagine an Euthanatoi as The Man with No Name, Doc Holliday, or Sanjuro<br /> <br /> -<b>Order of Hermes</b>: ...and I'm disappointed that this went almost too far into &quot;all Hermetics are complicit in colonialism and think Western Imperialism is Great-for-Everyone&quot;. To the point that if a group takes this depiction of them as is, and for whatever reason they don't have access to other depictions of the Hermetics, there'd be the sense of &quot;ok, so you're playing the Villain of the game&quot;. Or at worse, with the other Traditions being so against...why would any of them want to work with the Hermetics?<br /> <br /> Only time I could see this as an exception is if you do a game set in the heart of the British Empire and having everyone in the cabal be attached/hiding among the occultist and spiritualist movement and circles (so being with an Ecstatic, a Verbena), but with the whole conceit of the book's setting being about looking at people of groups and communities that aren't white Europeans or any other group who benefits directly from colonialism, that's going to severely limit the kind of games to have a Hermetic in. Not without Golden Ruling all over them.<br /> <br /> (also, counter to all the other Traditions listed, incredibly disappointed that it lists of the names of Hermetic Houses but...doesn't actually say anything about them)<br /> <br /> -<b>Verbena</b>: Same as Ecstatics: for the most part being pretty similar too their modern day counterparts and nothing too exciting and different to go over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":".  Edited to re add some incomplete thoughts. 03-05-2021, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:13:19-08:00","id":1438019,"title":"","content":"What I don't understand is why they're treating the Ecstatics with kid gloves, when they seem more than happy to hold every other Western European-based faction accountable for their role in colonialism and imperialism. <br /> <br /> I get wanting to air on the side of caution when portraying cultures that were pillaged and brutalized by the imperial powers, but I don't think the largely upper class epicurean culture of the time really fits that description. Hellfire clubs are hardly emancipatory for 99% of the population, and the primary function of Phantasmagoria performances was essentially bread and circuses. And that's not even getting into the Opium Wars.<br /> <br /> But their writeup is literally like &quot;nah, it's not really their fault, that's an OoR smear campaign and it's actually all the fault of all the OTHER European magi&quot;, which feels not only lopsided, but like the very same Imperial apologetics that the rest of the book bends over backwards to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:57:43-08:00","id":1438030,"title":"","content":"Just finished the Order of Reason and it was about what I expected. To echo what others have said, this is the Order at it's morally darkest, perhaps the darkest of the entire combined history of the Order and the Union. This is not the halcyon days of the Renaissance and their noble beginnings, this is the Order drunk off Victory and Power and Corruption. While without doubt there are noble groups and individuals within every Bloc and Convention, the Order they all work for has become a monster, driving the engines of Industrialization and Imperialism across the globe, with all the good and bad that entails.<br /> <br /> All and all, I love how the Order was handled in this chapter. We see how their ideals have become twisted and corrupted, driving them to backing some very awful ideas in this time. We can see where the future Technocracy came from and it's not a pretty sight. Even the Void Seekers were involved with the darker side of their explorations, something their modern counterparts would deny which for me adds more character to both the Seekers and their successors. <br /> <br /> And yet, the noble ideas that birthed the Order of Reason still remain beneath the blood and dirt that soaks the Order during this era. Just as with the era itself, there is more going on with the Order than blood-soaked Imperialism and the remorseless grinding engine of Industrialization. New ideas and technologies are making the lives of the Masses better. Advances in medicine are treating and curing diseases that plagued people in earlier times. Developments in communications and travel technology is bringing the world closer together. Political and social ideas born of the previous century are being developed and refined. The Middle Class is growing as old Feudal ways of thinking are fading away.<br /> <br /> It's changing, complicated time for the World and the Order. Good and Bad walk hand in hand here. The Good of what's being done does not absolve the Bad being done but at the same time, the Bad does not erase the Good. <br /> <br /> The Chapter is not painting the Victorian Order of Reason as evil monolith of greedy Imperialists and blackhearted villains but simply as people. People that are products of their time and are as flawed as anyone else.<br /> <br /> Anyway on to less depressing talk...<br /> <br /> The Blocs within the Order are an interesting idea. I wasn't entirely sure if I was going to like them or not but I ended up liking them. They add an interesting layer to the politics of the Order and could be intriguing to explore within chronicles and fiction. The Conventions themselves are... well the Conventions of the Order. We had long known most of them from previous books even if some of them have become the Blocs of this era instead. The Golden Guild being the one exception as we had know the Syndicate predecessor as just the Invisible Exchequers. Though they did turn the Skeleton Keys into Awakened investigators prior to joining the Order which I'm fairly certain was a retcon. But that's not a big sticking point for me as now we'd be potentially playing them and having them all or mostly being unAwakened would be potentially limiting and annoying. Though I will admit it does undermine the original awesomeness of the Keys being just ordinary men and women investigating and facing down the evils of the WoD.<br /> <br /> When I first saw that High Guild had been split into the Golden Guild and the Invisible Exchequers, I didn't get why we needed them split other than their Bloc needed another group within it. Then I got to their sections and better understood. This is the age that Wall Street and other modern financial institutions were born and would be a different beast from the businesses that the older High/Golden Guild leaders would be more familiar with, leading to the rise of younger minds that do understand these new concepts.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit that the Electrodyne Engineers using the symbol of the Craftmasons is a bit on the nose for my liking. It feels more like something the modern SoE would claim, that they are true successors of the Craftmasons and their ideals, than something that would have actually happened. Plus it did kind of come across like they were saying that the Engineers are the lone 'good guys' of the Luminaries of this era which I don't think should be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T16:45:59-08:00","id":1438046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438010#post1438010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure but the title also calls this to mind (this is from a British comedy show)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One technocrat to another: See, that proves we're not the bad guys!, we definitely don't have skulls in our elegant suits. Now, Control it's calling you to room 101<br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T01:17:47-08:00","id":1438082,"title":"","content":"One issue with the moral discussion going on, is there is the 21st century moral position (which includes the view that much of the colonial activity was not a good thing), this is balanced against the moral view of the period, that what was being done was very acceptable. The issues highlight to me are more a warning about the difference between the two moral views, and a warning to not use them as a excuse to go against current moral view for the sake of it, and if doing so, to do so with some awareness of what one is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T01:52:19-08:00","id":1438085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438082#post1438082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue with the moral discussion going on, is there is the 21st century moral position (which includes the view that much of the colonial activity was not a good thing), this is balanced against the moral view of the period, that what was being done was very acceptable. The issues highlight to me are more a warning about the difference between the two moral views, and a warning to not use them as a excuse to go against current moral view for the sake of it, and if doing so, to do so with some awareness of what one is doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's certainly an argument to be made for revisionist genre fiction as a way for marginalized creators to reappropriate and recontextualize otherwise potentially harmful genre tropes. <br /> <br /> But given that MtAs is basically a game ABOUT the evolution of the cultural zeitgeist and its ramifications, I think that move would be a little weird here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T03:28:12-08:00","id":1438099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438082#post1438082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> this is balanced against the moral view of the period, that what was being done was very acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very acceptable for Europe, perhaps. I don't think the cultures that were at the bad end of Brit guns were so happy about it.<br /> <br /> Our moral doesn't come from a vacuum, peoples on the short end of imperialism getting more of a voice it's part of why it isn't so PC anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T07:11:28-08:00","id":1438119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438099#post1438099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very acceptable for Europe, perhaps. I don't think the cultures that were at the bad end of Brit guns were so happy about it.<br /> <br /> Our moral doesn't come from a vacuum, peoples on the short end of imperialism getting more of a voice it's part of why it isn't so PC anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree fully","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T09:19:57-08:00","id":1438130,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned earlier - Exalted does a good job presenting imperialism as an evil horrific force and making members of those institutions fully playable. Its the second most popular option for play in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T09:24:09-08:00","id":1438131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1437991#post1437991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: Overpopulation can be real. It just isn't what they used to worry about. When the Medieval Climate Anomaly suddenly went away, the Inuit suffered brutally, but the Norse Greenlanders suddenly found that they could no longer feed themselves or their cattle. They experienced overpopulation relative to their resources. Many cultures have experienced environmental changes that collapsed their ability to feed themselves. The higher the population, the more brutal the collapse. Imperialism has several times caused this type of overpopulation by forcing improper farming methods on the people (many late 19th century Indian famines,) or by warping the local society and economy ( Ireland in the 1840s and after).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would strongly dispute those latter cases being examples of overpopulation (the Greenland example I agree with) - that's what the British blamed for the problems they'd (intentionally) caused via the means you correctly identified. But Ireland was growing more than enough food to feed itself during the Great Famine, but it was on land owned by English Protestants and said crops were exported to English markets, the very workers who grew the food not being able to afford to buy it. That's hardly a population problem. Nor is the English literally restricting aide from other countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T14:53:23-08:00","id":1438176,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s really weird actually that the whole Order of Reason chapter doesn\u2019t include the words<br /> <br /> - Eugenics<br /> - Social Darwinism<br /> - Race Theory<br /> - Galton<br /> - Malthus/Malthusianism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:40:55-08:00","id":1438223,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve given feedback with some of my suggestions, but I may end up writing a Vault expansion including more villainous aspects of the Hippocratic Circle, more exploration of the Gabrielites and how their devout didn\u2019t magically vanish when they were disbanded, more exploration of the politics around Ether, and some alternate/additional Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T19:46:32-08:00","id":1438224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438223#post1438223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve given feedback with some of my suggestions, but I may end up writing a Vault expansion including more villainous aspects of the Hippocratic Circle, more exploration of the Gabrielites and how their devout didn\u2019t magically vanish when they were disbanded, more exploration of the politics around Ether, and some alternate/additional Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see that. We already have the Templars as one example of a post-Gabrielite group, but you're right that there could be others. And while I'm not too upset if Galton's &quot;theories&quot; and related nonsense doesn't get called out by name (I can do that myself, too), there is absolutely room for fan-written explorations of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:40:24-08:00","id":1438233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bob the Skull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438224#post1438224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to see that. We already have the Templars as one example of a post-Gabrielite group, but you're right that there could be others. And while I'm not too upset if Galton's &quot;theories&quot; and related nonsense doesn't get called out by name (I can do that myself, too), there is absolutely room for fan-written explorations of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there\u2019s something definitely worth exploring in why the Chorus Celestial is currently dominated by (small-o) orthodox Christians carrying out purges of heretics, when that\u2019s literally why the Messianic Voice schismed into the Cabal of Pure Thought and the Chorus Celestial in the first place. I\u2019m not saying ex-Gabrielites are in the driver\u2019s seat, but I do think there\u2019s a factor where when a political party collapses, the party that usurps its place is generally shaped into those they replaced (see the rise of National Republicans in the US being indistinguishable from the Federalists despite being nominally the party of Jefferson). So the Chorus Celestial moving to seize the Gabrielites positions of power in institutional churches and (small-o) orthodox missionary campaigns, and inevitably gaining those newly awakened conservative Christian theurgists who would have in the past joined the Gabrielites, play a role here.<br /> <br /> and the \u201cOrder of the knights of the Last Temple\u201d sure sound like the \u201cPoor Knights of the Temple of Solomon\u201d don\u2019t they?!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also considering writing the Vishnudharadhara as currently a Craft, but formerly Chorusters, on the idea they renounced alignment with the European Christians over their support of British missionaries. They\u2019re still loosely tied to the Traditions through their Asthika bonds with the Chakravanti and the Sahajiya.<br /> <br /> obviously when the Monists and liberal Christians retake control of the Chorus, repairing these bonds with non-Christians on the receiving end of Septarian backed missionaries will be a top priority to restore to the Chorus to its true mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:56:56-08:00","id":1438238,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the Doylean reason for it is that it's already been firmly established that the Order of Reason went solidly atheistic in the Victorian Age (see the demise of the Gabrielites in the 1830s), and that left the Choir Celestial as the last major Christian mage faction standing \u2014 meaning that if you're going to talk about the missionary branch of the evils of imperialism, it's the Chorus or nothing. Thus the reason why the Chorus kind of feels like an adjunct to the Technocratic Union in this material. <br /> <br /> (The Order of Hermes suffers from a similar repurposing, as there's nothing in the Union that could be used to represent the various elitist mystical societies that served as the mystical arm of imperialism. The net result is that the Hermetics and Choristers end up being portrayed as largely complicit in the Union's goals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:27:36-08:00","id":1438254,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also considering a setting hack to let the Gabrielites last until the Victorian Reformation as part of the Ivory Tower, and rewrite the Chorus Celestial with the current Pontifex Maximus being a New England Transcendentalist<br /> <br /> Oh god, I just realized I\u2019ll need to write a section on Mormon Chorusters and various disputed theories about Joseph Smith\u2019s Awakened status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-06-2021, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T15:08:42-08:00","id":1438370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438176#post1438176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s really weird actually that the whole Order of Reason chapter doesn\u2019t include the words<br /> <br /> - Eugenics<br /> - Social Darwinism<br /> - Race Theory<br /> - Galton<br /> - Malthus/Malthusianism</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the goals of the Progenitors (I forget the Victorian name) the first is particularly bizarre. The Syndicate is virtually a celebration of the second, so that omission is every bit as weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T15:13:08-08:00","id":1438372,"title":"","content":"By the way, having read works like &quot;Strange and Secret Peoples&quot; and &quot;Magical Folk&quot; I know the Victorians generally believed in the Fae. Being open about it was in bad taste, but the evidence is strong that the Victorians, at least in the British Isles and Iceland, believed in the Fae. So, how do Victorian mages deal with the Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-07-2021, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T17:04:24-08:00","id":1438398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438372#post1438372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, having read works like &quot;Strange and Secret Peoples&quot; and &quot;Magical People&quot; I know the Victorians generally believed in the Fae. Being open about it was in bad taste, but the evidence is strong that the Victorians, at least in the British Isles and Iceland, believed in the Fae. So, how do Victorian mages deal with the Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that wrought iron (i.e., cold iron, as <i>Changeling</i> defines cold iron) was still very common in construction until the 1880s, I can imagine the Kithain of the time being a little tetchy. Those that don't have a clear understanding of mage factionalism wouldn't have a way to distinguish between the Order of Reason and any other mage, but they might get the impression (rightly or wrongly) that someone in magickal circles doesn't like them very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T11:46:30-08:00","id":1438781,"title":"","content":"*keeps reading Order of Reason...sees this bit in the Grand Faculty write-up*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This century alone has seen the Sleepers step from superstitious beliefs about miasma and bad air being the source of illness <u><b>to creating vaccines</b></u>, sanitizing water sources, and even \u201cPasteurizing\u201d foods to cleanse them. </div> </div> </div>*looks back at the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...ok, no, no, stop.<br /> <br /> No, this book does not get to say that the guys who are assisting with DEVELOPING VACCINES are Objectively/Mostly Evil. You do not get to tell me that the guys who helped develop the medical technology, that in the real world right now, is helping people combat an ACTUAL PANDEMIC. And where we have actual fringe groups promoting rhetoric that vaccines are harmful and making life harder for everyone else.<br /> <br /> So for a book to say, in 2021, that the organization of mages is More Evil then all of the other groups, and to conflate that with said organization being the ones who supported development of vaccines, is seriously crossing the line.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm even more convinced that the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar was written by someone who wasn't involved in the actual OoR chapter, and frankly needs to either be heavily rewritten, or cut from the book entirely.<br /> <br /> Otherwise as is, this is outright tone-deaf, irresponsible, and flat out dangerous to have.<br /> <br /> Enabling anti-vaxx views, even if accidental, takes things straight to V5 Chechnya-bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T11:57:14-08:00","id":1438783,"title":"","content":"I've said before, and I'll say again: while the good things that technology has brought doesn't excuse the bad things that took place in bringing them about z neither does the latter invalidate the former. <br /> <br /> I would second the notion that the \u201care we the baddies?\u201d box be rewritten with this in mind. Right now, it hits the \u201cthe good doesn't excuse the bad\u201d side pretty heavily, but says nothing about the bad not invalidating the good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T12:51:31-08:00","id":1438790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438783#post1438783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said before, and I'll say again: while the good things that technology has brought doesn't excuse the bad things that took place in bringing them about z neither does the latter invalidate the former.<br /> <br /> I would second the notion that the \u201care we the baddies?\u201d box be rewritten with this in mind. Right now, it hits the \u201cthe good doesn't excuse the bad\u201d side pretty heavily, but says nothing about the bad not invalidating the good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave some feedback that either removing or rewriting the sidebar to be more balanced, while playing up the negatives more so in the chapter text (discussing Malthusianism and Galtonism in internal paradigmatic struggles within the Conventions, for example) would probably strike a more effective tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T12:56:31-08:00","id":1438792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438781#post1438781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*keeps reading Order of Reason...sees this bit in the Grand Faculty write-up*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *looks back at the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...ok, no, no, stop.<br /> <br /> No, this book does not get to say that the guys who are assisting with DEVELOPING VACCINES are Objectively/Mostly Evil. You do not get to tell me that the guys who helped develop the medical technology, that in the real world right now, is helping people combat an ACTUAL PANDEMIC. And where we have actual fringe groups promoting rhetoric that vaccines are harmful and making life harder for everyone else.<br /> <br /> So for a book to say, in 2021, that the organization of mages is More Evil then all of the other groups, and to conflate that with said organization being the ones who supported development of vaccines, is seriously crossing the line.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm even more convinced that the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar was written by someone who wasn't involved in the actual OoR chapter, and frankly needs to either be heavily rewritten, or cut from the book entirely.<br /> <br /> Otherwise as is, this is outright tone-deaf, irresponsible, and flat out dangerous to have.<br /> <br /> Enabling anti-vaxx views, even if accidental, takes things straight to V5 Chechnya-bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you are unfortunately hitting the real world history problem that the imperial institutions doing these positive things were committing genocides at the same time. As long as the act of creating vaccines is itself framed as a positive (which the quote you gave does), I don\u2019t have a problem with acknowledging the reality the white man\u2019s burden institutions funding and spreading that work were also genocidal racists... because you know.... they were","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T13:13:28-08:00","id":1438796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438781#post1438781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*keeps reading Order of Reason...sees this bit in the Grand Faculty write-up*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *looks back at the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar*<br /> <br /> ...ok, no, no, stop.<br /> <br /> No, this book does not get to say that the guys who are assisting with DEVELOPING VACCINES are Objectively/Mostly Evil. You do not get to tell me that the guys who helped develop the medical technology, that in the real world right now, is helping people combat an ACTUAL PANDEMIC. And where we have actual fringe groups promoting rhetoric that vaccines are harmful and making life harder for everyone else.<br /> <br /> So for a book to say, in 2021, that the organization of mages is More Evil then all of the other groups, and to conflate that with said organization being the ones who supported development of vaccines, is seriously crossing the line.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm even more convinced that the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar was written by someone who wasn't involved in the actual OoR chapter, and frankly needs to either be heavily rewritten, or cut from the book entirely.<br /> <br /> Otherwise as is, this is outright tone-deaf, irresponsible, and flat out dangerous to have.<br /> <br /> Enabling anti-vaxx views, even if accidental, takes things straight to V5 Chechnya-bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really <b>dangerous </b>that a historical fiction sourcebook of a fringe TTRPG (played by like maybe thousands of people) is highlighting how the valorization of &quot;scientific progress&quot; was/is not just coincidentally connected to, but instead, essential to the logics of elimination and the subsequent material realities it produced (e.g., enslavement, genocide, environmental catastrophe)? Or is it more <b>frustrating (but also expected) </b>that--for myself as a Hawaiian and Puerto Rican fan--the first time this game talks about these things in a way that doesn't make me want to vomit, a bad faith argument arises on this forum connecting this critique to the anti-vaccination movement that <b><i>also </i></b>emerges out of what it is being critiqued (e.g., white supremacy, colonialism)? I'm sure some anti-vaxx mom is gonna read this book in Seattle, Washington, and be like, &quot;Now I have the proof I've been waiting for.&quot; I'll make sure to reach out to Robert F. Kennedy Jr. to let him know that Mage the Ascension--as the final bastion of the global vaccination conspiracy--has seen the light. Or is it that maybe for once this game has done a good job of making the Technocrats (and Order of Reason) a morally complex enough faction worthy of playing, but people just can't handle the fact that genocide and actual evil has to come along with the group that best represents their white hegemonic fantasy? Feelings are complex and hard. Shit that is real tough. It must be as tough as having to look at the <b><i>Kopa Loei </i></b>and being like cool most of my people died because of the intentional spread of disease by European settlers who actively neglected their own public health practices to ensure that they could wipe out people and own their land...so this Craft only get a few pages in thousands of pages of fiction despite the word &quot;mana&quot; and several other key tropes of magic being appropriated from us for centuries. Cool yeah that feels fair.<br /> <br /> Let's not act like the need for the development of vaccines, the subsequent use of them, and that continued legacy is also not completely bound up in fucking settler colonialism, white supremacy, and capitalism. I am pretty sure the need for a smallpox vaccine would not be necessary if Europeans did not literally dispossess millions of people of their lands and sovereignty--which included their own very successful public health and hygiene practices. Actually I know for a fact that that is the case because there is so much research on how Indigenous peoples of the world had really fucking amazing public health and hygiene practices that worked for them which were specifically targeted by Europeans as a means of destroying these people. Often times these practices were supported by arguments of what were best practices and scientifically sound. If you don't believe me look up how boarding schools completely demolished how Indigenous children cleaned themselves out of a belief that they were literally living in states of savagery and squalor. But wait there is more. I am pretty sure Hansen's disease (Leprosy) was only spread to Hawaii and the Pacific because of colonization and imperialism. Shit. Oh and that the quarantining and management of those illnesses by Europeans settlers was also often used as a mean of exiling and arresting Indigenous leaders. Shit...its almost like every major illness that affects the &quot;globe&quot; (quotation intentional because we know this shit be hitting different among the colonized and the descendants of the enslaved) has been because of the material mechanisms that drive and are driven by the ideologies cine qua non to modernity (e.g., science, progress, industry, state nationalism). It's not like several key figures in epidemiology and medical anthropology have talked about for decades how industrial capitalism and global imperialism create global pandemics through their need for unsustainable economic development and environmental degradation. Oh right they have and this current pandemic is the result of those very processes. But it's also not like the development and distribution of the vaccine for COVID has been criticized because of how capitalism, corporations, and the supremacy of the global North has resulted in a medical apartheid in our global public health system...oh wait.<br /> <br /> I mean I could go on forever on this--because this is the history of the world--, but I think my point has been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 03-09-2021, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:12:49-08:00","id":1438806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438792#post1438792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you are unfortunately hitting the real world history problem that the imperial institutions doing these positive things were committing genocides at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438796#post1438796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really <b>dangerous </b>that a historical fiction sourcebook of a fringe TTRPG (played by like maybe thousands of people) is highlighting how the valorization of &quot;scientific progress&quot; was/is not just coincidentally connected to, but instead, essential to the logics of elimination and the subsequent material realities it produced (e.g., enslavement, genocide, environmental catastrophe)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're really trying to deliver to me bad faith-&quot;whatabout-isms&quot; about anti-vaxx ideology, I'm not even going to bother engaging.<br /> <br /> No, no you do not get to &quot;whatabout-ism&quot; a crisis that's happening right now, or try to say that OOC context of when a book is written somehow doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> I'll just report anyone that tries to do anything like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:21:25-08:00","id":1438808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438806#post1438806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you're really trying to deliver to me bad faith-&quot;whatabout-isms&quot; about anti-vaxx ideology, I'm not even going to bother engaging.<br /> <br /> No, no you do not get to &quot;whatabout-ism&quot; a crisis that's happening right now, or try to say that OOC context of when a book is written somehow doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> I'll just report anyone that tries to do anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a whataboutism to portray Victorian Inperialists accurately. If they act like \u201cthis means vaccines are bad\u201d then yes, I\u2019d agree with you. But \u201cdespite promoting the creation of vaccines, which was good, there\u2019s no getting around these institutions were actively carrying out genocides at the time\u201d is just reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:48:57-08:00","id":1438812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't realize we were role-playing white ignorance and scientific exceptionalism in the thread. On point for the Era.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> = colonizer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Chinese-Japanese American. Cut the shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-09-2021, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:13:47-08:00","id":1438822,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bb