zon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:16:27-08:00","id":1438826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438808#post1438808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not a whataboutism to portray Victorian Inperialists accurately. If they act like \u201cthis means vaccines are bad\u201d then yes, I\u2019d agree with you. But \u201cdespite promoting the creation of vaccines, which was good, there\u2019s no getting around these institutions were actively carrying out genocides at the time\u201d is just reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's just move off from vaccines, everyone. I'm pretty sure we all agree they're good.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:12:24-08:00","id":1438846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said before, and I'll say again: while the good things that technology has brought doesn't excuse the bad things that took place in bringing them about z neither does the latter invalidate the former.<br /> <br /> I would second the notion that the \u201care we the baddies?\u201d box be rewritten with this in mind. Right now, it hits the \u201cthe good doesn't excuse the bad\u201d side pretty heavily, but says nothing about the bad not invalidating the good</div> </div> </div> </div>About invalidating the good:<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, as an institution, has the moto of: &quot;One World, One Truth, One Reality&quot; Understood in the cosmology that the very Technocracy proposes, where conepts like &quot;Reality Deviant&quot; are accepted...this equals genocide (as per the definition of the man who introduced the concept). You simply can't end Reality Deviants w/o eradicating the cultures that support deviant belief systems.<br /> <br /> Colonialism wasn't accidentaly endorsed by them, it's a good part of what Technocracy *is* (well, it's their bad part).<br /> <br /> But they're not all that bad because they created goods? I can't accept that: Sometimes nuance<i> isn't</i> a good thing. One has to stress that an organization that's so on-board with imperialism it's very much *evil*. No grays here.<br /> <br /> You don't get to say: &quot;We're genocides but, oh!, look!, our trains are good, we made them, so we can be good guys too! - Gray morality!&quot;.<i> In this particular scenario, the bad should invalidate the good</i> (or, rather: The trains are good, their makers...perhaps not so much).<br /> <br /> Nuances must be found and <i>applied </i>elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2021, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:39:21-08:00","id":1438852,"title":"","content":"Did you not read the other part of what I just said? The part where I said that the good does not excuse the bad? I asked because you're response here seems to assume that I'm trying to have the good excuse the bad.<br /> <br /> Expanding on this, nuance is a good thing. Even here. The Technocracy is home to the future Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts. Did they cease to be evil when they left the Union and joined the Traditions? Or was there room in the Technocracy for entire factions of good even as far back as it's founding? (Not that I consider either of the Etherites or the VAs purely good; but again, they didn't suddenly switch their ethics upon leaving the Union. What's good about them now was good about them then.)<br /> <br /> And it isn't just the future Traditions that this holds for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-10-2021, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T03:53:44-08:00","id":1438920,"title":"","content":"So is the \u201cM\u00fcbarek Maharet Meclisi\u201d the Turkic name for the institution known in Arabic as \u201cMokteshaf al Nour\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T07:03:18-08:00","id":1438932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438852#post1438852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you not read the other part of what I just said? The part where I said that the good does not excuse the bad? I asked because you're response here seems to assume that I'm trying to have the good excuse the bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, and I can agree with that in general, but I didn't feel the need to address it: My point was that sometimes including the opposite isn't quite right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Expanding on this, nuance is a good thing. Even here. The Technocracy is home to the future Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts. Did they cease to be evil when they left the Union and joined the Traditions? Or was there room in the Technocracy for entire factions of good even as far back as it's founding? (Not that I consider either of the Etherites or the VAs purely good; but again, they didn't suddenly switch their ethics upon leaving the Union. What's good about them now was good about them then.)<br /> <br /> And it isn't just the future Traditions that this holds for. </div> </div> </div>They're are many places where you can hint the Technocracy as not absolute monsters. There can be individuals figthing crime and making good stuff, but <u><i>as a global institution</i></u><b> in this <i>specific historical period</i>, they're<u> the bad guys</u> </b>- period.<br /> <br /> Any nuances you add <b><i>here</i> </b>are nothing more and nothing less than the same nuances historical apologists of imperialism would add when they describe Europe as bringing culture and science to the naked indians. &quot;Oh, Cristobal Columbus did some atrocities, there's no denying that, but he was necessary for western culture to arrive at the west&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;there was bad, but also good&quot;, with imperialist organizations, it's exactly the kind of thing I don't want to see - even if it was trivially true. Do you fail to see *why* I don't care about the good the genocides also did while they were doing their thing?<br /> <br /> Sometimes talking about the good just muddies the waters in ways that just mentioning that the bad it's still there doesn't really help solve, so it's better to say the institution were &quot;the bad guys&quot;, even if their actions were sometimes correct. I really don't want to mention the obvious example, if I can help it, hence why I hope you can see it<br /> <br /> Etherites and VA are also the bad guys insofar they're part of an imperialistic institution - Especially Etherites, that are based on the &quot;adventurer&quot; trope, that has a long history in fictional romantizations of such henious acts. I don't want to see *those* Etherites described as anything but the bad guys when talking about imperialism.<br /> <br /> Send your nuances elsewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-10-2021, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T08:48:44-08:00","id":1438946,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to remember that the technological progress and inventions were not gifts to the Masses to uplift all of humanity. They were products, sold to middle- and upper-class white people. Increased farm output has enriched some billionaires, given cheap (but not great) food and clothes to middle-class people, but deprived millions of poor people of access to produce, and undermined subsistence farmers in poor countries. Then the farming methods cause preventable environmental and public health problems for the colonized peoples.<br /> <br /> With the Native Americans, Australian Aborigines, Pacific Island Natives, and other peoples suffering genocide via biological weapons like smallpox ... the whites in charge didn't offer to cure those people of those epidemics.<br /> <br /> The inventions aren't an exception to imperialism's evils. They are an <i>example</i> of imperialism. The harms of stolen land, resource extraction, slave labor, and pollution are dumped on the colonized &quot;primitive&quot; peoples. That exploitation gave white elites the raw materials and fuel to build their inventions and infrastructure. It's true of electricity, water sanitation, railroads, medical advances ... It's not as obvious as the link between Southern cotton output and slavery, but it's often a similar link. The industrial goods produced by these actions are sold to well-off whites (and nowadays, other well-off groups around the world.) When those goods break, they are dumped in landfills and seas where black and brown people live - even some waste that could have been recycled.<br /> <br /> These wonderful inventions have the <b>potential</b> to improve the quality of life for all humanity, and could be made sustainably too (although global overpopulation is becoming an obstacle to that). But in practice that isn't and wasn't how they have been produced or distributed. If you want to play a heroic Technocrat in any era, I think a good avenue is someone who wants these benefits available equally to all humanity, holding that up as the ideal the Union <i>should</i> strive for. True Utopians, in other words.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Is there any chance that a novel and/or anthology will come out of this Kickstarter, as a stretch goal? I don't play Mage or have a play group, but I would buy Mage stories if they're good.<br /> <br /> 2. What are the current (VAM) blocs and conventions within them, who were they in Sorcerer's Crusade time, and who they will become in modern times? I am not a backer, so I can't see them. Would someone be so kind as to post an outline of the groups, please? Just names, not details or copied text.<br /> <br /> <u>Daedaleans/Artisans &gt; Order of Reason (1325) &gt; Technocratic Union (1851) ?</u><br /> Gabrielites (320 ce) &gt; Cabal of Pure Thought (800) &gt; convention (when?) &gt; Knights Templar (1830s) ?<br /> ? &gt; Difference Engineers (1823) &gt; Analytical Reckoners (1851) &gt; Virtual Adepts (1880s) &gt; tradition (1956) &gt; Mercurial Elite (2000s)<br /> ? &gt; Voltarian Order (1806) &gt; Electrodyne Engineers (1866) &gt; Sons of Ether tradition (1906)<br /> Explorers' Society (1851) &gt; Explorators (1897?) &gt; Void Engineers (1890s?)<ul><li>? &gt; Celestial Masters (1300)</li> <li>? &gt; Void Seekers (1325)</li> </ul><br /> Grand Faculty<ul><li>Cosian Circle (400 bce) &gt; Hippocratic Circle (when?) &gt; \u00c6sculapian Order (1851) &gt; Progenitors</li> <li>who?</li> </ul><br /> [bloc ?]<ul><li>? &gt; High Guild (1325) &gt; Invisible Exchequer (1851) &gt; Syndicate (1900) ?</li> <li>Craftmasons (997) &gt; Golden Guilds (1250) ? &gt; Golden Guild &gt; ?</li> </ul><br /> Ivory Tower (1880s or 1890s) +Operatives &gt; New World Order (1914)?<ul><li>? &gt; Lightkeepers (1851) &gt; ?</li> <li>? &gt; Skeleton Keys (founded?) &gt; ?</li> </ul><br /> Ixoi &gt; House of Ixion &gt; Ksirafai (1336) &gt; Hermetic House Janissary (1600s-1716)?<br /> League of Constructors<ul><li>? (1480 bce) &gt; Artificers (1325) &gt; International Brotherhood of Mechanicians &gt; Iteration X ?</li> </ul><br /> Hermetic House Golo (1171) &gt; Natural Philosopher's Guild (1188) &gt; convention (1193)<br /> <br /> Were these blocs formed in 1851? I thought that was the same year they renamed themselves the Technocratic Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-10-2021, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T09:17:24-08:00","id":1438950,"title":"","content":"The Craftmasons definitely do not become the Golden Guild specifically. I mean some of their members who practice Ars Cupiditae might have survived the purge by joining the newly forming Golden Guild, just as some Gabrielites more oriented toward selling common shared thought, than the specifics of those thoughts being devoted to God, might have similarly survived, but it's not a direct continuation I don't believe. The Craftmasons don't have a direct continuation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T09:31:02-08:00","id":1438955,"title":"","content":"The progressions aren't all linear. <br /> <br /> The Natural Philosophers Guild exists within the Electrodyne Engineers, and is basically the part that will eventually leave the Union to become the Sons of Ether. <br /> <br /> The Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers are each split between the League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty. <br /> <br /> When the Gabrielites were purged, those who were able to adapt their worldview to the Union's new insistence on atheism became the Lightkeepers; the rest more or less ended up joining the Templars. The Lightkeepers and the Skeleton Keys make up the bulk of the Ivory Tower. <br /> <br /> The International Brotherhood of Mechanicians has been retconned to just the Brotherhood of Mechanicians, and are primarily found in the League of Constructors. <br /> <br /> The \u00c6sculapians make up the other part of the Grand Faculty. <br /> <br /> Note that for the most part, it's not the original Conventions that become the new Conventions after the 1897 reorganization; it's the voting Blocs. The Exploratory Society (Void Seekers and Celestial Masters) becomes the Void Engineers; the League of Constructors becomes Iteration X; the Grand Faculty becomes the Progenitors; the Ivory Tower becomes the New World Order. The Syndicate exists in the Victorian Age as a voting Blocs, combining the Invisible Exchequers and the Golden Guild. Only the Analytical Reckoners continue on as a separate Convention (and perhaps the Electrodyne Engineers; but they're gone within five years of the reorganization), renaming themselves the Virtual Adepts. <br /> <br /> The Craftmasons were destroyed well before the Victorian Age began, by a few centuries. If they survived in any form, that's still a mystery. <br /> <br /> The Ksirafai disappeared and infiltrated the Traditions as House Janissary right after destroying the Gabrielites. It wouldn't surprise me if some of them stuck around in the Technocracy among the Skeleton Keys; the M.O. is similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T10:45:49-08:00","id":1438969,"title":"","content":"Thanks, this is helping me to start to understand.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438955#post1438955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Natural Philosophers Guild exists within the Electrodyne Engineers, and is basically the part that will eventually leave the Union to become the Sons of Ether.<br /> <br /> The Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers are each split between the League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only the Analytical Reckoners continue on as a separate Convention (and perhaps the Electrodyne Engineers; but they're gone within five years of the reorganization), renaming themselves the Virtual Adepts. </div> </div> </div>This part confuses me. If part of each of the Electrodyne Engineers and the Analytical Reckoners joined the League of Constructors &gt; Iteration X and the Grand Faculty &gt; Progenitors, did they each have a third part that stayed separate from the voting blocs and left the Union later? Or were part of some other bloc?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Daedaleans/Artisans &gt; Order of Reason (1325) &gt; Technocratic Union (1897?)</u><br /> Craftmasons (997) &gt; join Artisans (1210) &gt; join Order of Reason (1325) &gt; destroyed (1670)<br /> <br /> origin? &gt; Difference Engineers (1823) &gt; Analytical Reckoners (1851) &gt; split between League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty (<b>in year?</b>)<br /> <br /> Hermetic House Golo (1171) &gt; Natural Philosopher's Guild (1188) &gt; convention name? (1193) &gt; Voltarian Order (1806) &gt; Electrodyne Engineers (1866) &gt; split between League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty (<b>year?</b>)<br /> <br /> Grand Faculty (<b>founded year?</b>) &gt; Progenitors (1897?)<ul><li>Cosian Circle (400 bce) &gt; Hippocratic Circle (when?) &gt; \u00c6sculapian Order (1851)</li> <li>some Analytical Reckoners</li> <li>some Electrodyne Engineers</li> </ul><br /> League of Constructors (<b>founded year?</b>) &gt; Iteration X (1897?)<ul><li>name? (1480 bce) &gt; Artificers (1325) &gt; <s>International</s> Brotherhood of Mechanicians (1851)</li> <li>some Analytical Reckoners</li> <li>some Electrodyne Engineers</li> </ul><br /> origin? &gt; Sons of Ether tradition (1906)<br /> <br /> origin? &gt; Virtual Adepts (1880s) &gt; join Traditions (1956) &gt; Mercurial Elite (2000s)<br /> <br /> Explorers\u2019 Society (1851) &gt; Exploratory Society/Explorators (1897?) &gt; Void Engineers (1890s?)<ul><li>origin? &gt; Celestial Masters (1300)</li> <li>origin? &gt; Void Seekers (1325)</li> </ul><br /> Gabrielites (320 ce) &gt; Cabal of Pure Thought in Sacred Congregation (800) &gt; joined Order of Reason (1325) &gt; driven out, survivors form Disparate Knights Templar (1830s); a few become Lightkeepers instead<br /> <br /> Ivory Tower (1880s or 1890s?) + Operatives &gt; New World Order (1914)?<ul><li>some Gabrielites &gt; Lightkeepers (1851)</li> <li>origin? &gt; Skeleton Keys (<b>founded year?</b>)</li> </ul><br /> Ixoi &gt; House of Ixion (<b>year?</b>) &gt; Ksirafai convention (1336) &gt; Hermetic House Janissary (1600s-1716? or 1830s?)<br /> <br /> Syndicate (<b>founded year?</b>)<ul><li>origin? &gt; High Guild (1325) &gt; Invisible Exchequer (1851)</li> <li>origin? &gt; Golden Guilds (1250) &gt; Golden Guild &gt; (<b>year?</b>)</li> </ul><br /> Which parts of the above are still incorrect? And please help correct the dates above?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ksirafai disappeared and infiltrated the Traditions as House Janissary right after destroying the Gabrielites. </div> </div> </div>When, please? In the 1830s, not in 1716? Or were the Cabal of Pure Thought destroyed at an earlier date?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-10-2021, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:23:59-08:00","id":1438993,"title":"","content":"The Blocs aren't official organizations, per se; they're more like political parties, with individuals joining. When I say that the Brotherhood of Mechanicians is in the League of Constructors, what I mean is that most of the members of the Brotherhood vote with the League. The Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers have members who tend to split more or less evenly between two voting Blocs. After the Grand Housecleaning in 1897, most of the original Conventions get dissolved, and the voting Blocs become the new Conventions; the Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers are the exceptions to this. I suspect that during the Great Housecleaning, there were vocal factions within these two Conventions who identified more with their original Conventions than with their voting Blocs, and insisted on keeping their original Conventions in place (albeit with a name change, in the case of the Analytical Reckoners). <br /> <br /> The voting Blocs come into existence in 1861 as part of the Victorian Reformation, when the Order of Reason becomes the Technocratic Union. <br /> <br /> And you're right about the Ksirafai; they disappeared right after destroying the <i>Craftmasons</i>, not the Cabal of Pure Thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:26:07-08:00","id":1438994,"title":"","content":"Third manuscript excerpt is up.<br /> <br /> Also new stretch goals:<br /> <br /> $75k is just expanding the companion and adding more story options.<br /> <br /> $78k is...PDFs of the Victorian Vampire novel trilogy<br /> <br /> ...well that last one is underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:57:56-08:00","id":1439005,"title":"","content":"OK, thanks.<br /> <br /> Between 1193 and 1806 what were the Natural Philosopher's Guild/Voltarian Order called?<br /> Where did the Skeleton Keys come from, and when did they form?<br /> Where did the Difference Engineers and High Guild originally come from?<br /> When did the 3 Golden Guilds become the one Golden Guild?<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm not backing but I'm kinda disappointed at the stretch goals that just hand out novels we can already buy. I'm still hoping the next goal will be novellas. One way to show that Victorian Technocrats (and Hermetics, and Choristers, and whites in general) don't all have to be evil:<br /> Write a novella about a protagnoist in one of those groups (hopefully a Technocrat/Reasonite) who IS a Utopian and opposes slavery and genocide. There were abolitionists on both sides of the Atlantic before the US Civil War started, and I'm pretty sure there were whites who opposed genocide and conquest too. So let's read about someone heroic (and humanly flawed, and culturally not modern, and not a White Savior trope) who did oppose these evils - not in a milquetoast way just saying a few tepid words but actually working to stop them, how hard they had to fight against the establishment and their own leadership and peers, and some hard-won thing they did accomplish despite how history turned out overall. It would be good to depict two things: that your white/Techno/Hermetic/Chorister/whoever PC could be and can be a hero in any era, no matter what their leaders are doing* and that opposing racism is more than just saying &quot;no I'm not racist&quot; but also not a hopeless struggle against inevitable defeat by The Man. Well, and that even if your side lost and your leaders erased you from the history books, that doesn't mean you weren't a hero.<br /> <br /> And then hopefully also write a novella by, and from the perspective of, some of those voices who are usually marginalized from the depiction of the 1800s.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Unless they went thru the Cauls. Sorry Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-10-2021, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:33:46-08:00","id":1439011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439005#post1439005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, thanks.<br /> <br /> Between 1193 and 1806 what were the Natural Philosopher's Guild/Voltarian Order called?<br /> Where did the Skeleton Keys come from, and when did they form?<br /> Where did the Difference Engineers and High Guild originally come from?<br /> When did the 3 Golden Guilds become the one Golden Guild?</div> </div> </div> </div>The truth of the matter is that there just isn't a direct precedent for a lot of these Conventions. The High Guild is essentially a splinter sect of the Craftmasons, while the Voltarian Order has only tangential relation to the NPG and most of its members probably came from the Artificers and Celestial Masters in the 1700s. As for the Reckoners, while one could argue that there is some precedent for them from the various Pythagorean math cults, they really didn't crystallize into a discreet order until Babbage and Lovelace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T13:42:17-08:00","id":1439017,"title":"","content":"The Voltarian Order was founded in 1806; the Difference Engineers were founded in 1823. They were not part of the Order of Reason, but were friendly with it and joined up with the Technocracy when it was founded in 1861. As far as I know, there was no single antecedent to the Difference Engineers: Babbage's Difference Engine inspired mathematicians and engineers to form a new faction. When the Technocracy was founded, the Voltarian Order joined forces with the Society of Ether to form the Electrodyne Engineers. The Society of Ether's history stretches back much further. <br /> <br /> And yes, this is a retcon. I have no idea when the Natural Philosopher's Guild started calling itself the Society of Ether; apparently, it was closer to 1861 than to 1905. Given that Maxwell published his famous equations in the 1950s and 1960s, and that those were the origin of the beliefs that light is an electromagnetic wave and that the Ether is the medium through which it propagates, I could see them taking on the name somewhere around then. <br /> <br /> The origins of the Skeleton Keys are unknown, other than that they were a technomantic faction allied with, but not part of, the Union \u2014 sorry of like the case of the Difference Engineers and Voltaic Order with respect to the Order of Reason. They worked for Queen Victoria originally, and ended up joining the Union at her insistence. <br /> <br /> The High Guild was one of the original Conventions of the Order of Reason from way back in the early Renaissance, and became the Golden Guild in 1861. See <b>Sorcerers Crusade</b> to get the date of their founding. The Invisible Exchequers likewise trace their roots back to the High Guild; essentially, the High Guild split into two Conventions in 1861, which then remerged in 1897.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:01:03-08:00","id":1439024,"title":"","content":"Now I am more and more confused.<br /> <br /> Either the NPG joined the Order of Reason in 1193 and dissolved. Or it appeared out of nowhere in 1851 and called itself the Society of Ether in 1861, 100 years before scientists first proposed the ether theory. What?<br /> <br /> The Voltarian Order or the Voltaic Order?<br /> <br /> The High Guild split in what year? And into what, please? I thought the Golden Guild was three separate guilds (Golden Pyramid, Golden Coin, and Golden Wheel) that merged together into the Golden Guild at some point. And I thought the High Guild became the Invisible Exchequer in 1851.<br /> <br /> What year did the Explorers' Society form? What year did they change into the Explorators? What year did they change into the Void Engineers?<br /> <br /> Nothing makes any sense now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Could someone please replace my failed diagram with a new, correct and accurate diagram?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:39:32-08:00","id":1439036,"title":"","content":"First of all, the Ether Theory of light originated in the middle of the 19th century, in the 1850s and 1860s more or less. A hundred years later (1950s, post-WWII), it was well and truly dead. This is real-world history. <br /> <br /> Getting back to the WoD history: the Natural Philosophers' Guild was founded in the 12th century. It didn't last long after its founder died, but continued on within other Conventions over the centuries, with the defining feature being the Kitab al-Alacir. That is, for the next 700 years, there wasn't an official Natural Philosopher's Guild; but there were individuals in the various Conventions who were Awakened by the Book of Ether, and they formed a continuation of the Natural Philosophers' Guild in spirit. <br /> <br /> It reemerged in the 1800s during the chaos of that century, and joined with the Voltaic Order to form the Electrodyne Engineers. <br /> <br /> The High Guild split into the Golden Guild and the Invisible Exchequers; as voting Blocs began to form over the next fifty years, those two Conventions tended to vote together as the Syndicate. The Golden Guild is presented as having been a single faction from its start in the Victorian Age; the manuscript makes no mention of a Golden Pyramid/Coin/Wheel divide. That comes from Sorcerers Crusade, and its a 13th century development where those three groups join up with the Craftmasons. The Golden Guild mentioned in Victorian Mage is, as far as I know, unrelated to that one. <br /> <br /> The Void Seekers and Celestial Masters started working together in the late 19th century as the Exploratory Society; no specific founding year is given. The Exploratory Society was rechristened the Void Engineers and made into a formal Convention in 1897.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:58:47-08:00","id":1439065,"title":"","content":"<u>Daedaleans/Artisans &gt; Order of Reason (1325) &gt; Technocratic Union (1851) &gt; [Great Housecleaning 1897]</u><br /> <br /> League of Constructors (~1861-1897)<ul><li>Artificers (1480 bce) &gt; join Order of Reason (1325) &gt; <s>International</s> Brotherhood of Mechanicians (1851) &gt; Iteration X (1897)</li> <li>some Analytical Reckoners (temporarily ~1861-1897)</li> <li>some Electrodyne Engineers (temporarily ~1861-1897)</li> </ul><br /> Ixoi (before 700 bce) &gt; House of Ixion (<b>year?</b>) &gt; Ksirafai convention (1336) &gt; Hermetic House Janissary (1600s-1716)<br /> <br /> Grand Faculty (~1861-1897)<ul><li>Cosian Circle (400 bce) &gt; Hippocratic Circle (when?) &gt; \u00c6sculapian Order (1851) &gt; Progenitors (1897?)</li> <li>some Analytical Reckoners (temporarily ~1861-1897)</li> <li>some Electrodyne Engineers (temporarily ~1861-1897)</li> </ul><br /> Gabrielites (320 ce) &gt; Cabal of Pure Thought in Sacred Congregation (800) &gt; joined Order of Reason (1325) &gt; driven out, survivors form Disparate Knights Templar (1830s); a few become Lightkeepers instead<br /> <br /> Ivory Tower (~1861 - 1880s or 1890s?) + Operatives &gt; New World Order (1914)<ul><li>a few Gabrielites &gt; Lightkeepers (1851)</li> <li>Skeleton Keys (joined Union on Queen Victoria\u2019s insistence)</li> </ul><br /> Craftmasons (997) &gt; join Artisans (1210) &gt; merge with Golden Pyramid Guild, Gold Coin Guild, and Golden Wheel Guild (1250) &gt; join Order of Reason (1325) &gt; destroyed (1670)<br /> <br /> a few Craftmasons &gt; High Guild (1325) &gt; split into Invisible Exchequer (1861) and Golden Guild (1861?)<br /> Syndicate (late 1800s) &gt; merged back together as Syndicate (1897)<ul><li>Invisible Exchequer (1861)</li> <li>Golden Guild (1861)</li> </ul><br /> Hermetic House Golo (1171) &gt; Natural Philosopher's Guild (1188) &gt; dissolved among the Artisans (1193) &gt; restarted under the name Society of Ether (late 1850s or early 1860s ?)<br /> <br /> Voltarian Order (1806) + Society of Ether &gt; Electrodyne Engineers (1866) &gt; voting informally split between League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty (1861) &gt; re-merged (1897) &gt; Sons of Ether tradition (1906) &gt; Society of Ether (2000s)<br /> <br /> Exploratory Society/Explorators (~1861-1897) &gt; Void Engineers (1897)<ul><li>Celestial Masters (1300)</li> <li>Void Seekers (1325)</li> </ul><br /> Difference Engineers (1823) &gt; Analytical Reckoners (1851) &gt; voting informally split between League of Constructors and the Grand Faculty (1861) &gt; Virtual Adepts (1880s) &gt; join Traditions (1956) &gt; Mercurial Elite (2000s)<br /> <br /> <br /> better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T17:23:37-08:00","id":1439073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1438920#post1438920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is the \u201cM\u00fcbarek Maharet Meclisi\u201d the Turkic name for the institution known in Arabic as \u201cMokteshaf al Nour\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See page 128 of Mage20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T18:09:20-08:00","id":1439079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439073#post1439073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See page 128 of Mage20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! So more the Ottoman successor to the latter having declined with the Abbasids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T18:55:58-08:00","id":1439086,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know when the Cosian Circle became the Hippocratic Circle?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone else feel like it's a bit ... coincidental ... that the two conventions who ditched the Technocracy were also the last to joinn the Union? It sort of feels like it's implying they were never <i>really</i> Technocrats, and therefore one doesn't have to feel bad about playing one (if all other Technocrats = automatically bad), or something. I don't have the manuscript to read, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-10-2021, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T22:12:55-08:00","id":1439096,"title":"","content":"I admit to being kind of amusing that a large part of the issues here are from the very basic premise that was always a major part of mage.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....bad.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....world domination obsessed technomagic-using conquerors.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....bad.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:20:15-08:00","id":1439099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439096#post1439096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit to being kind of amusing that a large part of the issues here are from the very basic premise that was always a major part of mage.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....bad.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....world domination obsessed technomagic-using conquerors.<br /> <br /> Technocracy....bad.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...issues that got phased out after Mage 1e, because people found the idea of mainstream scientists being Objectively Evil to be ridiculous. And that Mage as &quot;Traditions = GOOD vs Technocracy = EVIL&quot; makes no sense. Moreso now as time went on and in the wake of...particular current events.<br /> <br /> (Or to be blunt: &quot;No, the Technocracy is NOT magickal-Pentex&quot;)<br /> <br /> Although personally I think it's because Technocracy-as-sci-fi being much easier for new players to wrap their heads around since that's a lot more accessible, versus the Traditions and Crafts that are based on real-world cultures. Where if you had no personal cultural background in or studied them academically, you were locked out of them.<br /> <br /> Like me personally: I have no background or knowledge of Hinduism or any monotheistic religion. So I feel it would be kind of awkward to play a Chakravanti or a Choristor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:29:59-08:00","id":1439100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439099#post1439099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...issues that got phased out after Mage 1e, because people found the idea of mainstream scientists being Objectively Evil to be ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the problem was that they missed they were fascists first, scientists second.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the past few years indicates that the people in charge of the world are not interested in science but control.<br /> <br /> Which means the Union must be evil or the Union is not in charge, the Nephandi is.<br /> <br /> But yes, Victorian Age Mage will be very much at the heart of &quot;technology as the weapon of colonialism, racism, and Empire building.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:36:48-08:00","id":1439101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439100#post1439100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the problem was that they missed they were fascists first, scientists second.</div> </div> </div> </div>...which is a problematic view because the Union are specifically coded as mainstream scientists.<br /> <br /> And I've spoken to Mage fans who are IRL scientists...and yeah, they don't like that 1e was telling them that being a scientist or believing in science makes one an evil fascist.<br /> <br /> (one of said fans being Jewish, and who finds it doubly offensive considering their heritage)<br /> <br /> Plus, Mage just fundamentally doesn't work if you take it into black and white moral absolutism and say that Traditions = GOOD and Technocracy = EVIL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:47:40-08:00","id":1439104,"title":"","content":"Honestly the more that I think about it, the idea of a faction of magic users who use the British Empire as a means to spread control and oppression isn't inherently a bad idea. It works fine...<br /> <br /> ...in Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> Swap it out with the Seers of the Throne, who are much more unambiguously EVIL, in motivation have always been tied to being about control and oppression, and NOT being tied to mainstream science the same way that the Technocracy are.<br /> <br /> So it would make sense if this was a Dark Era for Mage: the Awakening. It does not make sense to do it within Mage: the Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:55:48-08:00","id":1439105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439099#post1439099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...issues that got phased out after Mage 1e, because people found the idea of mainstream scientists being Objectively Evil to be ridiculous. And that Mage as &quot;Traditions = GOOD vs Technocracy = EVIL&quot; makes no sense. Moreso now as time went on and in the wake of...particular current events.<br /> <br /> (Or to be blunt: &quot;No, the Technocracy is NOT magickal-Pentex&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Although personally I think it's because Technocracy-as-sci-fi being much easier for new players to wrap their heads around since that's a lot more accessible, versus the Traditions and Crafts that are based on real-world cultures. Where if you had no personal cultural background in or studied them academically, you were locked out of them.</b><br /> <br /> Like me personally: I have no background or knowledge of Hinduism or any monotheistic religion. So I feel it would be kind of awkward to play a Chakravanti or a Choristor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right...which might be a problematic manifestation of the real world processes of global hegemony, colonization, and white supremacy. The Technocracy <b>is </b>based on a real-world culture--white culture. &quot;Mainstream&quot;, &quot;conventional&quot;, &quot;accessible&quot;, and &quot;take-for-granted&quot; are all terms of a global white hegemony. &quot;Global&quot; culture can be easily traced to historical and contemporary practices that seek to make white culture disappear and become the invisible global culture--or not culture at all. This isn't to say that I am anti-science--I'm an environmental and sustainability scientist at a major Midwestern University--, but I do believe that perpetuating a deracialized and dehistoricized science or modernity is dangerous.<br /> <br /> Like maybe there is a problem that a majority of the fanbase (or new players) can so easily sees themselves in the Technocracy? No shade, I love the new write-ups and think it makes the Technocracy actually worth playing, but maybe it's something to be reflective of why that is the case. Similarly, why is it easier imagine a global non-ethnoracial, non-religious, and non-local group of Mages using the trapping of modernity (e.g., science, capitalism, individual rights) for their magic when these groups also can use them? The Dreamspeakers have the Ghost Wheel Society to speak to that very reality. Other groups either or could be made to have similar factions. Hell, I rolled up a character that was a Ex-Void Engineer combat vet turned Kopa Loei who can't really shake the techno bug to aid in his return to traditional navigation because of the over representation of Hawaiian (and other BIPOC folks in the U.S. Military).<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying that people have to play what represents who they are. I get that. But it does seem like Mage is a game that asks players to stretch to think about why some choices are easier than others. The game provides an in-game metaphor for it--Reality Zones. Sometimes depending on where you are, who you are, what's around you, and what you do makes certain character choices more <i>Paradoxical</i>. Allusion intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 03-11-2021, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T00:18:44-08:00","id":1439107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439101#post1439101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...which is a problematic view because the Union are specifically coded as mainstream scientists.<br /> <br /> And I've spoken to Mage fans who are IRL scientists...and yeah, they don't like that 1e was telling them that being a scientist or believing in science makes one an evil fascist.<br /> <br /> (one of said fans being Jewish, and who finds it doubly offensive considering their heritage)<br /> <br /> Plus, Mage just fundamentally doesn't work if you take it into black and white moral absolutism and say that Traditions = GOOD and Technocracy = EVIL.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution to this, IMHO, is to introduce Enlightened Scientists who are <i>not</i> Technocrats, and who can represent science and technology that <i>isn't</i> being used to control and destroy. The Etherites and VAs were originally intended to fill this role; though for various reasons, the same people that tend to not like the Technocracy representing science because it paints science as evil, also tend to find the Etherites and VAs unsatisfactory as the counterpoint. And in the Victorian Age (which, remember, is what this thread is about), <i>they're part of the Technocracy</i>. So they can't be an alternative to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T02:12:32-08:00","id":1439122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439104#post1439104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the more that I think about it, the idea of a faction of magic users who use the British Empire as a means to spread control and oppression isn't inherently a bad idea. It works fine...<br /> <br /> ...in Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> Swap it out with the Seers of the Throne, who are much more unambiguously EVIL, in motivation have always been tied to being about control and oppression, and NOT being tied to mainstream science the same way that the Technocracy are.<br /> <br /> So it would make sense if this was a Dark Era for Mage: the Awakening. It does not make sense to do it within Mage: the Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree with that notion.<br /> <br /> The Seers in Awakening are kind of detached of real world history by design. But this is an actual historical problem with real consequences that span to the current day and the Technocratic Union is the faction that is culturally tied to it, like it or not. The options are to tackle it and making it clear how bad it was (and sometimes still is) or to ignore it and go into fully whitewash romanticed victorian era (like many other stuff does). And of course, the latter is not a sensible option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 03-11-2021, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T04:09:22-08:00","id":1439140,"title":"","content":"Yep. Mage is fictional, but it's a kind of fiction that it's loaded with political and historical comentary. That's why going full whitewash romantic it's not sensible.<br /> <br /> This time the &quot;bad guy&quot; ball it's well within the OoR park (It's arguably their darkest time, in a sense - Crafmason blood, and broken ideals, still fresh in their hands).<br /> <br /> Usually it's in the OoH park, and nobody complains. Heck, in the Victorian Era this isn't the exception, the Order of Hermes are very much bad guys on board with colonialism, just to a lesser degree 'cuz they have less power. Yet nobody demands Houses that are universally less bigoted than most of the Order is (Well, there's always House Ex, but that's almost a comentary on segregation).<br /> <br /> The reason, as stated above: We don't really have much alternatives to play science mages in this era. <hr /><br /> But the answer it's not to divorce European science from the evils of imperialism. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar896_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"896\" data-vbnamecard=\"896\">Erinys</a> posted, those advancements had the potential to be universaly good, but ultimately were made, intended, and used, as a way to further the goals of the empire and little more. The inventions aren't an exception to imperialism's evils. They are an <i>example</i> of imperialism.<br /> <br /> I would imagine there were OoR members that were against such practices but, as part of an organization, they obviously weren't calling the shots. <hr /><br /> In my opinion, the best answer to this nerdy problem of &quot;we wan't science to be good&quot; it's not to whitewash the OoR but ... to aknowledge for once that science wasn't invented by Europe, and that it's colonialist practices weren't a <i>necessary </i>evil to spread it, but rather just the way it was.<br /> <br /> To aknowledge that while European OoR certainly were able to asceleate the spread and dominance of Technomancy trough most *horrific* practices, the magick of science was everywhere - that technomancers existed everywhere, and could have evolved in different ways.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> : That would also give more credence of the idea that technomancy isn't just mages that delude themselves in thinking objective truth exists out there. If the principles of technomancy are everywhere, then technomancy shouldn't be the sole province of Queen Victoria's OoR - incidentaly, this is canon because it's canon that there were technomancers everywhere, but their history it's so small and so tied to the european branch of the OoR that they end being &quot;assimilated&quot; by it<br /> <br /> And if it's bad taste to say Victorian Technocrats weren't the bad guys, it's also bad taste to say technomancers in the colonized parts of the world were always accomplice of their colonizers.<br /> <br /> What would be better?. To say that reason mages actualy *weren't* always in the same side as the Victorian OoR (Much like how many Traditions fell and went Disparate, why can't we have Disparate scientists?).<br /> <br /> That this was erased from Mage history because neither the Technocracy nor the Traditions see such a history as a good thing to share (The Technocracy, because that would make them the bad guys in that era, the Traditions becuse they were largely ruled by mystics that ain't fans of technomancy, and ex-OoR)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T04:36:23-08:00","id":1439145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439107#post1439107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution to this, IMHO, is to introduce Enlightened Scientists who are <i>not</i> Technocrats, and who can represent science and technology that <i>isn't</i> being used to control and destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the option of House Thig, within the the OoH.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T06:50:39-08:00","id":1439157,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Victorian Mage also mentions three technomancer Crafts: one Chinese, one Japanese, and one Zulu. It also mentions Siamese Akashayana who hold the position that rejecting science and progress is ultimately doomed, and instead seek to help Siam adopt science and technology on its own terms. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, there's a subtext that runs through all of these examples, one that gets imported into Mage because it was true in the real world, and despite it <i>not</i> being true in the usual interpretation of Mage: <br /> <br /> The Dalou'loushi are impressed by the effectiveness of the Order of Reason's innovations, and seek to modernize China so it can compete on equal terms. The effort of more traditional mages to use magick to oppose the colonization of China ultimately fails in the Boxer Rebellion. <br /> <br /> Technomancy in Japan is either Uncanny or Catastrophic, until Admiral Perry's gunboat diplomacy forces the Japanese to open their ports; at which point the Jidai start trying to learn the Technocracy's secrets so that Japan can benefit from them. <br /> <br /> The Zulu Mechanists come into being after a military assault where technology allowed the Boers to slaughter their Zulu adversaries with no losses on their own side. <br /> <br /> All of these imply that technology has an edge somewhere that lets it smash into Territories where it has no right winning out according to a strict reading of the Reality Zone rules and the Consensus-dominated Reality model of Mage. And that's fundamentally what the Siamese Akashayana noticed and responded to: they worked to get Siam's Territory into a state where when and if an Admiral Perry or Boer invasion took place, whatever it was that was causing the Technocracy's Science to dominate and the local magics to fail wouldn't result in Siam's defenses crumbling. <br /> <br /> The question is how to square this notion that technology has an acknowledged advantage in these conflicts with the idea in Mage that it's all just a matter of belief. In modern times, the latter view characterizes the former as a Technocratic delusion; but given the incidents I highlighted above, and other examples from real world history that <i>didn't</i> make it into Victorian Mage, can we really say that the Victorian Order of Reason was delusional about the nature of reality? <br /> <br /> The section in Victorian Mage on Quiet, specifically about Denial, has an interesting observation in this regard; and if it turns out that the Negation Men phenomenon described in <b>Book of Secrets</b> has a much longer history than that entry implies, that could provide a Mage-consistent explanation for the Union's edge: all you'd need would be a handful of Denial-based Marauders mixed in with Admiral Perry's fleet, or the Boer side of the Boer/Zulu conflict, or the colonizers' side of the Boxer Rebellion, and the otherwise inexplicable failure of the Japanese blockade, Zulu forces, and Boxer Rebellion, respectively, suddenly makes a lot more sense. And the Order of Reason wouldn't identify it as embedded Marauders; they'd attribute it to the inherent superiority of their Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:15:30-08:00","id":1439161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439101#post1439101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...which is a problematic view because the Union are specifically coded as mainstream scientists</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the government, megacorporations, and, well, fascists.<br /> <br /> They were the &quot;secret rulers of humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> To say they were &quot;mainstream scientists&quot; you also had to ignore the literal Men in Black, the Terminators, the Military Industrial Complex, and the fact they controlled the entirety of the world's economy. There was a very weird desire to only talk about the Technocracy making penicillin and not cigarettes or guns. It's interesting in 2020 to also note that the racial element of the Technocracy (and Traditions) were heavily de-emphasized.<br /> <br /> Basically, that the Union was very much representing white European power structures and the Traditions to be mixed global. Which is interesting to also look at from a perspective of who gamers sided with.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I always think we need the &quot;Serious Etherites&quot; as a faction or basically <b>House of Thig</b> (&quot;We like Science! We combine it with magic!&quot;). It's also possible the Union flat out may just have been a bad idea and is irredeemable as a concept. I've run plenty of Technocracy games (emphasizing &quot;evil leaders, good people on the ground&quot;) but if you want to do them as enlightened scientists then you can't put them in charge of the World of Darkness. It does not track unless you're making a anti-scientist message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:16:35-08:00","id":1439162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439157#post1439157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these imply that technology has an edge somewhere that lets it smash into Territories where it has no right winning out according to a strict reading of the Reality Zone rules and the Consensus-dominated Reality model of Mage. And that's fundamentally what the Siamese Akashayana noticed and responded to: they worked to get Siam's Territory into a state where when and if an Admiral Perry or Boer invasion took place, whatever it was that was causing the Technocracy's Science to dominate and the local magics to fail wouldn't result in Siam's defenses crumbling.<br /> <br /> <b>The question is how to square this notion that technology has an acknowledged advantage in these conflicts with the idea in Mage that it's all just a matter of belief. In modern times, the latter view characterizes the former as a Technocratic delusion; but given the incidents I highlighted above, and other examples from real world history that <i>didn't</i> make it into Victorian Mage, can we really say that the Victorian Order of Reason was delusional about the nature of reality?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So this sounds like the false equivocation between Western technological exceptionalism and the complicity of Western technology and technologists to collaborate in acts of genocide, slavery, theft, and dispossession. Western technology doesn't have an advantage, a willingness to commit heinous acts in the name of profit and superiority with little disregard for the environmental or social consequences (for their own people and the world) does. Sure, maybe Western technology really mastered the means of industrializing labor, exploiting the land for natural resources, and killing millions of people, but is that not a delusional conceptualization of reality?<br /> <br /> There is more science now showing how delusional historical and contemporary Western models of science are than not. Especially with regards to the social sciences and environmental/sustainability sciences. Look at the fires in California, antiquated settler forest management technologies are what produced the conditions that have led to the disasters we see today. Only now has the state admitted that maybe they shouldn't have banned Indigenous practices (read: technologies) of controlled seasonal burns. And now they are playing catch up trying to realign their practices. <br /> <br /> Not to mention the fact that we have to accept that the authors of Mage are just as susceptible to the myths and ideologies of Western hegemony. So to assume that because a game system or narrative went a certain way should be used as a means of reflecting on this reality without acknowledging that fact is problematic in the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:26:24-08:00","id":1439165,"title":"","content":"I admit, as a Storyteller, I am frequently tempted to suggest the OOC statement, &quot;Mages believe that belief shapes reality. However, mages are mistaken that ALL PEOPLE&quot;S BELIEFS shape reality. When, in fact, it only is the case if you're a mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which undercuts the Ascension War massively but cleans up a lot of the setting's kookiness and makes it more understandable.<br /> <br /> For better and worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:35:55-08:00","id":1439166,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I hear that. And I think each Storyteller has to make that choice. I have had my issues reconciling the ease with which Mage lends itself to cultural relativism and postmodern ambivalence, but Mage is still one of my favorite games and has helped give me space to think about these issues in ways that I can't in my scholarly/professional work. I have been working on a landed cosmology/ontology for Mage that tries to reconcile those tensions, but it's tough.<br /> <br /> Either way, I am glad that the upcoming release of this sourcebook has brought these conversations up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:49:26-08:00","id":1439167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439166#post1439166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I hear that. And I think each Storyteller has to make that choice. I have had my issues reconciling the ease with which Mage lends itself to cultural relativism and postmodern ambivalence, but Mage is still one of my favorite games and has helped give me space to think about these issues in ways that I can't in my scholarly/professional work. I have been working on a landed cosmology/ontology for Mage that tries to reconcile those tensions, but it's tough.<br /> <br /> Either way, I am glad that the upcoming release of this sourcebook has brought these conversations up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. Isn't cultural relativism kinda... the whole point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:59:11-08:00","id":1439171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439162#post1439162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this sounds like the false equivocation between Western technological exceptionalism and the complicity of Western technology and technologists to collaborate in acts of genocide, slavery, theft, and dispossession. Western technology doesn't have an advantage, a willingness to commit heinous acts in the name of profit and superiority with little disregard for the environmental or social consequences (for their own people and the world) does. Sure, maybe Western technology really mastered the means of industrializing labor, exploiting the land for natural resources, and killing millions of people, but is that not a delusional conceptualization of reality?<br /> <br /> There is more science now showing how delusional historical and contemporary Western models of science are than not. Especially with regards to the social sciences and environmental/sustainability sciences. Look at the fires in California, antiquated settler forest management technologies are what produced the conditions that have led to the disasters we see today. Only now has the state admitted that maybe they shouldn't have banned Indigenous practices (read: technologies) of controlled seasonal burns. And now they are playing catch up trying to realign their practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.<br /> <br /> Mage it's based on outdated notions about what advancement *is*, that also happen to be very eurocentiric and even racist. This is not their fault, it's a very normal way to understand science, culture and advancement. I myself think like that, I'm learning about the subject while I write at this very thread<br /> <br /> This video it's about Columbus, but just see the first 10 minutes. It talks about this equivocation: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaJDc85h3ME\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OaJDc85h3ME</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:00:11-08:00","id":1439172,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that nearly every post here defending the books uncompromising take on the evil of Imperialism is doing so strictly from the perspective of what sort of messaging the book should be sending, with little to no regard given to how well or poorly that may or may not work in the context of the game.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that they're wrong, mind you. My perspective, though, comes more from an angle of making sure that the game works.<br /> <br /> In that regard, I find it somewhat ironic that my own proposal for how to resolve the dilemma of the inordinate effectiveness of the Technocracy's methods in the Victorian Age is in fact to embrace the idea that they actually <i>were</i> delusional. As in, in Denial. See the text's section about Denial in the Victorian Age. <br /> <br /> Traditionally, Marauders have had a rather loud Quiet. That's natural, considering the nature of Madness-based Quiets. But Denial-based Quiet actually <i>is</i> quiet, and easy to overlook; and if it's backed up by Marauderdom, there's power in it. <br /> <br /> Perry didn't have time to use the methods described in Victorian Mage to change the nature of the Territory Zone that he broke into with his gunship diplomacy; but it worked anyway. A Denial-based Marauder among his crew, causing the Straits that should have targeted the Americans to instead got the Japanese while simultaneously hitting the Japanese with countermagick, would explain why it worked. And again, Perry wouldn't chalk it up to a Marauder; heck, the <i>Marauder</i> wouldn't chalk it up to a Marauder. They'd all just credit it to the superiority of the American technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:07:06-08:00","id":1439173,"title":"","content":"With Perry's case, that thing has always been kind of very exaggerated anyway. Japanese people knew about cannons, guns and artillery, those weapons were extensively used during the Sengoku period. Let's not forget that there were gunsmiths in Japan producing guns through the entire Edo Period, so their reaction wouldn't be &quot;oh god what is this strange magic&quot; but &quot;oh god they have much more advanced guns than the ones we have.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:15:11-08:00","id":1439175,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Perhaps the Boer and Zulu would have been a better example. The essence of it was that the Zulu got trounced in their own Territory, <i>before</i> the Boers had a chance to use the tools of colonialism to subvert it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:18:09-08:00","id":1439176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439167#post1439167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused. Isn't cultural relativism kinda... the whole point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no because the entire point of the Ascension War is a conflict between choosing what you believe your culture to be RIGHTTM vs. believing you can all get along. The fact lots of people unironically decided the Technocracy was the good guys and eventually all the local (explicitly non-white origin) cultures would have to get with the program is a very, uh, let's just say unfortunate set of beliefs that fans latched onto without considering what their equivalent in RL is about.<br /> <br /> Quite a few fans went, &quot;The Traditionalists are anti-vaxxers!&quot; without realizing they were going, &quot;Get rid of those First Nations people! They can get with white atheist secularism!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439175#post1439175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Perhaps the Boer and Zulu would have been a better example. The essence of it was that the Zulu got trounced in their own Territory, <i>before</i> the Boers had a chance to use the tools of colonialism to subvert it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I am biased just to saying, &quot;The Technocracy was spectacularly racist in the 19th century. It wasn't until the modern era they began addressing that and the guys leftover from the Victorian Era are probably still incredibly racist. Good thing the Avatar Storm killed most of them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though now I'm thinking of a less serious but still relevant, &quot;Captain Nemo was the first Indian Son of Ether and inspired others to rise up against the Union.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:19:38-08:00","id":1439177,"title":"","content":"You all have some good points, folks.<br /> <br /> The notion of science-as-superior-technology is very much the mainstream notion that supports the notiion of white culture as superior. In real life, I am all in favor of trying to view the world objectively, and yet real science (in the real world) is agnostic on the existence of God and such. The core of <b>real</b> science isn't dogmatic atheism or racial superiority, it's objectively accepting the world as we observe it, preconceived notions be damned. Real science requires the humility to always say &quot;I could be wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the WOD? Real science would look at the supernatural elements of the world and acknowledges they exist and are significant, including the entire spirit world and the obvious efficacy of Mystick magick. It can't be anything <b>but</b> delusion to call supernatural elements &quot;reality deviants&quot;, and to bend over backwards inventing a complex, anti-Occam's-razor delusion like Tychoidean cosmology to explain away the obvious reality of the spirit world. The Technocratic paradigm only works on a basis of anti-science censorship. And in the real world, idiocy like Euro-American fire-suppression also isn't remotely scientific, it's just an exercise in blindly declaring that white ways are always superior to Native ways, and ignoring the constant avalanche of evidence disproving that BS.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer, I don't own any Mage corebooks. But to see how many people read the Mage message as &quot;science is evil&quot; suggest to me that the messaging hasn't been effective in conveying how utterly deluded and non-scientific the Technocray really is. They ought to be depicted as <i>non</i>-mainstream scientists, who manipulate sleeper scientists and silence the ones who discover or invent anything Control wants to destroy. The ones who erase the history of non-European scientific practices and kill off everyone who practices or remembers them, so they can continue lying about white people &quot;inventing&quot; science and suppress the scientific knowledge of other cultures. Their thing is mechanical technology, not the scientific method.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would somebody please summarize for me the Zulu, Chinese, and Japanese technomagic factions in VAM? I would like to know some about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:23:54-08:00","id":1439178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439167#post1439167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused. Isn't cultural relativism kinda... the whole point?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I don't necessarily agree that the original intention for Mage was to make an argument for cultural relativism, but instead wanted to support theories of localized resistance against oppressive Western hegemony. That being said, the philosophies that were pulled from and their subsequent operationalizations in game lend themselves to an extreme epistemological (and in turn cosmological) stance of relativism.<br /> <br /> Relativism can be broadly understood as problematic for two reasons. First, it is a tautology. If Truth is constructed or cultures can all be understood as equally relative that is actually making a very strong Truth statement about reality that itself would negate. Second, and more importantly, relativism and cultural relativism lend themselves to a depoliticized, demoralized, and deracialized understanding of reality, behavior, and knowing which is super beneficial for in power, but not for anyone else. Namely, if truth, justice, and morality, are completely relative then systems like colonization, racism, and capitalism aren't <b><i>essentially </i></b>wrong, but wrong because they are taking up the most space. So in the context of Mage, the Technocracy isn't bad or wrong because they were complicit and collaborative with genocide, but because they aren't leaving enough of the pie for the other belief systems. While Franz Boas (the guy that kind of invented the idea) made an argument that cultural relativism lends itself to the study of a human or historical science with human subjects studying human subjects, the material realities of science, study, and research did not shift from its object/subject relationship. Moreover, this allows cultural relativism to be used as a cover for moral relativism (i.e., what is good is not up for debate because its all relative) in the discussion of such things like colonialism and slavery.<br /> <br /> I instead pull from decolonial leftist materialist critiques of history like those espoused by Glenn Sean Coulthard in his work <i>Red Skin White Masks</i>. Moreover, he makes an argument for a landed realism that seeks to reconcile the real material world with the calls for sovereignty and justice in the face of Western hegemony. This goes to my point earlier about the use of Indigenous vs. non-Indigenous technologies of land management. There are some really bad ways of land management and natural resource policy that sure can be argued as True, but are clearly destroying reality which I would argue invalidates those claims.<br /> <br /> Many apologies for being long winded on this. I study the human interface with wildlife and wilds management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:26:55-08:00","id":1439180,"title":"","content":"Heck, even if you don't believe in religion then you can still note that attacking local religious structures has been done explicitly as a means of dis-empowering and demoralizing people you want to oppress. One of the interesting Technocracy concepts I created was <b>The Church of Nothing</b>, which was a Syndicate inspired megachurch that existed for the purpose of making a religion that had absolutely nothing about it other than generic feel good platitudes that existed to keep people content while also donating as well as working for the community.<br /> <br /> The Church of Nothing was being plotted against by both a Progenitor who considered it vile AND a Celestial Choirster that both considered it to be an abomination.<br /> <br /> Both the New Atheist Materialist and genuine believer loathed the concept of religion as a empty cultural expression of unity as well as ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:28:53-08:00","id":1439181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439176#post1439176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no because the entire point of the Ascension War is a conflict between choosing what you believe your culture to be RIGHTTM vs. believing you can all get along. The fact lots of people unironically decided the Technocracy was the good guys and eventually all the local (explicitly non-white origin) cultures would have to get with the program is a very, uh, let's just say unfortunate set of beliefs that fans latched onto without considering what their equivalent in RL is about.<br /> <br /> Quite a few fans went, &amp;quot;The Traditionalists are anti-vaxxers!&amp;quot; without realizing they were going, &amp;quot;Get rid of those First Nations people! They can get with white atheist secularism!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I admit, I am biased just to saying, &amp;quot;The Technocracy was spectacularly racist in the 19th century. It wasn't until the modern era they began addressing that and the guys leftover from the Victorian Era are probably still incredibly racist. Good thing the Avatar Storm killed most of them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Though now I'm thinking of a less serious but still relevant, &amp;quot;Captain Nemo was the first Indian Son of Ether and inspired others to rise up against the Union.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, unless you're saying that racism has power, that doesn't explain why the Boers were so effective.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I'm more interested in making sure that the game works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:30:40-08:00","id":1439182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439172#post1439172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that nearly every post here defending the books uncompromising take on the evil of Imperialism is doing so strictly from the perspective of what sort of messaging the book should be sending, with little to no regard given to how well or poorly that may or may not work in the context of the game.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that they're wrong, mind you. My perspective, though, comes more from an angle of making sure that the game works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, about the context of the game: Again, Mage it's a game loaded with political and historical comentary. The game allows you to play the evils of imperialism either as part of britain or outside of it. I think talking about these, and giving sensible options to play this drama, it's very important, from the perspective of how the game works<br /> <br /> How Victorian Technomancers came on top? It could be explained in various ways.<br /> <br /> I do like very much your idea of them having many Negation Man. That would fit the themes of a OoR that's falling to Hubris.<br /> <br /> Also I think that perhaps (correct me if I'm wrong) such a thing cleverly written may even be used as a reference to <i>british humor</i>?<br /> (Like ppl would ignore the obviously supernatural out of politeness?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:31:09-08:00","id":1439183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439172#post1439172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that nearly every post here defending the books uncompromising take on the evil of Imperialism is doing so strictly from the perspective of what sort of messaging the book should be sending, with little to no regard given to how well or poorly that may or may not work in the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> My point has not, and never has been \u201cthey need to whitewash the crimes of the Victorian Era to make the Order of the Reason sympathetic\u201d.<br /> <br /> (Nvm that the text as is...is already kind of doing that)<br /> <br /> My point has been \u201cthe \u2018Are we the Baddies?\u2019 sidebar is actively restricting options and wagging its finger about badwrongfun... while still providing the factions it\u2019s condemning as a playable option.\u201d<br /> <br /> It\u2019s mixed messaging.<br /> <br /> Victorian Mage is NOT a history textbook. It\u2019s a tabletop game sourcebook. It\u2019s supposed to provide a framework and options to play a game during a particular time period. So it\u2019s bizarre that we have a sidebar that basically says \u201cdon\u2019t play these guys as anything other then EVIL\u201d.<br /> <br /> It restricts play options.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s not doing that, then it fails as a game sourcebook.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s one thing if y\u2019all already decided that in your near future VM chronicle to lock off playable OoR PCs and only allowed Traditions and Craft PCs. But I want the book to give me that decision as a player and an ST myself, not make that decision for me.<br /> <br /> This would be like if the V5 corebook DID provide write ups for the Independent and Sabbat Clans, but had a sidebar telling you that you\u2019d be Playing the Game Wrong and be a Terrible Person if you chose not to play a Camarilla or Anarch game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-11-2021, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:31:10-08:00","id":1439184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439181#post1439181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, unless you're saying that racism has power, that doesn't explain why the Boers were so effective.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I'm more interested in making sure that the game works.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages can warp reality with their beliefs, Sleepers can warp reality with guns.&quot;<br /> - How I view Mage cosmology as part of a larger World of Darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:31:34-08:00","id":1439185,"title":"","content":"Also as a disclaimer, I am totally for <b>real </b>science as a scientist/human being if it were possible, but the actual industry of scientific production is so fucking far from that. Publishing, journals, university politics, tenure promotion, and funding are just a few of the barriers to a <i>True </i>implementation of postpositivism--or the scientific method. I could go on forever about how much easier it would be to critique science if science was actually being done as it is espoused. If you are interested in critiques of what is the real ontological grounding for the real world industry of science I would suggest reading Mark Fisher's <i>Capitalist Realism.</i> It's short and I think he could have expanded his critique more, but I think he does a good job outlining how capitalism is more involved in defining what is reality than any individual or collective belief in objective realism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:43:49-08:00","id":1439188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439177#post1439177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YDisclaimer, I don't own any Mage corebooks. But to see how many people read the Mage message as &quot;science is evil&quot; suggest to me that the messaging hasn't been effective in conveying how utterly deluded and non-scientific the Technocray really is. They ought to be depicted as <i>non</i>-mainstream scientists, who manipulate sleeper scientists and silence the ones who discover or invent anything Control wants to destroy. The ones who erase the history of non-European scientific practices and kill off everyone who practices or remembers them, so they can continue lying about white people &quot;inventing&quot; science and suppress the scientific knowledge of other cultures. Their thing is mechanical technology, not the scientific method.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage books since late 2nd Edition and through Revised era had this idea being repeated that the problem with the Union is NOT Science, but Control. The Union has not the monopoly in all things scientific and they never had it, they just created that narrative because it suited their moral justification and propaganda.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I think what happened (in this specific instance with a section of the fanbase I mean) was the pop cultural shift in the 90s with punk resistance being replaced by X-Files or Men in Black. Add the Guide to the Technocracy prologue (written in-character as propaganda) being so well written that some people latched into it as if it was the actual truth.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:45:32-08:00","id":1439189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439176#post1439176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I am biased just to saying, &quot;The Technocracy was spectacularly racist in the 19th century. It wasn't until the modern era they began addressing that and the guys leftover from the Victorian Era are probably still incredibly racist. Good thing the Avatar Storm killed most of them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're not so biased.<br /> <br /> Books say so, too. But in the Victorian Era we're stuck with being them. This is the first time, as in Cruzade they weren't as bad either.<br /> <br /> In Book of the Traditions it's stated science stopped being marginalized in the more mystial Traditions after the Storm, when the salty old guard left the premisses. So you can say that for both factions getting rid of &quot;the elders&quot; was a positive thing from a certain standpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though now I'm thinking of a less serious but still relevant, &quot;Captain Nemo was the first Indian Son of Ether and inspired others to rise up against the Union.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I would like to play that. Nemo's faction :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:50:35-08:00","id":1439190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439183#post1439183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bingo.<br /> <br /> My point has not, and never has been \u201cthey need to whitewash the crimes of the Victorian Era to make the Order of the Reason\u201d.<br /> <br /> (Nvm that the text as is...is already kind of doing that)<br /> <br /> My point has been \u201cthe \u2018Are we the Baddies?\u2019 sidebar is actively restricting options and wagging its finger about badwrongfun... while still providing the factions it\u2019s condemning as a playable option.\u201d<br /> <br /> It\u2019s mixed messaging.<br /> <br /> Victorian Mage is NOT a history textbook. It\u2019s a tabletop game sourcebook. It\u2019s supposed to provide a framework and options to play a game during a particular time period. So it\u2019s bizarre that we have a sidebar that basically says \u201cdon\u2019t play these guys as anything other then EVIL\u201d.<br /> <br /> It restricts play options.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s not doing that, then it fails as a game sourcebook.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s one thing if y\u2019all already decided that in your near future VM chronicle to lock off playable OoR PCs and only allowed Traditions and Craft PCs. But I want the book to give me that decision as a player and an ST myself, not make that decision for me.<br /> <br /> This would be like if the V5 corebook DID provide write ups for the Independent and Sabbat Clans, but had a sidebar telling you that you\u2019d be Playing the Game Wrong and be a Terrible Person if you chose not to play a Camarilla or Anarch game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this supposed to be a horror game where you play monsters? As someone who wants to play characters from cultures and beliefs that are demonized--or made monstrous--for being savage, superstitious, or downright forgotten I am confused as to why there is tension. Like yeah you can play member of the OoR with a good heart, but hey you are part of a monstrous institution and the things that you are doing that might even look good are probably super fucked. That's just reality. Like you can play the Victorian equivalent of Oppenheimer, but the consequences don't change. I don't understand how that is any more limiting for players when compared to how people would feel playing any of the more racialized, localized, or spiritual groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:50:44-08:00","id":1439191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439188#post1439188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage books since late 2nd Edition and through Revised era had this idea being repeated that the problem with the Union is NOT Science, but Control. The Union has not the monopoly in all things scientific and they never had it, they just created that narrative because it suited their moral justification and propaganda.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I think what happened (in this specific instance with a section of the fanbase I mean) was the pop cultural shift in the 90s with punk resistance being replaced by X-Files or Men in Black. Add the Guide to the Technocracy prologue (written in-character as propaganda) being so well written that some people latched into it as if it was the actual truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a certain sense of the cultural zeitgeist at the time being one that fed into the issue. Steve Jobs, iphones, X-Files, and the Men in Black with Will Smith made it seem like being part of cool edgy morally ambiguous conspiracies as well as Technological WonderlandTM being just around the corner. The Technocracy has always had a cool<b> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">EDGE</span> </b>that Vampire: The Masquerade's protagonists have but the Traditions flat out don't.<br /> <br /> Being part of THE MAN seemed cool.<br /> <br /> However, this was generally before the War on Terror hit its public backlash, Occupy Wallstreet, and a lot of the nastiest revelations that the Far Right factions of the government really did want all the brown and poor people to die.<br /> <br /> Now I feel like a lot of people just want to shoot THE MAN in the face.<br /> <br /> The one big irony being THE MAN is clearly not a fan of science and actively denies it whenever it doesn't align with his figures. The Union was not designed with the world's leaders to be more like Pentex or Low Humanity Ventrue than misguided idealists.<br /> <br /> Who suspected &quot;Captain Planet Villains&quot; were just realistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:02:31-08:00","id":1439192,"title":"","content":"The capitalist makes money on fossil fuels. He's a multibillionaire and owns the governments and militaries of several powerful nations. He still wants more, because he's a greedy, racist, and possibly sadistic monster.<br /> <br /> The Indigenous activitsts rise up, pointing out that the fossil fuel industry is unnecessary for electricity, it's causing extreme pollution and disease and climate change, and it's a weapon of genocidal colonialism. They even get some white environmentalists to agree with them.<br /> <br /> The honest scientist comes along, looks at the data, sees the activitsts are 100% right, and starts complaining to people in government.<br /> <br /> The capitalist says &quot;you're threatening my profit.&quot; He spends $2 million to have the activists jailed and shot. He spends $6 billion spreading propaganda denying everything the activists and honest scientist said, replacing Truth with his lies. He tries to arrange for the academic ostracism and disgrace of the honest scientist.<br /> <br /> The corrupt politicians, who are also white supremacists, happily support the capitalist and enjoy his payoffs. Killing millions of black and brown people is a <i>bonus</i> to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, replace capitalist with &quot;Technocracy&quot; and you have Mage. A truly honest scientist, who isn't ideologically attached to white supremacy, wouldn't join the Technocracy. The honest scientists, if Awakened, would join the Society of Ether or the Navalon.<br /> <br /> I know someone said that the Technocracy shouldn't be Pentex. But they're inextricably tied to white supremacy and colonialism, not to mention the Syndicate IS capitalism. It would be nonsensical and dishonest to portray them as having any pro-environment or pro-civil rights element large eough to pose any internal threat to the colonialism-capitalism-Pogrom Agenda. Just some few utopians who keep their heads down, and are too few and powerless to pose a threat to the Agenda, so there's a playable Technocrat option.<br /> <br /> So who are the honest, non-evil scientists in Victorian Mage? There aren't as many plausible options. Either play a Technocrat who objects strongly and fights the Man, or play a technomancer of a non-white, non-colonialist group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:05:53-08:00","id":1439193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439183#post1439183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorian Mage is NOT a history textbook. It\u2019s a tabletop game sourcebook. It\u2019s supposed to provide a framework and options to play a game during a particular time period. So it\u2019s bizarre that we have a sidebar that basically says \u201cdon\u2019t play these guys as anything other then EVIL\u201d.<br /> <br /> It restricts play options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously you think the Players Guide to the Sabbat fails as a game sourcebook, as they're portrayed as proud monsters playing football with the heads of innocents...Since we're at it: Can you really say the Camarilla, as an institution, isn't evil for any other reason than &quot;well, they're better than the Sabbat&quot;?.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D used to said Drow are evil. Dritzz it's an exception, not the rule. Obviously D&amp;D fails as a game sourcebook when it states you can play a good Drow but the book says they're extremely rare and not representative of their culture.<br /> <br /> Really, how is saying that the OoR are genocidal monsters restricting anything BUT playing an unrepentant imperialist supporter?<br /> What option it's being restricted here, exactly?.<br /> <br /> I can't play a scotland yard detective interested in stopping crime, just because it's stated that I happen to be part of an institution that does far worse overboard and thus not really a good guy by modern standards, but rather a bigot that happens to be good in a limited fashion?<br /> <br /> Because I think I can ... Do you really need your hero points so bad?, I really don't think I need those points to play such a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:12:38-08:00","id":1439194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439182#post1439182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, about the context of the game: Again, Mage it's a game loaded with political and historical comentary. The game allows you to play the evils of imperialism either as part of britain or outside of it. I think talking about these, and giving sensible options to play this drama, it's very important, from the perspective of how the game works<br /> <br /> How Victorian Technomancers came on top? It could be explained in various ways.<br /> <br /> I do like very much your idea of them having many Negation Man. That would fit the themes of a OoR that's falling to Hubris.<br /> <br /> Also I think that perhaps (correct me if I'm wrong) such a thing cleverly written may even be used as a reference to <i>british humor</i>?<br /> (Like ppl would ignore the obviously supernatural out of politeness?)</div> </div> </div> </div>On the first point, you seem to be under the mistaken impression that I'm trying to argue that the messaging in the book be changed. I'm not. What I'm trying to do is to find a way to reconcile a couple of dilemmas I have with the book. One is the one that tasti Man LH is arguing, that there's a cognitive dissonance between saying that the Victorian Technocracy is as bad as the Nephandi and presenting them as a playable option. That's already being addressed quite effectively without my input, so I'm staying out of that one. The other is the conflict between Territories defining how likely something is to either work or fail on the one hand, contrasted with Technocratic methods working in Territories where they shouldn't. <br /> <br /> And in that note, my head-canon is that there's been an infestation of Negation Men in the Technocracy since its founding in the Victorian Age, for the reasons cited in the manuscript in its discussion about Denial, but that the Union has been blind to it until recently, when the phenomenon started to bite them in the ass with the rise of Negation Men who are denying Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> And since no one else has commented on it either, it needs to be presented as a subtle phenomenon that's easily overlooked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:19:18-08:00","id":1439197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439194#post1439194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in that note, my head-canon is that there's been an infestation of Negation Men in the Technocracy since its founding in the Victorian Age, for the reasons cited in the manuscript in its discussion about Denial, but that the Union has been blind to it until recently, when the phenomenon started to bite them in the ass with the rise of Negation Men who are denying Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> And since no one else has commented on it either, it needs to be presented as a subtle phenomenon that's easily overlooked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your Negation Men idea, to the [quite limited] extent I think I can understand it and the narrative problem you're arguing against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439157#post1439157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that Victorian Mage also mentions three technomancer Crafts: one Chinese, one Japanese, and one Zulu. It also mentions Siamese Akashayana who hold the position that rejecting science and progress is ultimately doomed, and instead seek to help Siam adopt science and technology on its own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really like to know more about these guys. Would you please share a little summary about them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:28:32-08:00","id":1439198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439193#post1439193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously you think the Players Guide to the Sabbat fails as a game sourcebook, as they're portrayed as proud monsters playing football with the heads of innocents...Since we're at it: Can you really say the Camarilla, as an institution, isn't evil for any other reason than &quot;well, they're better than the Sabbat&quot;?.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D used to said Drow are evil. Dritzz it's an exception, not the rule. Obviously D&amp;D Core fails and always failed as a game sourcebook, statistics be damned.<br /> <br /> Really, how is saying that the OoR are genocidal monsters restricting anything BUT playing an unrepentant imperialist supporter?<br /> What option it's being restricted here, exactly?.<br /> <br /> I can't play a scotland yard detective interested in stopping crime, just because it's stated that I happen to be part of an institution that does far worse overboard and thus not really a good guy by modern standards, but rather a bigot that happens to be good in a limited fashion?<br /> <br /> Because I think I can ... Do you really need your hero points so bad?, I really don't think I need those points to play such a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. If your game happens to be set in the UK, your average Electrodyne Engineer or Machinist is probably on the same level morally as a Verbena or a Hermetic from the same era, which is to say pretty reprehensible by modern standards, but that kinda comes with the territory. If you're playing outside of Europe, maybe just accept that any Europeans that show up are probably going to be there for terrible reasons. This doesn't really restrict your range of playable options, unless you're married to playing exclusively white people. <br /> <br /> Context is important here. Player options that are appropriate in Paris will probably seem less palatable in Tazmania. Not all European magi are actively engaging in genocide, but the ones interacting with the outside world usually are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:28:51-08:00","id":1439199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439197#post1439197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really like to know more about these guys. Would you please share a little summary about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much to say: in all three cases, the nation in question for hit by the Order of Reason/Technocracy, which demonstrated inordinate effectiveness with their Technology that convinced mages in those nations to try to adopt it as their own as a way to fight the Union. That resulted in Technomantic Crafts that either stood in opposition to the Union or attempted to infiltrate and subvert it. Little is said about the specifics of their theory and practice; just that they're trying to use the Union's tools against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:29:51-08:00","id":1439200,"title":"","content":"ASSASSINS CREED: SYNDICATE is an interesting possible take on Victorian Age Mage. You have the fact the British Empire is already in full swing and only growing each point. However, that is coming at considerable cost and there are people who support it not for racist reasons and want to use the &quot;benefits&quot; of technology to help the public (starting with the lower classes of the very white world but believing they're helping other people against feudal tyrannies in the brown and black worlds). You know, whether they want to be or not.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of people who could believe that the Union will ULTIMATELY be a force of good but those people are going to be outnumbered by those who are just....the worst.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate DLC THE LAST MAHARAJA deals with the tragic life of real-life Ranjit Singh who attempted many times to work within the system to restore himself as monarch of India as well as benefit the people of his home as a whole. He wanted to be part of it and make India part of the &quot;Modern&quot; world. And couldn't....because the British Empire was racist as fuck. That DLC pretty much dealt with what could be an interesting case for a Technocrat who ends up defecting from the Union or gets brainwashed into compliance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:39:14-08:00","id":1439202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439157#post1439157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that Victorian Mage also mentions three technomancer Crafts: one Chinese, one Japanese, and one Zulu. It also mentions Siamese Akashayana who hold the position that rejecting science and progress is ultimately doomed, and instead seek to help Siam adopt science and technology on its own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mubarek Maharet Meclisi (Ottoman Technomancers) are also mentioned in passing but didn't get a Craft writeup.<br /> <br /> They seem similar to the Jidai in that they want to BE the Technocratic Union in order to not get EATEN by the Technocratic Union (Western Europe) - which is quite apt as its the sentiment behind both Turkish Nationalism and the Meiji Restoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-11-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:46:16-08:00","id":1439204,"title":"","content":"There's a reason I phrase things in an earlier post as one of the sources of cognitive dissonance being the contrast between the Victorian Technocracy being portrayed as evil as the Nephandi and them being portrayed as a playable faction: playing the Nephandi has been explicitly discouraged all throughout the Mage line. If there isn't a way to present the option to play a Victorian Technocrat who isn't a genocidal racist, then the books approach to the Technocracy ought to the similar to The Book of the Fallen approach to the Nephandi: \u201cwe really recommend against playing them. Instead, here's some advice on how to recognize and combat the evils they represent.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T09:56:31-08:00","id":1439205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439204#post1439204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason I phrase things in an earlier post as one of the sources of cognitive dissonance being the contrast between the Victorian Technocracy being portrayed as evil as the Nephandi and them being portrayed as a playable faction: playing the Nephandi has been explicitly discouraged all throughout the Mage line. If there isn't a way to present the option to play a Victorian Technocrat who isn't a genocidal racist, then the books approach to the Technocracy ought to the similar to The Book of the Fallen approach to the Nephandi: \u201cwe really recommend against playing them. Instead, here's some advice on how to recognize and combat the evils they represent.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference is that the OoR is a corrupt and evil organization when taken as an aggregate, while the Nephandi are all corrupt and hateful at an individual level. The book lists several branches and sub-organizations that explicitly are fighting against those tendencies. The book is telling you to acknowledge what the organization as a whole has complicit in, not saying that this is an immutable state of affairs. There is resistance, just not enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:02:23-08:00","id":1439208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439204#post1439204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason I phrase things in an earlier post as one of the sources of cognitive dissonance being the contrast between the Victorian Technocracy being portrayed as evil as the Nephandi and them being portrayed as a playable faction: playing the Nephandi has been explicitly discouraged all throughout the Mage line. If there isn't a way to present the option to play a Victorian Technocrat who isn't a genocidal racist, then the books approach to the Technocracy ought to the similar to The Book of the Fallen approach to the Nephandi: \u201cwe really recommend against playing them. Instead, here's some advice on how to recognize and combat the evils they represent.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a question of it being impossible to play an individual who isn\u2019t a genocidal racist, it\u2019s a matter of the institution they\u2019re part of actively carrying out genocide, so it\u2019s a bit different from the Nephandi in that regard.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m starting to agree that the sidebar might have been an over correction against imperial fetishism, and getting it to a more balanced tone while including more references to the horrific part of the Victorian \u201cScientific\u201d Paradigm in the actual Convention writeup, and conflicts around those (say Hippocratic internal conflict between spreading public health, vs Malthusian efforts against surplus population) would be stronger, and have submitted feedback to that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:03:14-08:00","id":1439209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439202#post1439202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mubarek Maharet Meclisi (Ottoman Technomancers) are also mentioned in passing but didn't get a Craft writeup.<br /> <br /> They seem similar to the Jidai in that they want to BE the Technocratic Union in order to not get EATEN by the Technocratic Union (Western Europe) - which is quite apt as its the sentiment behind both Turkish Nationalism and the Meiji Restoration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have liked to have seen that, yes. Maybe it can be proposed as an addition to the manuscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:06:44-08:00","id":1439210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439205#post1439205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the difference is that the OoR is a corrupt and evil organization when taken as an aggregate, while the Nephandi are all corrupt and hateful at an individual level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me think of the first season of <i>The Terror--</i>supernatural retelling of the real world catastrophe of the HMS Erebus and HMS Terror--and the role of Harry Goodsir--the sympathetic assistant surgeon who befriends the main Indigenous character. Eventually he realizes, &quot;Oh maybe me being good doesn't mean anything when we just shouldn't have thought of coming here in the first place.&quot; Might be a good inspiration source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:11:15-08:00","id":1439211,"title":"","content":"I really want an Indian technomancer faction. The Indian subcontinent has an astonishing and wondrous history of scientific and technological accomplishment on par with anything Rome or China did, and this would have been a great place to highlight this. It really would have underlined the amount of scientific knowledge and technology that imperialism actually destroyed. Not to say the other techno-Crafts aren't great (they are), but many of them are explicitly described as adopting or being formed in reaction to the Union, as opposed to being outgrowths of their own home culture's tradition of inquiry and innovation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:16:07-08:00","id":1439213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439204#post1439204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason I phrase things in an earlier post as one of the sources of cognitive dissonance being the contrast between the Victorian Technocracy being portrayed as evil as the Nephandi and them being portrayed as a playable faction: playing the Nephandi has been explicitly discouraged all throughout the Mage line. If there isn't a way to present the option to play a Victorian Technocrat who isn't a genocidal racist, then the books approach to the Technocracy ought to the similar to The Book of the Fallen approach to the Nephandi: \u201cwe really recommend against playing them. Instead, here's some advice on how to recognize and combat the evils they represent.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's where my example of Scotland Yard shines - and while I don't have the book I seem to remember that WAS an option.<br /> <br /> A Nephandi it's almost <i>cartoonishly </i>evil. A Nephandi doesn't need to think himself as good while doing or supporting bad things, they do bad things &quot;for the evil&quot;. They support Satan because he's bad, not because they mistakenly think of demons as misunderstood spirits. Heck, I've seen implied they want to betray Satan too, because he's too good for their tastes.<br /> <br /> Nephandi do want to see the world burn.<br /> <br /> All Victorian Technocrats are, by action or omission, supporting a genocidal institution - but they do so within a historical context, and that's a rational perspective it's easy to accomodate. I don't need to think of VT as anything but &quot;the bad guys&quot; to play a Technocrat that is a farly decent chap.<br /> <br /> Have you ever read fiction of that period? The protagonists tend to be pretty bad by our moral standards, but were also clearly the heores of their own narrative - this doesn't make their narrative correct in any way or fashion, however, but I would say it does make them <i>relatable and playable</i>. In ways Nephandi aren't<br /> <br /> Unless the ST it's constanlty sending me against natives and colonized people, my Scotland Yard detective *would* be, perhaps not good, but decent. In a limited fashion.<br /> <br /> What I don't get it's to support an imperialistic institution w/o getting dirt. I don't get to say my detective isn't evil, that he isn't ignoring (and proffiting from) the suffering of innocents. My character either it's very ignorant, or, more likely, thinks Britain IT'S superior. This is very patently evil, evil as Sao Cristavo from the OoH - but it doesn't need to make the character unplayable in any way, if the ST isn't merciless about it.<br /> <br /> Hence why I think the contradiction it's a fake one. It's a very different kind of evil.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's the chance of being a good mage within the OoR trying to figth it's evils. But these members clearly weren't the ones to call the shots, and were limited in what they could do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:20:19-08:00","id":1439214,"title":"","content":"YES to a homegrown Indian scientific faction that isn't atheist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439199#post1439199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much to say: in all three cases, the nation in question for hit by the Order of Reason/Technocracy, which demonstrated inordinate effectiveness with their Technology that convinced mages in those nations to try to adopt it as their own as a way to fight the Union. That resulted in Technomantic Crafts that either stood in opposition to the Union or attempted to infiltrate and subvert it. Little is said about the specifics of their theory and practice; just that they're trying to use the Union's tools against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Have they got names? Or listed Future Fates? Did they try to coopt the Technocrats or directly oppose them?<br /> <br /> The Chinese ones are Dalou'laishi and the Japanese ones are Jidai, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:20:42-08:00","id":1439215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439208#post1439208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not a question of it being impossible to play an individual who isn\u2019t a genocidal racist, it\u2019s a matter of the institution they\u2019re part of actively carrying out genocide, so it\u2019s a bit different from the Nephandi in that regard.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m starting to agree that the sidebar might have been an over correction against imperial fetishism, and getting it to a more balanced tone while including more references to the horrific part of the Victorian \u201cScientific\u201d Paradigm in the actual Convention writeup, and conflicts around those (say Hippocratic internal conflict between spreading public health, vs Malthusian efforts against surplus population) would be stronger, and have submitted feedback to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be my preferred solution as well. The problem with the write up as is is that it presents the situation as one where there is no internal conflict, as opposed to there being opposition within the Union but it being on the losing side. <br /> <br /> Or, and I know this isn't popular here, there's always the option to say that yes, these things did in fact happen and should not be whitewashed; but that's not what my Chronicle is going to be about. I understand that the reason why it is not popular is it it treads extremely close to whitewashing; but it's something that's <i>going</i> to happen, as there are gametes who don't want to play either the evil Technocrat or the fight against the evil Technocrat (whether it's from within our from without); so I think I'd like to see some advice on how to do that without stepping over the line into racist tropes. Say, something out of the Etherite Adventurers that doesn't make the mistake of presenting the locals as backward savages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:26:39-08:00","id":1439216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439215#post1439215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that would be my preferred solution as well. The problem with the write up as is is that it presents the situation as one where there is no internal conflict, as opposed to there being opposition within the Union but it being on the losing side. <br /> <br /> Or, and I know this isn't popular here, there's always the option to say that yes, these things did in fact happen and should not be whitewashed; but that's not what my Chronicle is going to be about. I understand that the reason why it is not popular is it it treads extremely close to whitewashing; but it's something that's <i>going</i> to happen, as there are gametes who don't want to play either the evil Technocrat or the fight against the evil Technocrat (whether it's from within our from without); so I think I'd like to see some advice on how to do that without stepping over the line into racist tropes. Say, something out of the Etherite Adventurers that doesn't make the mistake of presenting the locals as backward savages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the game makes allowances for that, as long as you're ok with the locals in question being space aliens or Atlantians or some other made up thing that wasn't brutalized and denigrated by imperialism. It's really more a matter of recognizing which genre tropes are harmless fun and which are edging into problematic territory.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I want to highlight the Celestial Masters in all of this, because even as the rest of the Order is engaging in atrocity after atrocity, there's this poor underfunded Convention that literally just wants to go to space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:28:37-08:00","id":1439217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439204#post1439204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason I phrase things in an earlier post as one of the sources of cognitive dissonance being the contrast between the Victorian Technocracy being portrayed as evil as the Nephandi and them being portrayed as a playable faction: playing the Nephandi has been explicitly discouraged all throughout the Mage line. If there isn't a way to present the option to play a Victorian Technocrat who isn't a genocidal racist, then the books approach to the Technocracy ought to the similar to The Book of the Fallen approach to the Nephandi: \u201cwe really recommend against playing them. Instead, here's some advice on how to recognize and combat the evils they represent.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, there's a lot of room to be had playing someone in an evil organization that they aren't necessarily WILLINGLY a part of. One of the recommendations in the GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY is <i>La Femme Nikita</i> which is based around the premise of being an assassin who is, essentially, working under pain of deaths. In this situation, escape from the Union is obviously a major goal.<br /> <br /> Imagine being a young person of color or political radical (Karl Marx is a Unionist but probably very unpopular in the capitalist driven British Empire) only to be recruited at the point of a gun to buld weapons because you're Awakened. Something that the game de-emphasized is that you do not always get a CHOICE to be part of the Union. Brainwashing is a thing but so is threats to you or your family.<br /> <br /> You can build up to the Electrodyne Engineers defection that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:28:46-08:00","id":1439218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439216#post1439216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the game makes allowances for that, as long as you're ok with the locals in question being space aliens. It's really more a matter of recognizing which genre tropes are harmless fun and which are edging into problematic territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that depicting the victims of genocide as space aliens, werewolves, Umbrood, changelings, talking animals, or bygones makes it OK to play with the justified-imperialism trope.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that oppressed racial and disabled groups are actively dehumanized, and that some of those fantasic creatures originate in allegories about dehumanized humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:32:25-08:00","id":1439219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439211#post1439211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want an Indian technomancer faction. The Indian subcontinent has an astonishing and wondrous history of scientific and technological accomplishment on par with anything Rome or China did, and this would have been a great place to highlight this. It really would have underlined the amount of scientific knowledge and technology that imperialism actually destroyed. Not to say the other techno-Crafts aren't great (they are), but many of them are explicitly described as adopting or being formed in reaction to the Union, as opposed to being outgrowths of their own home culture's tradition of inquiry and innovation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chinese one is kind of doing that. Specifically, the Dalou'loushi have been around for a long time, and have been technocrats throughout their existence. The reason why they didn't balloon into a scientific revolution according to the book is because the Wu Lung restrained them. <br /> <br /> But yes, I could go for an Indian Luminary Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:33:16-08:00","id":1439221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439213#post1439213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's where my example of Scotland Yard shines - and while I don't have the book I seem to remember that WAS an option.<br /> <br /> A Nephandi it's almost <i>cartoonishly </i>evil. A Nephandi doesn't need to think himself as good while doing or supporting bad things, they do bad things &quot;for the evil&quot;. They support Satan because he's bad, not because they mistakenly think of demons as misunderstood spirits. Heck, I've seen implied they want to betray Satan too, because he's too good for their tastes.<br /> <br /> Nephandi do want to see the world burn.<br /> <br /> All Victorian Technocrats are, by action or omission, supporting a genocidal institution - but they do so within a historical context, and that's a rational perspective it's easy to accomodate. I don't need to think of VT as anything but &quot;the bad guys&quot; to play a Technocrat that is a farly decent chap.<br /> <br /> Have you ever read fiction of that period? The protagonists tend to be pretty bad by our moral standards, but were also clearly the heores of their own narrative - this doesn't make their narrative correct in any way or fashion, however, but I would say it does make them <i>relatable and playable</i>. In ways Nephandi aren't<br /> <br /> Unless the ST it's constanlty sending me against natives and colonized people, my Scotland Yard detective *would* be, perhaps not good, but decent. In a limited fashion.<br /> <br /> What I don't get it's to support an imperialistic institution w/o getting dirt. I don't get to say my detective isn't evil, that he isn't ignoring (and proffiting) from the suffering of innocents. My character either it's very ignorant, or, more likely, thinks Britain IT'S superior. This is very patently evil, eivl as Sao Cristavo from the OoH - but it doesn't need to make the character unplayable in any way, if the ST isn't merciless about it.<br /> <br /> Hence why I think the contradiction it's a fake one. It's a very different kind of evil.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's the chance of being a good mage within the OoR trying to figth it's evils. But these members clearly weren't the ones to call the shots, and were limited in what they could do</div> </div> </div> </div>To do a different perspective.<br /> <br /> It's The WHEEL OF TIME.<br /> <br /> The Seanchan and the Children of Light are based on real-world conquering Imperial states as well as the Hollywood version of the Papal Inquisition as well as Teutonic Knights/Knights Templar. The Darkfriends are literally the servants of the Dark One (Satan) and working to bring about the apocalypse. So the Technocracy and the Nephandi/their cultists.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is that historically, fans have felt the Darkfriends were MORE sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Because they were often people who were tricked/coerced or brought down by EPIC TRAGIC FLAWS.<br /> <br /> While the Seanchan and Children of Light are just fascists, racist, and slavers. Them believing they're the good guys make them LESS sympathetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:34:12-08:00","id":1439223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439214#post1439214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YES to a homegrown Indian scientific faction that isn't atheist.<br /> <br /> Cool. Have they got names? Or listed Future Fates? Did they try to coopt the Technocrats or directly oppose them?<br /> <br /> The Chinese ones are Dalou'laishi and the Japanese ones are Jidai, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And the Zulu one just says Zulu mechanists. Apparently, they never chose a formal name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe