eylel Thoabath and the Janissaries. Because the Nephandi are by nature more extreme than mere infernalists or traitors, and once you know somebody's Nephandi you realize they have been torturing and eating babies just for fun this whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:36:20-08:00","id":1439225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439218#post1439218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that depicting the victims of genocide as space aliens, werewolves, Umbrood, changelings, talking animals, or bygones makes it OK to play with the justified-imperialism trope.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that oppressed racial and disabled groups are actively dehumanized, and that some of those fantasic creatures originate in allegories about dehumanized humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of the X-men really.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy isn't supposed to be racist but their definition of &quot;reality deviant&quot; seem to include of indiginous cultures.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the best benefit of the X-men isn't that it teaches racism against mutants is wrong, its that a large number of the X-men are of color.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:39:37-08:00","id":1439228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439218#post1439218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that depicting the victims of genocide as space aliens, werewolves, Umbrood, changelings, talking animals, or bygones makes it OK to play with the justified-imperialism trope.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that oppressed racial and disabled groups are actively dehumanized, and that some of those fantasic creatures originate in allegories about dehumanized humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That came out wrong, and I'm sorry about that. What I meant was that there's nothing wrong with having gonzo adventures that don't focus on man's inhumanity to man, but you probably have to do it on the other side of the Gauntlet, because there's no getting around the fact that what's happening on Earth is pretty generally fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:44:38-08:00","id":1439231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439225#post1439225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of the X-men really.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy isn't supposed to be racist but their definition of &quot;reality deviant&quot; seem to include of indiginous cultures.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the best benefit of the X-men isn't that it teaches racism against mutants is wrong, its that a large number of the X-men are of color.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the WOD, in which all those nonhumans are <i>people</i>, genocide against them is just as evil as genocide against any human group. I purposely leave out vampires because they are cannibalistic parasites and I'm not familiar with how morally grey they're capable of being. But the rest? No way that genocide/the Pogrom/the Oath of Fire is anything but pure, irredeemable evil.<br /> <br /> This is the same reason I can't abide Imbued hunters as PCs. The self-righteous delusion and lie that they're The Good Guys just makes me hate them more, like the Technocracy and (in the Wheel of Time) the Children of Light.<br /> <br /> It's why I find it odd that people think of the Sorcerer's Crusade-era Order of Reason as less evil than the Victorian Technocracy. The moment they swore the Oath of Fire, they dedicated themselves to omnicide for the sake of omnicide, and hate for the sake of hate. Also... you know in The Fragile Path where they torture the First Cabal just for sadistic pleasure, instead of cleanly killing them? Yeah, and the Technocracy has continued that practice uninterrupted up to the modern day and even after the Avatar Storm. Heck, they're worse than Nephandi and Black Spiral Dancers in a way, because they do this of their own free will, on purpose, just because they want to instead of having their Avatar turned inside out. They're people who could stop committing atrocities any time they wanted, and simply <i>choose</i> to continue.<br /> <br /> I don't think players should get a break to play a member of that and pretend their PC is any better than the Sabbat or Ba'ali vampires, unless they're opposed to ALL of that -- the genocide, the imperialism, the torture, the Pogrom, the fascism... in short, every single thing the Order of Reason stands for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:53:53-08:00","id":1439234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439228#post1439228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That came out wrong, and I'm sorry about that. What I meant was that there's nothing wrong with having gonzo adventures that don't focus on man's inhumanity to man, but you probably have to do it on the other side of the Gauntlet, because there's no getting around the fact that what's happening on Earth is pretty generally fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I didn't want my post to come across as accusing you of imperialism-apologia, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:56:52-08:00","id":1439235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439213#post1439213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's where my example of Scotland Yard shines - and while I don't have the book I seem to remember that WAS an option.<br /> <br /> A Nephandi it's almost <i>cartoonishly </i>evil. A Nephandi doesn't need to think himself as good while doing or supporting bad things, they do bad things &amp;quot;for the evil&amp;quot;. They support Satan because he's bad, not because they mistakenly think of demons as misunderstood spirits. Heck, I've seen implied they want to betray Satan too, because he's too good for their tastes.<br /> <br /> Nephandi do want to see the world burn.<br /> <br /> All Victorian Technocrats are, by action or omission, supporting a genocidal institution - but they do so within a historical context, and that's a rational perspective it's easy to accomodate. I don't need to think of VT as anything but &amp;quot;the bad guys&amp;quot; to play a Technocrat that is a farly decent chap.<br /> <br /> Have you ever read fiction of that period? The protagonists tend to be pretty bad by our moral standards, but were also clearly the heores of their own narrative - this doesn't make their narrative correct in any way or fashion, however, but I would say it does make them <i>relatable and playable</i>. In ways Nephandi aren't<br /> <br /> Unless the ST it's constanlty sending me against natives and colonized people, my Scotland Yard detective *would* be, perhaps not good, but decent. In a limited fashion.<br /> <br /> What I don't get it's to support an imperialistic institution w/o getting dirt. I don't get to say my detective isn't evil, that he isn't ignoring (and proffiting from) the suffering of innocents. My character either it's very ignorant, or, more likely, thinks Britain IT'S superior. This is very patently evil, evil as Sao Cristavo from the OoH - but it doesn't need to make the character unplayable in any way, if the ST isn't merciless about it.<br /> <br /> Hence why I think the contradiction it's a fake one. It's a very different kind of evil.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's the chance of being a good mage within the OoR trying to figth it's evils. But these members clearly weren't the ones to call the shots, and were limited in what they could do</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone mentioned Atlantis recently, which reminded me of Disney's animated Atlantis movie. That would be one way to include the evils of imperialism in the game without making your OoR protagonists evil: you're playing Milo and the gang who are idealists searching for Atlantis; and when the leader of the expedition starts the plunder, you end up siding with Kida and her people. And you don't get blacklisted from the Order for doing so. <br /> <br /> Anna and the King does something similar, in that Anna want a genocidal racist (though she did hold some cultural chauvinist beliefs), and the clash between her and the King was one of differing worldviews rather than oppressor vs. oppressed; and when her own people decided to assassinate the King, she ended up helping him out. Again, without being punished for standing against the British Empire. If you're going to include the evils of imperialism in your chronicle while having the protagonists aligned with the Union, that's the way to do it. <br /> <br /> And incidentally, that's also something to consider: at this point in the Technocracy's history, you don't have Room 101 or Conditioning; while the Union as a whole is doing evil things, is still at a stage in its existence where individual Technocrats aren't being forced into conformity. That doesn't happen until well into the 20th century, with the rise of the NWO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T10:58:40-08:00","id":1439236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439231#post1439231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the WOD, in which all those nonhumans are <i>people</i>, genocide against them is just as evil as genocide against any human group. I purposely leave out vampires because they are cannibalistic parasites and I'm not familiar with how morally grey they're capable of being. But the rest? No way that genocide/the Pogrom/the Oath of Fire is anything but pure, irredeemable evil.<br /> <br /> This is the same reason I can't abide Imbued hunters as PCs. The self-righteous delusion and lie that they're The Good Guys just makes me hate them more, like the Technocracy and (in the Wheel of Time) the Children of Light.<br /> <br /> It's why I find it odd that people think of the Sorcerer's Crusade-era Order of Reason as less evil than the Victorian Technocracy. The moment they swore the Oath of Fire, they dedicated themselves to omnicide for the sake of omnicide, and hate for the sake of hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that said gonzo adventures should involve destroying entire alien species and Umbrood courts. I'm saying that in the Umbra, any story you tell won't exist under the grim shadow of the fact that everyone you meet there has or will be brutalized and exploited by your compatriots. They're fictional worlds, meaning that they can allow you to explore what could have been, instead of the grim reality that actually happened, without whitewashing or downplaying the horror inflicted on real, non-fictional people on this side of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:05:57-08:00","id":1439240,"title":"","content":"It doesn't necessarily have to be a matter of crossing the Gauntlet. At this point, the Hollow Earth hasn't yet been banished to the other side of a Gauntlet; there's even a section about how the Void Seekers are working on making away such locations; though I think that there's still room for some who are actually trying to explore them instead. Another case of a majority/minority rift, or perhaps a change in mission statement as the Victorian Age progresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:11:32-08:00","id":1439243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439224#post1439224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Admittedly, the closest Mage equivalent is like, Heylel Thoabath and the Janissaries. Because the Nephandi are by nature more extreme than mere infernalists or traitors, and once you know somebody's Nephandi you realize they have been torturing and eating babies just for fun this whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember Sennex and Mercy?<br /> <br /> She became a Nephandi for love.<br /> <br /> Which is....the worst reason.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:35:29-08:00","id":1439249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439231#post1439231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's why I find it odd that people think of the Sorcerer's Crusade-era Order of Reason as less evil than the Victorian Technocracy. The moment they swore the Oath of Fire, they dedicated themselves to omnicide for the sake of omnicide, and hate for the sake of hate. Also... you know in The Fragile Path where they torture the First Cabal just for sadistic pleasure, instead of cleanly killing them? Yeah, and the Technocracy has continued that practice uninterrupted up to the modern day and even after the Avatar Storm. Heck, they're worse than Nephandi and Black Spiral Dancers in a way, because they do this of their own free will, on purpose, just because they want to instead of having their Avatar turned inside out. They're people who could stop committing atrocities any time they wanted, and simply <i>choose</i> to continue.<br /> <br /> I don't think players should get a break to play a member of that and pretend their PC is any better than the Sabbat or Ba'ali vampires, unless they're opposed to ALL of that -- the genocide, the imperialism, the torture, the Pogrom, the fascism... in short, every single thing the Order of Reason stands for.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I can count the number of playable factions in WoD that haven't committed myriad atrocities, up to and including genocide, on one hand.<br /> <br /> Not that that absolves them of guilt, but when you sign up to play WoD, working for superiors and elders who are actively reprehensible in every way imaginable kinda comes with the territory.<br /> <br /> They might be worse than (most of) the Traditions, but it's hard to call them exceptionally evil compared to the Garou or the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:44:32-08:00","id":1439251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439211#post1439211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want an Indian technomancer faction. The Indian subcontinent has an astonishing and wondrous history of scientific and technological accomplishment on par with anything Rome or China did, and this would have been a great place to highlight this. It really would have underlined the amount of scientific knowledge and technology that imperialism actually destroyed. Not to say the other techno-Crafts aren't great (they are), but many of them are explicitly described as adopting or being formed in reaction to the Union, as opposed to being outgrowths of their own home culture's tradition of inquiry and innovation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, heck 18th century Britain studied India's agricultural technologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:50:38-08:00","id":1439255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439177#post1439177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all have some good points, folks.<br /> <br /> The notion of science-as-superior-technology is very much the mainstream notion that supports the notiion of white culture as superior. In real life, I am all in favor of trying to view the world objectively, and yet real science (in the real world) is agnostic on the existence of God and such. The core of <b>real</b> science isn't dogmatic atheism or racial superiority, it's objectively accepting the world as we observe it, preconceived notions be damned. Real science requires the humility to always say &quot;I could be wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the WOD? Real science would look at the supernatural elements of the world and acknowledges they exist and are significant, including the entire spirit world and the obvious efficacy of Mystick magick. It can't be anything <b>but</b> delusion to call supernatural elements &quot;reality deviants&quot;, and to bend over backwards inventing a complex, anti-Occam's-razor delusion like Tychoidean cosmology to explain away the obvious reality of the spirit world. The Technocratic paradigm only works on a basis of anti-science censorship. And in the real world, idiocy like Euro-American fire-suppression also isn't remotely scientific, it's just an exercise in blindly declaring that white ways are always superior to Native ways, and ignoring the constant avalanche of evidence disproving that BS.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer, I don't own any Mage corebooks. But to see how many people read the Mage message as &quot;science is evil&quot; suggest to me that the messaging hasn't been effective in conveying how utterly deluded and non-scientific the Technocray really is. They ought to be depicted as <i>non</i>-mainstream scientists, who manipulate sleeper scientists and silence the ones who discover or invent anything Control wants to destroy. The ones who erase the history of non-European scientific practices and kill off everyone who practices or remembers them, so they can continue lying about white people &quot;inventing&quot; science and suppress the scientific knowledge of other cultures. Their thing is mechanical technology, not the scientific method.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more complicated than that. First off, of all the factions within the entire World of Darkness, the Technocracy has received the most change and evolution across the editions. Seriously, early 1E Technocracy is utterly alien compared to the Technocracy of M20.<br /> <br /> Like in the second MtAs book, the adventure module Loom of Fate, sees the Technocrats attempting to replace a dying Weaver Spirit by turning a young Orphan mage (a Mage with no alignment to any Tradition, Convention or Craft) into a new Weaver Spirit. All because early MtAs tried to have loose connections to WtA and the Triad with the Technocracy being connected to the Weaver. M20 Technocrats would look at those Technocrats as at best lunatics, at worst Nephandi or Marauders pretending to be Technocrats.<br /> <br /> But because of that evolving view of them, depending when you came into Mage and what books you read, will HEAVILY influence how you view them. For example I came into MtAs with the Rev Ed which had taken a middle of the road stance on the Union. They were shady and certainly villains to the Traditions but at the same time the Rev Ed in the beginning was depressed and apathetic, with the Ascension War begin waged between the two factions fizzling out, both sides loosing as the Masses chose instead to wallow in muck than reach for something higher regardless of what either side were selling.<br /> <br /> Basically I saw them as bad guys but not necessarily the worst of the bad guys.<br /> <br /> Then I got to 2E's Guide to the Technocracy and saw just how nuanced and complicated the Union was. The Technocracy for me moved from being antagonists to being alternate protagonists of MtAs. Certainly they were more morally questionable in their actions than the Traditions but it gave the whole line a new layer of depth to not just them but the whole line. They were trying to protect the Masses from the various dangerous supernatural things in the WoD while trying to advance Humanity and down the path of Enlightenment. Their path admittedly but it was still more than the Traditions seemed to be doing, as all they seemed to be doing is waging war on the Technocracy. Though likewise, with the Traditions that's much more complicated than it seems at first glance. This was just my more simplistic view of things as I first dived into MtAs.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Introduction Chapter of Guide had a really good opening.<br /> <br /> It was also around that time that I started coming into contact with the larger WoD fandom, mostly at local stores and players but also some online interactions. That's when I first discovered that there were people that strongly hated the Technocracy. And while I could understand some of it, I couldn't completely understand it.<br /> <br /> Then I read the 1E Convention Books and understood where those people were coming from...<br /> <br /> Because, yeah the early books treated the Technocracy as one-note villains and at times, really the over the top of their villainy.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy of M20 is in line with the trend of Guide to the Technocracy but with the Union realizing two things. First, the previous generations of Technocrats were... well... *Points to Victorian Mage* and trying to get away from that. The Euro-centric nature of the Union is giving way to a more Global Union. Some of the more recent books have straight up have Technocrats criticize the actions of their predecessors or talk about how their demographics are changing with the world. <br /> <br /> The second is much more alarming for them, that for all their plans and Time Tables and attempts to elevate Humanity, they have forgotten to factor into an important thing, the Masses themselves. The Sleepers like the toys the Technocracy provides them but they don't want to actually reach out for Enlightenment. Indeed, in many ways the Sleepers are rejecting Logic and Reason and Science as much as they are Magic and Spirituality.<br /> <br /> Case in point, the Progenitors <u><i><b>HATE</b></i></u> Faith Healers, the Anti-vaxx Movement and the like. So much so that despite the Union ending their Pogroms against Supernaturalist Mages and wanting to get away from those methods, some Progenitors want to restart it in hopes of ending that nonsense and all the harm it's doing because some of those Mages have helped spread those ideas because they either line up with their Beliefs or to weaken the Beliefs the Technocracy is trying to impose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would somebody please summarize for me the Zulu, Chinese, and Japanese technomagic factions in VAM? I would like to know some about them. </div> </div> </div>Chinese Dalou\u2019laoshi (or Five Elemental Dragons) were a group that already existed, originally as a group of Asian Technocrats, part of the Union but different. You know, back in that Year of Lotus stuff. Certainly they weren't the worst but they were kind of not great either. The modern take on them now is as a specifically Chinese group of Technomancers that would go on to join the Order of Reason/Technocracy.<br /> <br /> In VAM, the Dalou\u2019laoshi are still independent Technomancers though they have been in a loose partnership with the Wulong, the Chinese Craft that has long dominated the Courts of Imperial China. However it is not a happy partnership for the Dalou\u2019laoshi as while the Wulong are happy to use their works and inventions, they have long been hindering the Dalou\u2019laoshi's attempts to increase their influence within China as the Wulong don't want anyone to challenge their stranglehold on power within China or the social order that supports them.<br /> <br /> But with the Europeans entering Eastern Asia, bringing with them new ideas and inventions, the Qing Dynasty crumbling and all the rising chaos being generated by all that, the Dalou\u2019laoshi find themselves at a crossroads. In earlier years, the Order of Reason had approached them with joining but the Dalou\u2019laoshi rebuffed them as like the Wulong, they were very China-centric and kind of looked down on those outside of China.<br /> <br /> There's now three rising factions within the Dalou\u2019laoshi, centered around what they're going to do in response to this all. The first group thinks that joining the Order is the best option for them, that doing so will not just ensure their protection but give them a seat at the table when it comes to deciding the future of China. Second wants to join with the Wulong and Akashayana in fighting the Order. The third and likely smallest of these groups are those that seek to utterly reform China, to modernize it technologically and socially, pushing out the Order, the Europeans and the old Imperialists. In fact, few even dream of creating a pan-Asian alliance of magi against the Europeans.<br /> <br /> Historically, the first group wins out after the Boxer Rebellion that second group backed failed and the Dalou\u2019laoshi becomes a part of the Order/Union.<br /> <br /> The Jidai (or Next Era) of Japan are a new group for MtAs (at least as far as I know) so there isn't much on them. They were Japanese Technomancers that came together during Oda Nobunaga's reunification of Japan and likely bolstered by the country's trade with Europe during that time but went into decline during the period of isolation that followed.<br /> <br /> When Admiral Perry's Expedition shattered that isolation, the Jidai saw as their chance to rise. While Japanese magi panicked and saw their Magicks being threatened by the changing Consensus, the Jidai thrived as never before. They embraced modernizing Japan, believing it to be the only way to maintain Japanese independence.<br /> <br /> But it's also likely that they will help bring about the expansionist Empire of Japan in the coming decades.<br /> <br /> Currently they are independent of the Order but thanks to the importing of Western experts while sending Japanese observers to the West to aid in the modernization of Japan, the two groups have come into contact with each other. At the moment, both groups are looking to use the other for their own advantage.<br /> <br /> Their likely fate is like that of the Dalou\u2019laoshi, joining the Union.<br /> <br /> Finally the Zulu Mechanists. They are new, having been born as a reaction to the clashes with the Boer. Basically some Zulu Magi saw what the Boer and their technology was capable of against their warriors and were horrified by it. In response, some of these magi abandoned their previous ways and are embracing Technomancy to compete against the Europeans. That said, they are still holding to some of their older practices. So they are probably the most mystical of the Technomancers of this Age.<br /> <br /> Like the Dalou\u2019laoshi, there is a divide within the group, those it's more between those of a more warrior mindset and those more focused on their crafts.<br /> <br /> As with the Jidai, they are a new faction for MtAs and we don't really know what their fate is. Likely outcome is either getting absorbed into the Union or fracturing between those join the Union, the Traditions and Crafts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T11:51:56-08:00","id":1439256,"title":"","content":"Where would you put the very real 18th and 19th century British scholars who worked to find, print in volume, and distribute India's ancient literature to Indians? Works like the Mahabharata and the Ramayana were nearly lost in the 18th century. British scholars found manuscripts, edited them, and printed vast numbers of copies. Whatever the motives, the action was good for India's people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:00:08-08:00","id":1439257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439235#post1439235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone mentioned Atlantis recently, which reminded me of Disney's animated Atlantis movie. That would be one way to include the evils of imperialism in the game without making your OoR protagonists evil: you're playing Milo and the gang who are idealists searching for Atlantis; and when the leader of the expedition starts the plunder, you end up siding with Kida and her people. And you don't get blacklisted from the Order for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the OoR leadership it's represented by a benevolent cranky old dude that want's to find Atlantis for a bet, and totally didn't wanted to kill everyone.<br /> <br /> But a bad, bad hombre, that totally doesn't represent the Order as a whole, wanted to kill everyone to get rich because he's mean, convinced everyone of doing that, but latter everyone saw the cruelty in doing this and killed that bad hombre, they come back saying they found nothing but well, they tried - the end.<br /> <br /> I'm totally ok with the player being like Milo, perhaps even with the development, but I'm suspicious of your last implication.<br /> <br /> I'm not ok at all about saying that enslaving the indians and taking their magick wasn't the 1\u00b0 and foremost goal of those who funded the expedition, and thus he wouldn't be reprimended <i>at all</i> by failing at doing this. Esp. if this gets repeated in other missions<br /> <br /> Perhaps blacklisted would be too much because he said Atlantis was a myth after all (or something on those lines), but it shouldn't be all laughs and happy ending.<br /> <br /> I'm not OK about portraying the leadership as sympathetic in this context. You ARE rebelling against the grand and obvious goals of the Union, you should at least have some problems when you fail over and over to produce the desired results - because genocide IS the desired result here. Saying anything else would be crapping in all we talked in this thread<br /> <br /> Ah...maybe I'm not remembering something of the movie. But if I'm not far, far, off: that's a good example of what whitewashing imperialism is. It also has good savages to make it better. Really?, <b><i>Disney</i></b> ..., well, let's leave it at that <i>Disney may not be a good example about how to not do whitewashing</i><br /> <br /> I think you really, really, want the OoR <i>as an institution </i>to not be the bad guys. That the bad things are someting that a few vocal ones, like the bad guys in these Disney movies, endorse. But not the organization itself. And that, that, I'm not OK with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:02:13-08:00","id":1439258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439256#post1439256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would you put the very real 18th and 19th century British scholars who worked to find, print in volume, and distribute India's ancient literature to Indians? Works like the Mahabharata and the Ramayana were nearly lost in the 18th century. British scholars found manuscripts, edited them, and printed vast numbers of copies. Whatever the motives, the action was good for India's people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put them in the Grand Faculty, or perhaps the Lightkeepers, as part of the \u201cthere's good in the Order, too\u201d side of things. Again: the good doesn't excuse the bad; but neither does the bad invalidate the good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:08:33-08:00","id":1439260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439258#post1439258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put them in the Grand Faculty, or perhaps the Lightkeepers, as part of the \u201cthere's good in the Order, too\u201d side of things. Again: the good doesn't excuse the bad; but neither does the bad invalidate the good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to throw my hat into the ring for the Blue Cog Cognate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:14:22-08:00","id":1439262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy of M20 is in line with the trend of Guide to the Technocracy but with the Union realizing two things. First, the previous generations of Technocrats were... well... *Points to Victorian Mage* and trying to get away from that. The Euro-centric nature of the Union is giving way to a more Global Union. Some of the more recent books have straight up have Technocrats criticize the actions of their predecessors or talk about how their demographics are changing with the world </div> </div> </div>The problem I had with the Convention books was that they were all about whitewashing (in the context of making them more moral and justified not racially) the Union so much so that the ITERATION X Revised Convention book removed all morally repugnant elements that the Guide to the Union left in (that everyone was &quot;Conditioned&quot;/brainwashed and terrorism as a Skill). Making them better because of the Avatar Storm is fine.<br /> <br /> BUTTTttt...<br /> <br /> Now is not the time to believe that the Establishment, Corporate rule, government, politicians, and militaristic idealogues to be the Good GuysTM. My big problem with the M20 guide to the Union is, &quot;Uh, where are the racist assholes?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't mind them being opposed by globalist progressives in the Union but they ABSOLUTELY would still be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:20:24-08:00","id":1439263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439262#post1439262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I had with the Convention books was that they were all about whitewashing (in the context of making them more moral and justified not racially) the Union so much so that the ITERATION X Revised Convention book removed all morally repugnant elements that the Guide to the Union left in (that everyone was &quot;Conditioned&quot;/brainwashed and terrorism as a Skill). Making them better because of the Avatar Storm is fine.<br /> <br /> BUTTTttt...<br /> <br /> Now is not the time to believe that the Establishment, Corporate rule, government, politicians, and militaristic idealogues to be the Good GuysTM. My big problem with the M20 guide to the Union is, &quot;Uh, where are the racist assholes?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't mind them being opposed by globalist progressives in the Union but they ABSOLUTELY would still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean globalism and globalists can be hella racist in its own right--colonization being the creation of a global system of oppression that hasn't really changed much-- but yeah I agree with your read of where did all the racists go.<br /> <br /> Reconciliation commissions, more participatory or collaborative relations with domestic dependent indigenous nations, and multiculturalism have all been heavily criticized as just modern moves to hide or evade historical responsibility and contemporary atrocities. Just look at the Trudeau administration in Canada. Wants to act like they are all friendly with First Nations People but indigenous people are still wildly over represented in the prison system, oil companies are still given greater leeway and support, and violence against Indigenous peoples is on the rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:25:31-08:00","id":1439265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439256#post1439256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would you put the very real 18th and 19th century British scholars who worked to find, print in volume, and distribute India's ancient literature to Indians? Works like the Mahabharata and the Ramayana were nearly lost in the 18th century. British scholars found manuscripts, edited them, and printed vast numbers of copies. Whatever the motives, the action was good for India's people.</div> </div> </div> </div>W/O context? I would put that as the work of the Traditions, or Disparate, or humans using well established mojo...<br /> <br /> Because it makes 0 sense for the Union in any period of history to foment the exact same religious practices they label as deviant and are actively figthing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:30:09-08:00","id":1439266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439262#post1439262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I had with the Convention books was that they were all about whitewashing (in the context of making them more moral and justified not racially) the Union so much so that the ITERATION X Revised Convention book removed all morally repugnant elements that the Guide to the Union left in (that everyone was &quot;Conditioned&quot;/brainwashed and terrorism as a Skill). Making them better because of the Avatar Storm is fine.<br /> <br /> BUTTTttt...<br /> <br /> Now is not the time to believe that the Establishment, Corporate rule, government, politicians, and militaristic idealogues to be the Good GuysTM. My big problem with the M20 guide to the Union is, &quot;Uh, where are the racist assholes?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't mind them being opposed by globalist progressives in the Union but they ABSOLUTELY would still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the revised conbooks action do a good job at adding nuance to the Conventions without totally excusing them. Not to mention, the Revised conbooks were meant for Union player characters, and were paired with in-universe attempts at reforms being made, rather than just retconning the skeletons out of their closet entirely. ItX, in particular, replaces the stupid &quot;they want to make you a CYBORG so you're no longer part of NATURE, isn't that SCARY!?&quot; schtick with a more nuanced and human, but still chilling, critique about their (and by extension, the general tech sector's) complicity in the perpetuation of the military industrial complex. <br /> <br /> The transition (in and out of universe) from &quot;Technocracy as implacable imperialist nightmare&quot; to &quot;Technocracy as ostensibly progressive organization that still harms people through their unwillingness to acknowledge the systemic problems created by their forebears&quot; seems perfectly plausible to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:31:02-08:00","id":1439267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: the good doesn't excuse the bad; but neither does the bad invalidate the good.</div> </div> </div> </div>- erased - there's no reason to go there. I'm sorry<br /> <br /> I'm just going to say: Do you know how many apologists of the worst things of humanity go there?<br /> <br /> Even in my own country. Everywhere really. Not denying the bad because it's undeniable, but insisting on focusing also on the good<br /> <br /> You really don't want to go there. I certainly don't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:58:26-08:00","id":1439269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439257#post1439257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the OoR leadership it's represented by a benevolent cranky old dude that want's to find Atlantis for a bet, and totally didn't wanted to kill everyone.<br /> <br /> But a bad, bad hombre, that totally doesn't represent the Order as a whole, wanted to kill everyone to get rich because he's mean, convinced everyone of doing that, but latter everyone saw the cruelty in doing this and killed that bad hombre, they come back saying they found nothing but well, they tried - the end.<br /> <br /> I'm totally ok with the player being like Milo, perhaps even with the development, but I'm suspicious of your last implication.<br /> <br /> I'm not ok at all about saying that enslaving the indians and taking their magick wasn't the 1\u00b0 and foremost goal of those who funded the expedition, and thus he wouldn't be reprimended <i>at all</i> by failing at doing this. Esp. if this gets repeated in other missions<br /> <br /> Perhaps blacklisted would be too much because he said Atlantis was a myth after all (or something on those lines), but it shouldn't be all laughs and happy ending.<br /> <br /> I'm not OK about portraying the leadership as sympathetic in this context. You ARE rebelling against the grand and obvious goals of the Union, you should at least have some problems when you fail over and over to produce the desired results - because genocide IS the desired result here. Saying anything else would be crapping in all we talked in this thread<br /> <br /> Ah...maybe I'm not remembering something of the movie. But if I'm not far, far, off: that's a good example of what whitewashing imperialism is. It also has good savages to make it better. Really?, <b><i>Disney</i></b> ..., well, let's leave it at that <i>Disney may not be a good example about how to not do whitewashing</i><br /> <br /> I think you really, really, want the OoR <i>as an institution </i>to not be the bad guys. That the bad things are someting that a few vocal ones, like the bad guys in these Disney movies, endorse. But not the organization itself. And that, that, I'm not OK with</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier (paraphrasing), it would be nice to address the \u201cgonzo adventures\u201d aspect of things in terms of what pitfalls to avoid if you go that route. And your suggestion here, that the backer being a nice old man and the villain not representing the Order is the wrong way to go, is the sort of advice I'm thinking of. <br /> <br /> At the risk of triggering another criticism that I'm into Imperialist apologism, let me reiterate my recent point that The Victorian Technocracy is still pre-Conditioning and will be until the rise of the NWO; and that that means that there's more room for dissent within the organization, up to and including in upper management. Again, the Victorian Technocracy includes the Analytical Reckoners and the Electrodyne Engineers; and at the very least, <i>their</i> leadership shouldn't be utterly rotten. I tend to think that that should extend to the other Conventions as well, to being degrees; but the Union can be Imperialists on the whole without insisting that the only good guys in the organization are the ones who aren't in leadership positions.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm not saying to excuse anything. I'm pointing out that this was a period of time when there was a fight for the soul of the Order of Reason. Things started going <i>really</i> bad in 1885 when the Union approached Queen Victoria with a plan for global domination; and that eventually lead to the Etherites jumping ship because by then the Imperialist faction within the Union had all but won. And I'm not saying that the Order of Reason was sunshine and rainbows <i>before</i> 1885; but there was more room for idealists in their ranks back then. <br /> <br /> I think the <i>Atlantis: the Lost Empire</i> model <i>could</i> be used, right up to the benevolent patron, with just one change: make it clear that the <i>patron</i> isn't the guy who represents the Order as a whole; but the plunderer does. Say that he's acting on the orders of someone further up the food chain than even the expedition's financier, rather than just being a guy who let his greed get the better of him. Either say that the financier didn't know about the orders or that he was prevented from stopping it by Order intrigue \u2014 similar to how King Mongkut was forced to put an innocent man to death because of court politics. You're not excusing the imperialism of the Order, or downplaying how bad it was; but you're allowing for the possibility of a Future Fate where the Imperialist impulse can be curbed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2021, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T12:59:56-08:00","id":1439270,"title":"","content":"Akatsukileader and Dataweaver, thanks for that info.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439236#post1439236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that said gonzo adventures should involve destroying entire alien species and Umbrood courts. I'm saying that in the Umbra, any story you tell won't exist under the grim shadow of the fact that everyone you meet there has or will be brutalized and exploited by your compatriots. They're fictional worlds, meaning that they can allow you to explore what could have been, instead of the grim reality that actually happened, without whitewashing or downplaying the horror inflicted on real, non-fictional people on this side of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you didn't mean it that way. Nobody on this thread is arguing in favor of the justified imperialism trope. I was more pointing out an angle that isn't always obvious, because there's no real history of atrocities against fictional creatures, and lots of fiction depicts the like of werewolves and fae as irredeemably evil and deserving of death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439243#post1439243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember Sennex and Mercy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know anything about that story, sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439249#post1439249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, I can count the number of playable factions in WoD that haven't committed myriad atrocities, up to and including genocide, on one hand.<br /> <br /> Not that that absolves them of guilt, but when you sign up to play WoD, working for superiors and elders who are actively reprehensible in every way imaginable kinda comes with the territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no unblemished side in the WoD, true. However, there is a huge difference between what your leaders or ancestors used to do 500 years ago, and what the PCs themselves personally do or support in their <i>current</i> incarnation. The playable Werewolves and changelings in the WoD are not actually Automatically Evil like vampires, and their institutional goals aren't remotely close to the evil of Technocrats and Nephandi. Even during the Wyld West setting, there are individuals or whole factions of almost every Garou tribe who oppose imperialism. Compare [these modern concepts] :<br /> <br /> 1. I'm a werewolf. My ancestors committed genocide 10,000 years ago, and maybe also 400 years ago. I'm white so I benefit from White privilege. Or I'm black or Indigenous or Asian or etc. I'm not in favor of that imperialism shit and my sept han't done that shit for 400+ years. My oldest elders are in their 30s or 40s because our death rate is astronomical. We spend all our time fighting demons and Black-Spiral Dancers because they're constantly trying to kill us and our families, and we're on the defensive back foot. Our entire species is being hunted to extinction. My generation is the last.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm a Hermetic Disciple. My Master is a 500-year-old racist madman, and I mouth off behind his back and try to make my modern, not-a-dou***bag mark in the hopeless quagmire of the Mi'as. I have past life memories of being a colonizing jerkass, which is why I try not to be one in this lifetime. <s>When</s> If the old merlins finally kick the bucket, there are going to be some big changes around here. Er, I hope. I spend most of my time fighting the Technocracy because they're constantly trying to kill me and my friends, and we're on the defensive back foot.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm a wraith. Every single item I own is made out of eternally tortured souls. If I question this, <i>ever</i>, they'll take me to the soulforges next. If I run away, my soul will be shredded instantly by the Maelstrom. There is, literally, no escape from the Hierarchy anywhere. This makes it really hard to argue for hope as I spend every waking minute fighting against the spectre in my head. That's every minute because the dead don't sleep. My rulers/owners are 4000-year old madmen who may be spectres. (Disclaimer: I may or may not be comically uninformed about the details of Wraith.)<br /> <br /> 4. I'm a Technocrat. My job is to direct the robots that clean out the body parts after a torture session. I also help round up Sleeper dissidents for the torture chambers. My side job is mind control to put down pro-democracy and pro-environment activists so we can have the Sleeper military kill off most of them instead of wasting money torturing all of them. If I ever had any notion to question this, the mind-controlling leaders would have killed/reprocessed me last decade, so I'm one of the guys who's A-OK with all of this. We already rule the world, but everyone who disagrees with us needs to die. FOR SCIENCE! My leaders, who are all 300-year old white supremacists, deliberately gave all of Mercury to the Nephandi, just last year, because at least they're not dirty savages. I'm OK with this, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I came into the WoD from Werewolf and that's still the most familiar and favorite game to me, by far. The Werewolves aren't unblemished, and some of them are racists, especially against other shapeshifters. However, most of them no longer knowingly support imperialism, and focused on fighting the Wyrm. They are actively opposed to exploitative capitalism and all the neoimperialism it depends on. Also, within the context of that game, the Technocracy is objectively just as evil as Pentex, and are actively destroying the world. The Fera (who I like much better than Garou anyway) aren't guilty of genocide* and are mostly the people of color <i>opposing</i> neoimperialism. Even when playing Simba* or Red Talons or Ratkin, there are significant factions of each who oppose genocide.<br /> <br /> I've read a fair bit about Mage and Changeling online, but own only a couple books of each and haven't read the corebooks. I ... don't really want to read the Technocracy books. I don't know how much nauseating whitewashing I'd have to wade through to find anything worth reading, and would never play a Technocrat anyway.<br /> <br /> *except the Amandu'o, and I'm no fan of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439263#post1439263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reconciliation commissions, more participatory or collaborative relations with domestic dependent indigenous nations, and multiculturalism have all been heavily criticized as just modern moves to hide or evade historical responsibility and contemporary atrocities. Just look at the Trudeau administration in Canada. Wants to act like they are all friendly with First Nations People but indigenous people are still wildly over represented in the prison system, oil companies are still given greater leeway and support, and violence against Indigenous peoples is on the rise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a big difference between lip-service to multiculturalism, and actually dismantling white supremacy and exploitative capitalism.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that, also, is one of the issues with playing Technocrats. Comparing them to playing Red Talons, Camarilla, Sabbat, Thallain, Black Spiral Dancers, infernalists, or even Nephandi is apples to oranges. Because there is not actually, among gamers or the wider human species, any genuine vocal contingent of people who eat babies, suck blood, want to wipe out the entire human species, sincerely worship Satan, or actually ally with genuine demons or world-destroying Elder Evils.<br /> <br /> But there are a huge, huge number of people - including a depressing proportion of gamers - who want to justify imperialism and capitalist exploitation and white supremacy and pretend these things are good and right in real life. People who freak out and blow a gasket if a Star Wars protagonist has dark skin. People who wouldn't <b>identify personally</b> with vampires or Red Talons or Nephandi, may actually identify with the Technocrats, and want to have an excuse to justfy their actions. Look at the lengths people in the US will go to, to justify genocide and the torture of small children. This is why the Technocracy needs to be treated a bit differently from the other evil factions. Because they represent a real evil that some gamers want to embrace for real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  grammar i can has? 03-11-2021, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:11:04-08:00","id":1439273,"title":"","content":"So my standing to do list for a Vault expansion...<br /> <br /> - Mubarek Maharet Meclisi\u2019s Craft writeup using the section to recontextualizing the divide in the Ahl-I-Batin a bit<br /> <br /> - the Acharne paradigm. The group itself has fallen but adherents to its teachings can be found hidden among Ecstatics and Hermetics<br /> <br /> - Chorus Celestial expansion with ex-Gabrielites contextualizing the risen power of the Septarians, including Transcendentalist resistance in the US, and the legacy of the Second Great Awakening including the Latter Day Saint Chorusters no one else has made heads or tails of yet<br /> <br /> - Vishnudharadhara with a Craft writeup as they defect from the Missionary backing Septarian led Chorus in 1857<br /> <br /> - Lions of Zion Craft writeup with Bat Binah and Chevrah Kedisha splinters in the context of the rising Reform movement<br /> <br /> - The \u201cTrue Levellers\u201d and the \u201cUniversal Brotherhood Ascendent\u201d seperate Craft writeups with the Hollow Ones not existing in any collective named sense until the 1920s<br /> <br /> - Chrysanthemum and Plum Blossom Orphans who reject Jidai reforms and are facing extinction in the face of the Meiji Restoration<br /> <br /> - Galton, Malthus, and the OoR paradigm (some horrific villain rotes here)<br /> <br /> - the actual economic politics around Ether and the plan to remove it from the Consensus<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> i like the idea of a Technomancer historic faction of the Asthika now being forcibly assimilated by the OoR, and possibly a more purely polytheist Verbena-aligned Vedic group... I\u2019ll tinker","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-11-2021, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:13:29-08:00","id":1439274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439265#post1439265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W/O context? I would put that as the work of the Traditions, or Disparate, or humans using well established mojo...<br /> <br /> Because it makes 0 sense for the Union in any period of history to foment the exact same religious practices they label as deviant and are actively figthing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. While I'm not for the notion of \u201call of the good things get credited to the Traditions while all of the bad things get blamed on the Technocracy\u201d, you do have a point about restoring documents about Hindu mythology not being the support of thing that the Order of Reason on the whole would be interested in doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:28:25-08:00","id":1439275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439270#post1439270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Akatsukileader and Dataweaver, thanks for that info.<br /> <br /> I know you didn't mean it that way. Nobody on this thread is arguing in favor of the justified imperialism trope. I was more pointing out an angle that isn't always obvious, because there's no real history of atrocities against fictional creatures, and lots of fiction depicts the like of werewolves and fae as irredeemably evil and deserving of death.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything about that story, sorry.<br /> <br /> There's no unblemished side in the WoD, true. However, there is a huge difference between what your leaders or ancestors used to do 500 years ago, and what the PCs themselves personally do or support in their <i>current</i> incarnation. The playable Werewolves and changelings in the WoD are not actually Automatically Evil like vampires, and their institutional goals aren't remotely close to the evil of Technocrats and Nephandi. Even during the Wyld West setting, there are individuals or whole factions of almost every Garou tribe who oppose imperialism. Compare [these modern concepts] :<br /> <br /> 1. I'm a werewolf. My ancestors committed genocide 10,000 years ago, and maybe also 400 years ago. I'm white so I benefit from White privilege. Or I'm black or Indigenous or Asian or etc. I'm not in favor of that imperialism shit and my sept han't done that shit for 400+ years. My oldest elders are in their 30s or 40s because our death rate is astronomical. We spend all our time fighting demons and Black-Spiral Dancers because they're constantly trying to kill us and our families, and we're on the defensive back foot. Our entire species is being hunted to extinction. My generation is the last.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm a Hermetic Disciple. My Master is a 500-year-old racist madman, and I mouth off behind his back and try to make my modern, not-a-dou***bag mark in the hopeless quagmire of the Mi'as. I have past life memories of being a colonizing jerkass, which is why I try not to be one in this lifetime. <s>When</s> If the old merlins finally kick the bucket, there are going to be some big changes around here. Er, I hope. I spend most of my time fighting the Technocracy because they're constantly trying to kill me and my friends, and we're on the defensive back foot.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm a wraith. Every single item I own is made out of eternally tortured souls. If I question this, <i>ever</i>, they'll take me to the soulforges next. If I run away, my soul will be shredded instantly by the Maelstrom. There is, literally, no escape from the Hierarchy anywhere. This makes it really hard to argue for hope as I spend every waking minute fighting against the spectre in my head. That's every minute because the dead don't sleep. (Disclaimer: I may or may not be comically uninformed about the details of Wraith.)<br /> <br /> 4. I'm a Technocrat. My job is to direct the robots that clean out the body parts after a torture session. I also help round up Sleeper dissidents for the torture chambers. My side job is mind control to put down pro-democracy and pro-environment activists so we can have the Sleeper military kill off most of them instead of wasting money torturing all of them. If I ever had any notion to question this, the mind-controlling leaders would have killed/reprocessed me last decade, so I'm one of the guys who's A-OK with all of this. We already rule the world, but everyone who disagrees with us needs to die. FOR SCIENCE! My leaders, who are all 300-year old white supremacists, deliberately gave all of Mercury to the Nephandi, just last year, because at least they're not dirty savages. I'm OK with this, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I came into the WoD from Werewolf and that's still the most familiar and favorite game to me, by far. The Werewolves aren't unblemished, and some of them are racists, especially against other shapeshifters. However, most of them no longer knowingly support imperialism, and focused on fighting the Wyrm. They are actively opposed to exploitative capitalism and all the neoimperialism it depends on. Also, within the context of that game, the Technocracy is objectively just as evil as Pentex, and are actively destroying the world. The Fera (who I like better much than Garou anyway) aren't guilty of genocide* and are mostly the people of color <i>opposing</i> neoimperialism. Even when playing Simba* or Red Talons, there are factions of each who oppose genocide.<br /> <br /> I've read a fair bit about Mage and Changeling online, but own only a couple books of each and haven't read the corebooks. I ... don't really want to read the Technocracy books. I don't know how much nauseating whitewashing I'd have to wade through to find anything worth reading, and would never play a Technocrat anyway.<br /> <br /> *except the Amandu'o, and I'm no fan of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, there's a big difference between lip-service to multiculturalism, and actually dismantling white supremacy and exploitative capitalism.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that, also, is one of the issues with playing Technocrats. Comparing them to playing Red Talons, Camarilla, Sabbat, Thallain, Black Spiral Dancers, infernalists, or even Nephandi is apples to oranges. Because there is not actually, among gamers or the wider human species, any genuine vocal contingent of people who eat babies, suck blood, want to wipe out the entire human species, sincerely worship Satan, or actually ally with genuine demons or world-destroying Elder Evils.<br /> <br /> But there are a huge, huge number of people - including a depressing proportion of gamers - who want to justify imperialism and capitalist exploitation and white supremacy and pretend these things are good and right in real life. People who freak out and blow a gasket if a Star Wars protagonist has dark skin. People who wouldn't <b>identify personally</b> with vampires or Red Talons or Nephandi, may actually identify with the Technocrats, and want to have an excuse to justfy their actions. Look at the lengths people in the US will go to, to justify genocide and the torture of small children. This is why the Technocracy needs to be treated a bit differently from the other evil factions. Because they represent a real evil that some gamers want to embrace for real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the institutions represented by the Technocracy are more plausible and insidious than the ludicrous extremes of the Nephandi or the BSD, but I'm going to have to disagree with you on the Werewolves. The Get in particular get under my skin, but the nation as a whole is coded with the kind of misanthropy, fear of &quot;miscegenation&quot;, bullheaded cultural chauvinism, unquestioning support for hierarchical hereditary power structures, religious fanaticism, dogmatism, abject refusal to consider the morality of their actions, maintaining breeding cults that you see in fascist populist movements <i>all the time</i>. Not to mention, they have committed genocides SINCE the Wyld West setting and, in universe, had significant chunks complicit in the Tazmanian genocide via the War of Shame. This in addition to their explicitly stated cultural belief in their status as a superior species (a thing the text never even tries to refute) and oh CHRIST the fucking ableism and social darwinism they espouse. This, in addition to the fact that they ALSO basically kill every other supernatural they encounter that isn't one of their pre-approved varieties of spirit. Not to mention also subscribing to the very same (or similar) Malthusian notions of population growth and how to &quot;solve it&quot;. <br /> <br /> I am willing to accept that the Technocracy is AS bad as the Garou, but I will not concede that they are worse, because I have seen firsthand where a martyr complex, a society that venerates violence to an almost fetishistic degree, an obsession with &quot;purity&quot;, and a doctrine of &quot;contempt for the weak&quot; get you. I have met people that personally identify with the Get, and they are not fun.<br /> <br /> The Union aren't the good guys. But I disagree that they are the single MOST viscerally distasteful of the playable factions in WoD.<br /> <br /> Upon consideration, they almost seem like two sides of the same terrible coin...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:43:11-08:00","id":1439276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439274#post1439274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. While I'm not for the notion of \u201call of the good things get credited to the Traditions while all of the bad things get blamed on the Technocracy\u201d, you do have a point about restoring documents about Hindu mythology not being the support of thing that the Order of Reason on the whole would be interested in doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah this could be an example of a positive the Hermetics could accomplish with their access to the levers of empire, given British Occult society\u2019s fascination with all things Indian (even as said access makes them complicit in many terrible things too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:45:14-08:00","id":1439277,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's a bunch of reasons I like some of the Fera more than most tribes of Garou, because they're better about most of those things. Except the religious fanaticism. I'm not sure what genocides you are talking about though, outside of the Australian Garou who are not under marching orders from other Garou anywhere else.<br /> <br /> That said, I have never personally gotten a real-world right-wing Christian-fundamentalist vibe from Werewolf. They just don't push that button for me. I can see how the game would disgust you if it reminded you of that, though. But if you don't think Werewolf ever discusses the morality of PC actions, in or out of character, you're badly mistaken. If you think that all or even the majority of Garou tribes or shapeshifters are in favor if killing whole human populations, you're badly mistaken. I can tell you have not read any of the same books I have, if you think that's more than a miniscule fringe faction, or that Werewolf fans are fans of genocide in real life (other than the one lunatic you met). I certainly hope you are not accusing me of promoting genocide, or whatever it is you suddenly <b>assume</b> I promote, just because I like Werewolf. I am getting the distinct impression you're accusing me of being a fascist all of the sudden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:47:34-08:00","id":1439278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439122#post1439122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of disagree with that notion.<br /> <br /> The Seers in Awakening are kind of detached of real world history by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they are.<br /> <br /> In Dark Eras 2, the &quot;Mysterious Frontiers&quot; Era, the Wild West chapter, AKA a time period that would be the same stretch of time as VM, specifically lists the Seers as being the ones that represent the worst of that era. That they do represent robber barons, corrupt politicians, and fire-and-brimstone preachers who are trying to incite violence against Native Americans. And in &quot;Devil and the Deep Blue Sea&quot;, the pirate era, they're listed as being the ones most vested in trying to curb Nameless orders that hide among pirates, siding with the 18th century European empires who are trying to halt piracy.<br /> <br /> So again: if this was an Awakening Dark Era that'd be one thing and you wouldn't be hearing any complaints from me about a faction of mages backing colonial empires. But they aren't, and it's dissonant with Ascension's themes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:51:09-08:00","id":1439279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439277#post1439277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's a bunch of reasons I like some of the Fera more than most tribes of Garou, because they're better about most of those things. Except the religious fanaticism. I'm not sure what genocides you are talking about though, outside of the Australian Garou who are not under marching orders from other Garou anywhere. And if you don't think Werewolf ever discusses the morality of PC actions, in or out of character, you're badly mistaken.<br /> <br /> That said, I have never personally gotten a real-world right-wing Christian-fundamentalist vibe from Werewolf. They just don't push that button for me. I can see how the game would disgust you if it reminded you of that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much right-wing Christian as appropriated Neo-Pagan beliefs barely concealing misanthropic cryptofascist fanaticism with a healthy dollop of eugenics. <br /> <br /> But then, my reading of the Technocracy was always more &quot;the Bavarian Illuminati with Terminators&quot;, with some pointed critiques at neoliberalism, rather than literal genocidal white supremacists. But likewise, your reading is valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T13:58:51-08:00","id":1439281,"title":"","content":"As I said, I really hope you are not accusing me of being a genocidal fascist maniac, but I feel like you may be. If you rely upon that lunatic you met for your understanding of what Werewolf depicts or promotes, instead of... reading a Werewolf book from after 1st Ed... then you'll be misinformed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439277#post1439277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think that all or even the majority of Garou tribes or shapeshifters are in favor if killing whole human populations, you're badly mistaken. I can tell you have not read any of the same books I have, if you think that's more than a miniscule fringe faction, or that Werewolf fans are fans of genocide in real life (other than the one lunatic you met).</div> </div> </div> </div>I once met a werewolf fan who was the most horrifically misogynistic man I have ever, ever met in real life <b>or</b> on the internet. His concept of what Werewolf should promote was... delusional, at best. Fortunately, I had actually read post-1E Werewolf books and joined a reasonable community on ShadownEssence, and wasn't desperate enough for a game to play with him, so I didn't mistake him for a representative of what all Werewolf fans are.<br /> <br /> The lunatic you met is about as representative of Werewolf fandom as the Asatru Futhark (the fictional ones in Mage) are of mainstream neo-Paganism. Which is to say they are a real but utterly despised minority. The rest of us hate them, ban them from our online games, and really wish that Changing Ways hadn't been editorily rewritten to please them. And like neo-Pagans, we really hate when we're accused of all being the same as those maniacs.<br /> <br /> <br /> And again... I personally am more a fan of some of the Fera, instead of the Garou, because I have some of the same complaints about some of Garou culture. And I also am aware that most people play them as deeply flawed antiheroes, doing bloody thingsagainst literal demons to oppose even more horrific things in a cosmic horror game, not anyone who's right about everything. PCs who kill innocent Pentex employees are supposed to get whammed with spiritual consequences equivalent to Jhor.<br /> <br /> As for overpopulation? I can guess that the Malthusian theory is an excuse for white supremacist genocide. But if you, or anyone, believes that overpopulation is inherently fictional, you really don't understand what a carrying capacity is or how close we are to a Permian-level extinction. And if you think that everyone who accepts that Earth has a carrying capacity must automatically favor genocide as the solution... you're delusional. Where I come from, there's this thing called voluntary birth control and voluntarily having only 2 children, and not forcing 11-year-old girls into child marriage to 70-year-old men. (Of course, I know that where I come from the child mortality rate is low enough to make this easy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:05:12-08:00","id":1439282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439278#post1439278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they are.<br /> <br /> In Dark Eras 2, the &quot;Mysterious Frontiers&quot; Era, the Wild West chapter, AKA a time period that would be the same stretch of time as VM, specifically lists the Seers as being the ones that represent the worst of that era. That they do represent robber barons, corrupt politicians, and fire-and-brimstone preachers who are trying to incite violence against Native Americans. And in &quot;Devil and the Deep Blue Sea&quot;, the pirate era, they're listed as being the ones most vested in trying to curb Nameless orders that hide among pirates, siding with the 18th century European empires who are trying to halt piracy.<br /> <br /> So again: if this was an Awakening Dark Era that'd be one thing and you wouldn't be hearing any complaints from me about a faction of mages backing colonial empires. But they aren't, and it's dissonant with Ascension's themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant as a whole, to be fair I never got to read Dark Eras 2.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not dissonant to Ascension's themes at all as it was mentioned in this very thread. As I said, the Tecnocracy is the faction that is ideologically and culturally tied to what it's being presented here. And Ascension is all about ideology, belief and willpower changing the world, both for good or bad. It's very thematically relevant to the themes of the game even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:11:08-08:00","id":1439283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439277#post1439277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's a bunch of reasons I like some of the Fera more than most tribes of Garou, because they're better about most of those things. Except the religious fanaticism. I'm not sure what genocides you are talking about though, outside of the Australian Garou who are not under marching orders from other Garou anywhere else.<br /> <br /> That said, I have never personally gotten a real-world right-wing Christian-fundamentalist vibe from Werewolf. They just don't push that button for me. I can see how the game would disgust you if it reminded you of that, though. But if you don't think Werewolf ever discusses the morality of PC actions, in or out of character, you're badly mistaken. If you think that all or even the majority of Garou tribes or shapeshifters are in favor if killing whole human populations, you're badly mistaken. I can tell you have not read any of the same books I have, if you think that's more than a miniscule fringe faction, or that Werewolf fans are fans of genocide in real life (other than the one lunatic you met). I certainly hope you are not accusing me of promoting genocide, or whatever it is you suddenly <b>assume</b> I promote, just because I like Werewolf. I am getting the distinct impression you're accusing me of being a fascist all of the sudden.<br /> <br /> And if you think that (non-Malthusian) overpopulation is fictional, you don't understand what environmental destruction is or how close we are to a Permian-level extinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I'm not calling you a fascist. I get the parts of the game that are appealing and, for the record, I also like a lot of the Fera (shoutout to the Mok\u00f2le). And I'm aware that overpopulation is a problem, but it's a problem caused by unsustainable production models and artificial scarcity, not because humans just aren't dying fast enough.<br /> <br /> The positions I see fetishized are those of the &quot;strong man of superior breeding, striking down the decadence of modernity and the weakness it enables&quot;. Like, if you want to be ecoterrorists and blow up factory farms, that's one thing. But when you start getting into shit like &quot;medical science is spurning Gaia by allowing the unfit to reproduce&quot; and &quot;things were a lot better when we, the divinely ordained elite, were allowed to engage in routine population culls&quot;, both sentiments expressed by <i>ostensibly sympathetic and reasonable characters in universe</i>, the game has lost me. <br /> <br /> But I suppose I have veered us wildly off-course...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-11-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:11:35-08:00","id":1439285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439278#post1439278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they are.<br /> <br /> In Dark Eras 2, the &quot;Mysterious Frontiers&quot; Era, the Wild West chapter, AKA a time period that would be the same stretch of time as VM, specifically lists the Seers as being the ones that represent the worst of that era. That they do represent robber barons, corrupt politicians, and fire-and-brimstone preachers who are trying to incite violence against Native Americans. And in &quot;Devil and the Deep Blue Sea&quot;, the pirate era, they're listed as being the ones most vested in trying to curb Nameless orders that hide among pirates, siding with the 18th century European empires who are trying to halt piracy.<br /> <br /> So again: if this was an Awakening Dark Era that'd be one thing and you wouldn't be hearing any complaints from me about a faction of mages backing colonial empires. But they aren't, and it's dissonant with Ascension's themes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Seers represent a different brand of realistic evil than the Union. The Union BELIEVE. Their imperialism is driven by real faith in White Man's Burden (rephrased less racially in Modern Nights, but point still stands). They explore how people justify these things to themselves, and what prioritizing &quot;peace&quot; over &quot;justice&quot; can do, and the blindness of cultural homogenuity.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Seers are more consciously selfish, but no less realistic, in that their motives are pure self interest. If Mage factions in Awakening are divided by &quot;what is magic for&quot; rather than Ascension's &quot;how does magic work&quot;, the Seers are the Mages who checked the &quot;absolutely comfort, power, wealth, luxury&quot; box, and that comes with required complicity in upholding the pyramid that lets them sit at the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:11:54-08:00","id":1439286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439282#post1439282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant as a whole, to be fair I never got to read Dark Eras 2.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not dissonant to Ascension's themes at all as it was mentioned in this very thread. As I said, the Tecnocracy is the faction that is ideologically and culturally tied to what it's being presented here. And Ascension is all about ideology, belief and willpower changing the world, both for good or bad. It's very thematically relevant to the themes of the game even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. My main contention is that the current presentation smacks of the 1e core book's monolithic Technocracy, something that Brucato set to work getting away from the moment he took over the line. I can get not wanting to make the mistake of coming across as justifying imperialism or colonialism; but you don't want to overcorrect, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:25:03-08:00","id":1439288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439283#post1439283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The positions I see fetishized are those of the &quot;strong man of superior breeding, striking down the decadence of modernity and the weakness it enables&quot;. Like, if you want to be ecoterrorists and blow up factory farms, that's one thing. But when you start getting into shit like &quot;medical science is spurning Gaia by allowing the unfit to reproduce&quot; and &quot;things were a lot better when we, the divinely ordained elite, were allowed to engage in routine population culls&quot;, both sentiments expressed by <i>ostensibly sympathetic and reasonable characters in universe</i>, the game has lost me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be reading 1st Edition. All the tribebooks and the corebook I have bought and read treat the Impergium as an atrocity, and idiotic mistake of almost cosmic scale, and I've never read the book that opposes letting the &quot;unfit&quot; reproduce. And (other than the wildly racist name I won't repeat) the children of Garou-Garou matings are a parody calling out ableism as garbage, not promoting ableism.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy: like the Garou Nation, and unlike the Nephandi or Black Spiral Dancers, the Technocrats can have dissidents in their ranks. This is a lot easier, as Dataweaver says, when they don't have literal mind-control.<br /> <br /> That said... the mind control thing confuses me. If your PC has no free will, why play them? If they do have free will, the mind-control isn't an excuse, is it? Non-psychic coercion is a (dark) vehicle for character conflict. Mind control is just deprotagonizing. Playing a Conditioned Technocrat sounds about as fun as playing a fomor in Werewolf, or an Akuma in Exalted. You're a meat-puppet for an evil empire. Yay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  spellilng. this website hates my keyboard 03-11-2021, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:35:55-08:00","id":1439289,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy has never had literal mind control. At most, they've had psychological conditioning, which lets you play games involving psychological horror and Big Brother style messing with your head. And it's unreliable. <br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that the Void Engineers regularly break the Conditioning, in part because being Conditioned in the Umbra can be fatal. <br /> <br /> But that's the modern Technocracy. The Victorian Technocracy predates that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:45:52-08:00","id":1439291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439288#post1439288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may be reading 1st Edition. All the tribebooks and the corebook I have bought and read treat the Impergium as an atrocity, and idiotic mistake of almost cosmic scale, and I've never read the book that opposes letting the &amp;quot;unfit&amp;quot; reproduce. And (other than the wildly racist name I won't repeat) the children of Garou-Garou matings are a parody calling out ableism as garbage, not promoting ableism.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy: like the Garou Nation, and unlike the Nephandi or Black Spiral Dancers, the Technocrats can have dissidents in their ranks. This is a lot easier, as Dataweaver says, when they don't have literal mind-control.<br /> <br /> That said... the mind control thinkf confuses me. If your PC has no free will, why play them? If they do have free will, the mind-control isn't an excuse, is it? Non-psychic coercion is a (dark) vehicle for character conflict. Mind control is just deprotagonizing. Playing a Conditioned Technocrat sounds about as fun as playing a fomor in Werewolf, or an Akuma in Exalted. You're a meat-puppet for an evil empire. Yay?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most blatant example is Book of the Weaver (a 2e book), but it can be generally seen in the whole &quot;humans were meant to be prey&quot; attitude that comes up all the time. Not to mention the Revised Get book is all like &quot;we're not ableist or supremacist, we're just a meritocracy&quot; bullshit. Also, it's in the fucking Litany: Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness. I just can't fully sympathize with a faction where &quot;Pure Breed&quot; is a literal stat.<br /> <br /> It's less of a meat puppet situation and more of an aggressive deluge of supernaturally enhanced propaganda. And for what it's worth, the Void Engineers (who are the most player-friendly of the modern Conventions anyway) explicitly don't put up with that shit and deprogram all of their personnel.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, lest I be judged entirely anti-Garou, I am <i>always</i> down to play as a Bone Gnawer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:52:24-08:00","id":1439295,"title":"","content":"Might I recommend moving this to the Werewolf forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:56:37-08:00","id":1439296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439295#post1439295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I recommend moving this to the Werewolf forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, I hadn't meant for it to go in this long. I'll drop it. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T14:57:46-08:00","id":1439297,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to drop or move it if I'm not called upon to defend my personal tastes and personal morality every other post. Nobody deserves to have this thread turn into a jury about their worth as a human being.<br /> <br /> We've already had people feel like they have to defend themselves against accusations of promoting imperialism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T15:01:22-08:00","id":1439298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439297#post1439297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to drop or move it if I'm not called upon to depend my personal tastes and personal morality every other post.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really wasn't meant as a personal attack, I swear. I think your points are valid and there's a lot in the game to like. I've played and enjoyed it before, even if there are parts I find distasteful, I don't automatically assume that those reflect on its players. That would be wildly hypocritical of me. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I've been insensitive or ignorant on the subject. I won't say any more about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T15:04:01-08:00","id":1439299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439295#post1439295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I recommend moving this to the Werewolf forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may actually bring this around, there is a werewolf story that's relevent to MAGE: THE ASCENSION.<br /> <br /> We're talking essentially for at least a SMALL chunk of the fanbase being the problem at this point rather than talking about the material itself. One of the things that has been a problem for quite a number of World of Darkness gamelines. Does anyone else remember Jason Carl's invocation of &quot;NAZI PUNKS FUCK OFF&quot; (a.k.a Dead Kennedys).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17565898/vampire-the-masquerade-white-wolf-neo-nazi-accusations\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17...zi-accusations</a><br /> <br /> This was for 5th Edition vampire.<br /> <br /> But there was actually a SIMILAR thing that happened in 2nd Edition to Revised for Werewolf that is relevant to Mage: The Ascension. Basically, Ethan Skemp had to deal with the fact that Werewolf had a white supremacy problem. NOT THE BOOKS THEMSELVES but the fact there was a not insignificant number of white supremacists who used LARPs and in-game justifications to &quot;act in character&quot; as a racist asshole.<br /> <br /> I have no difficulty believing this because Kindred of the East almost destroyed by local gaming community as a bunch of assholes harassed our Asina members by saying they should be playing Kueijin and Cainites were for &quot;white people.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, Ethan Skemp's decision was to utterly massacre the entire <i>Swords of Heimdall</i> Camp of the Garou and basically say that white supremacy was not tolerated among the Get. It struck some as heavy handed since, really, most of us knew the SoH were meant to be baddies but it was a direct statement on the issue. So the question with the Technocracy is part of a larger cultural issue (see, I said I would get back to this):<br /> <br /> &quot;At what point is including the nastiness of RL fascism, racism, imperialism, and so on a good thing as game material?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because I love steampunk but whenever I play steampunk, I'm usually playing:<br /> <br /> * An Irish socialist and two-fisted pulp hero<br /> * A mixed race mechanic female who can't be accepted despite being a genius.<br /> * An anti-imperialist mad scientist<br /> * A black cowboy<br /> <br /> Ie. people who love fighting the British Empire as a general rule even if they do occasionally also fight evil cults or mad scientists who have a decent motive. I remember doing an adaptation of the TEMPLE OF DOOM for a Chronicle that had the twist at the end that they were actually a bunch of con men who were invoking the Thugee legend to distract the British government while they looted the place. They believed the racism of the British would result in them cracking down on the locals rather than actually investigating a bunch of thieves as well as smugglers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T15:19:37-08:00","id":1439304,"title":"","content":"Was eradicating the House of Helekar a similar meta-choice? I have no trouble believing that some fans somewhere decided to creatively misinterpret the Euthanatoi (who I like, btw) into an excuse for playing Nephandi-lite.<br /> <br /> But the Euthanatoi - like the Garou - are an exploration of the kind of morality that can be sympathetic and even acceptable in a fictional universe where your character has objective proof of their beliefs, but still absolutely 100% wrong in real life. Sort of like the nature of reality in Mage and the existence of spirits and supernaturals puts a very different spin on what counts as acceptable, non-fringe science. In real life, anyone advocating theories out of <i>Paradigma</i> is a crackpot or a quack. In game, Etherites are the champions of honest science.<br /> <br /> But it can be difficult to write this in a way that's proof against creative misinterpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T15:29:34-08:00","id":1439307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439304#post1439304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was eradicating the House of Helekar a similar meta-choice? I have no trouble believing that some fans somewhere decided to creatively misinterpret the Euthanatoi (who I like, btw) into an excuse for playing Nephandi-lite.<br /> <br /> But the Euthanatoi - like the Garou - are an exploration of the kind of morality that can be sympathetic and even acceptable in a fictional universe where your character has objective proof of their beliefs, but still absolutely 100% wrong in real life. Sort of like the nature of reality in Mage and the existence of spirits and supernaturals puts a very different spin on what counts as acceptable, non-fringe science. In real life, anyone advocating theories out of <i>Paradigma</i> is a crackpot or a quack. In game, Etherites are the champions of honest science.<br /> <br /> But it can be difficult to write this in a way that's proof against creative misinterpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if that was at least a consideration with the Euthanatos Revised.<br /> <br /> I always felt the Etherites' biggest problem is that they're NOT supposed to be Marauders but the books always portray them as Doc Brown at their best and Rick at the worst. I feel like most Sons of Ether should be trying to work within the scientific pattern for the most part and push the consensus well rather than completely violating it out of hand. Even if you don't believe that and think that Sons of Ether should go, &quot;Well magic is real and my invention works with magic so fuck Paradox&quot; there should at least be a CAMP of Conventional Scientists trying to show that there's no reason not to have a solar battery that works at 99% with present-day science.<br /> <br /> Because I feel a lot is lost if the Technocracy is happy with all science being advanced. They're basically based on the conspiracy theory the oil companies are suppressing the electic car.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That turned out to be true except it was all renewable energy research period.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Sennex and Mercy was 2nd Edition fiction and maybe first edition. A 19th century Euthanatos assassin, Mercy, is killing Order of Reason members with her partner before they fall in love, only to find out that said partner is actually a Nephandus not a Euthanatos. She agrees to go through the Cauls with him and becomes a Nephandus. Then she allows herself to be killed while trying to kill her old master, seeing how warped her avatar has become.<br /> <br /> Sennex has begun teaching her reincarnation in the Modern Day, which pisses off all sorts of Traditionalists who believe she needs to be Gilguled. All indications are Amanda is a perfectly normal mage, though. Which has troubling implications to both the Traditions AND Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T15:35:07-08:00","id":1439308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439307#post1439307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I feel a lot is lost if the Technocracy is happy with all science being advanced. They're basically based on the conspiracy theory the oil companies are suppressing the electic car.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That turned out to be true except it was all renewable energy research period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. And it's still true. Clean energy is clearly not on the Time Table... <b>ever</b>. Not even after <s>Hell</s> the Cauls freeze over.<br /> <br /> I'm no Mage expert but maybe the Etherites are portrayed that way because the zeitgeist today thinks mad scientists are funny instead of terrifying. The pop-culture example is Rick or Girl Genius, not the Tuskegee Syphilis Experiment. Well, in the white zeitgeist anyway.<br /> <br /> Playing a Quiet-infected maniac with questionable appliances should be available... the same way you can play a likeable but batshit insane wizard who wanders around naked and accidentally farts explosions. Or look up to Porthos as a sort-of role model. But yeah, it shouldn't be the whole Tradition or even the majority.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Rick could be an actual dimension-hopping Etherite adventurer, and even be looked up to the way Porthos is by some Hermetics: With a ten-foot pole and a healthy appreciation of how insane he is, and nobody really wants to grow up to be him. Maybe he'd fit in as the kind of Victorian Etherite adventurer Dataweaver (and others) were suggesting be supported in VAM. Disclaimer, I have only watched 1 episode of Rick &amp; Morty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T16:24:43-08:00","id":1439315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439299#post1439299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;At what point is including the nastiness of RL fascism, racism, imperialism, and so on a good thing as game material?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that's an interesting point<br /> <br /> Mage has often &quot;solved&quot; this by pushing it under the Technocracy's metal rug. But this ended causing more problems than it solved<br /> <br /> A very cringe case it's Witch Hunts and the Inquisition. It's fascinating how in fiction these can be really good things, because it just happens that witches DO exist.<br /> But Mage tried to criticize this - good for Mage - and decouple it from the main (and for a long time only) playable christian theurgist faction: Celesital Chorus - good for Mage?.<br /> <br /> Note how the Chorus never, ever, it's to blame about any kind of fundamentalism. It's the fault of the Gabrielites (OoR)...how convinient Technocracy tolerates mystical christians just in the era when christians did some really, really, bad things.<br /> <br /> But then, there's no other choice because &quot;realistic&quot; christian Awakened would hardly side with pagans and heretics - and that would *destroy* the premises of them as a Tradition.<br /> <br /> Which makes many players rigthfully ask: With Belief/Paradigm working as it does, where are the fundamentalist christian mages?<br /> <br /> Some questions are better left unanswered... <hr /><br /> But back to the Technocracy, this sweeping of real world issues under Technocracy's rug caused the problem that when we wanted to have a &quot;Star Trek hard science good&quot; group of mages - we had the Technocracy, and they were full of shit<br /> <br /> I do fear that a small minority of the people who are Pro-Technocracy are so because they're facists. Most just like a harder version of science than what the Etherites usually are depicted practicing.<br /> <br /> But, frankly, I do think the Imperialist institutions were every bit as bad as Nazism was, and if we can't speak about this w/o the risk of some crazy people trying to make such an institution good in spite of the very book saying OOC that they're not, in any way or fashion, anything but the bad guys...I do think it could be better to say that the OoR just isn't playable.<br /> <br /> I don't have any problem with playing with the bad guys (or with trying to rebel against the system from within as an Idealist). I just think that, if we want them to be playable (and I do), there's not an ounce of land that we can concede. Not a milimeter. Not an ounce of nuance.<br /> <br /> It's Bad and they're Bad for doing it - period- And I do think it's a good thing fans of the OoR are angry at this, because that means it's really, really, hard not to see it.<br /> <br /> Even then, I would respect the idea of banning them as purely Antagonists on the grounds of Imperialism. I wouldn't like it, and I don't think it should be necessary, but I would understand it, if that was Brucato's choice. I think that what they did (an OOC declaration of intentions) it's the next best thing, in that sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T16:33:58-08:00","id":1439316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439286#post1439286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. My main contention is that the current presentation smacks of the 1e core book's monolithic Technocracy, something that Brucato set to work getting away from the moment he took over the line. I can get not wanting to make the mistake of coming across as justifying imperialism or colonialism; but you don't want to overcorrect, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nowhere near to the 1e Technocracy. That Union was moustache twirling evil + the Borg, with the Men in Black being constructs they send to kill everyone against them. This is a very real historical evil that has been associated with the Union since Guide of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T16:47:17-08:00","id":1439318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439267#post1439267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - erased - there's no reason to go there. I'm sorry<br /> <br /> I'm just going to say: Do you know how many apologists of the worst things of humanity go there?<br /> <br /> Even in my own country. Everywhere really. Not denying the bad because it's undeniable, but insisting on focusing also on the good<br /> <br /> You really don't want to go there. I certainly don't</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I don't think that's what the text of VAM, or myself and Data are saying. We're not saying ignore the bad, focus on the good. We're saying that both need to be recognized and understood.<br /> <br /> To focus solely on the good or bad is wrong because it will paint a biased picture of things.<br /> <br /> If we met one of our ancestors from the Victorian Era, we would be horrified by at least some of their beliefs and attitudes. Does that automatically make them bad people? No, it makes them just people from another time, just as complicated and flawed as us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439270#post1439270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I'm a Technocrat. My job is to direct the robots that clean out the body parts after a torture session. I also help round up Sleeper dissidents for the torture chambers. My side job is mind control to put down pro-democracy and pro-environment activists so we can have the Sleeper military kill off most of them instead of wasting money torturing all of them. If I ever had any notion to question this, the mind-controlling leaders would have killed/reprocessed me last decade, so I'm one of the guys who's A-OK with all of this. We already rule the world, but everyone who disagrees with us needs to die. FOR SCIENCE! My leaders, who are all 300-year old white supremacists, deliberately gave all of Mercury to the Nephandi, just last year, because at least they're not dirty savages. I'm OK with this, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I came into the WoD from Werewolf and that's still the most familiar and favorite game to me, by far. The Werewolves aren't unblemished, and some of them are racists, especially against other shapeshifters. However, most of them no longer knowingly support imperialism, and focused on fighting the Wyrm. They are actively opposed to exploitative capitalism and all the neoimperialism it depends on. Also, within the context of that game, the Technocracy is objectively just as evil as Pentex, and are actively destroying the world. The Fera (who I like better much than Garou anyway) aren't guilty of genocide* and are mostly the people of color <i>opposing</i> neoimperialism. Even when playing Simba* or Red Talons, there are factions of each who oppose genocide.<br /> <br /> I've read a fair bit about Mage and Changeling online, but own only a couple books of each and haven't read the corebooks. I ... don't really want to read the Technocracy books. I don't know how much nauseating whitewashing I'd have to wade through to find anything worth reading, and would never play a Technocrat anyway.<br /> <br /> *except the Amandu'o, and I'm no fan of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, there's a big difference between lip-service to multiculturalism, and actually dismantling white supremacy and exploitative capitalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much more complicated than you think it is and it's one of those things that you don't see from an outside perspective.<br /> <br /> The Union actually is fighting climate change and recognized it as an unexpected counter-reaction to their actions towards the Consensus. The Syndicate's old ties to Pentex have been long since severed and would be recognized as Nephandi-taint by most Technocracts nowadays.<br /> <br /> The issue with them and the Garou is born of out ignorance on both sides and that most of the time the Technocracy is responding to the violent, destructive actions of the Garou. The Technocracy has no concept of the Wyrm and view it's minions as either more violent shapeshifters or humans infected with extra-demenisional entities. All the Technocrats see is bunch of violent werewolves destroying factories and resource extraction sites and killing the people that work there because they're throwbacks to a more primitive age when supernaturals like them dominated Humanity. While most Garou would see the Technocrats as nothing more than slaves of the Weaver/Wyrm and therefore part of the enemy. Even those that would be less hostile to them, like Void Engineers who even in the early days of MtAs were seen as good guys, as the Star Trek Convention.<br /> <br /> Then there's the out-of-universe divides between game lines which muddy the whole situation.<br /> <br /> As for the Union and democracy, yeah they are pretty anti-democracy (though how anti-democracy they are can very between Conventions, groups and individuals) but at the same time they look at the sheer chaotic stupidity of the Masses and can't help but utterly frustrated by it.<br /> <br /> And that's really a big point of the Modern Technocracy. That in what should be their time, their Golden Age where they lead the Masses into their Enlightened Future and instead they're being forced more and more to putting out all the fires the Sleepers keep causing in their willfull stupidity.<br /> <br /> Far too many people will vote for a populous demigogue that will say anything to get elected. Political tribalism that drags governments to a halt. Politicians that slash spending on education and science again and again, helping to keep their voters ignorant and stupid. The internet being used to spread stupidity and quack science.<br /> <br /> All of this runs counter to what the Technocracy wants and it frustrates them to no end, whether it be those with sinister intentions or those still pursue the noble ideals they were founded upon.<br /> <br /> It's not hard to see why the Technocrats have only become more frustrated by the Masses and that democracy is not the way to go. Hell, I've lost a lot of faith in people and democracy over the last few years thanks to Trump and his ilk. I can only imagine how much worse it would be in a world that's designed to be ours but worse and filled with Supernatural things.<br /> <br /> While this does not excuse the worst the Union has and is doing, I do understand why they do such things or feel that they are necessary.<br /> <br /> As for their leadership, like with everyone else in the MtAs world, the events of the Rev Ed (at least if you're using the Metaplot as their recent books handle it) has shaken things up. Much of their old leadership is MIA, forcing the younger mid-level leadership that were still on Earth to take charge of the Union. There are those Utopian idealists that are striving to pull the Technocracy back to it's noble origins, not erase the sins of the past but to acknowledge and prevent them from happening again. Just as there are despotic control freaks that want to keep the status quo going because it suits them.<br /> <br /> As the Technocracy Reload said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the Technocratic Utopia: A monster-free bastion of human innovation, achieved through the benevolent management of an Enlightened elite.<br /> <br /> The trouble with Utopias is that they always look better in rarefied theory than they do in bloody practice. And the Technocratic Utopia, regardless of its ideals, is drenched in blood and tyranny.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, if you were to turn those mirrorshades around and look <i>into </i>them instead of <i>through </i>them, you might see the monster looking back at you.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when the hard work begins: The work of storming your own Utopia to salvage your ideals from the mess they have become.<br /> <br /> Welcome, then, to the Technocratic Union at the threshold of the third decade of this 21st century. Neither the shiny monster nor the gleaming knight, but the flawed machine crafted by gifted hands and all-too-human souls of people tasked with illuminating a World of Darkness by all available means.<br /> <br /> Welcome to a disunified Union where the future follows unpredictable paths that could lead to majesty or ruin. </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is not the Nephandi or Pentex or the BSD. Certainly they have their evil people and they have fallen far from what they once were. But they are not irredeemably evil nor beyond hope. That is what sets the Technocracy apart from other Antagonist factions in the WoD.<br /> <br /> But I think that's about all I have left to say on the morality of the Order and the Union.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439299#post1439299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I may actually bring this around, there is a werewolf story that's relevent to MAGE: THE ASCENSION.<br /> <br /> We're talking essentially for at least a SMALL chunk of the fanbase being the problem at this point rather than talking about the material itself. One of the things that has been a problem for quite a number of World of Darkness gamelines. Does anyone else remember Jason Carl's invocation of &quot;NAZI PUNKS FUCK OFF&quot; (a.k.a Dead Kennedys).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17565898/vampire-the-masquerade-white-wolf-neo-nazi-accusations\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.polygonimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/11686761/Screenshot_2018_07_13_12.10.43.png?w=1600&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17565898/vampire-the-masquerade-white-wolf-neo-nazi-accusations\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade maker responds to accusations it caters to neo-Nazi groups </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17565898/vampire-the-masquerade-white-wolf-neo-nazi-accusations\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.polygon.com/2018/7/13/17565898/vampire-the-masquerade-white-wolf-neo-nazi-accusations </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> &ldquo;Everybody is welcome. ... Unless you are a Nazi.&rdquo; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This was for 5th Edition vampire.<br /> <br /> But there was actually a SIMILAR thing that happened in 2nd Edition to Revised for Werewolf that is relevant to Mage: The Ascension. Basically, Ethan Skemp had to deal with the fact that Werewolf had a white supremacy problem. NOT THE BOOKS THEMSELVES but the fact there was a not insignificant number of white supremacists who used LARPs and in-game justifications to &quot;act in character&quot; as a racist asshole.<br /> <br /> I have no difficulty believing this because Kindred of the East almost destroyed by local gaming community as a bunch of assholes harassed our Asina members by saying they should be playing Kueijin and Cainites were for &quot;white people.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, Ethan Skemp's decision was to utterly massacre the entire <i>Swords of Heimdall</i> Camp of the Garou and basically say that white supremacy was not tolerated among the Get. It struck some as heavy handed since, really, most of us knew the SoH were meant to be baddies but it was a direct statement on the issue.<br /> So the question with the Technocracy is part of a larger cultural issue (see, I said I would get back to this):<br /> <br /> &quot;At what point is including the nastiness of RL fascism, racism, imperialism, and so on a good thing as game material?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because I love steampunk but whenever I play steampunk, I'm usually playing:<br /> <br /> * An Irish socialist and two-fisted pulp hero<br /> * A mixed race mechanic female who can't be accepted despite being a genius.<br /> * An anti-imperialist mad scientist<br /> * A black cowboy<br /> <br /> Ie. people who love fighting the British Empire as a general rule even if they do occasionally also fight evil cults or mad scientists who have a decent motive. I remember doing an adaptation of the TEMPLE OF DOOM for a Chronicle that had the twist at the end that they were actually a bunch of con men who were invoking the Thugee legend to distract the British government while they looted the place. They believed the racism of the British would result in them cracking down on the locals rather than actually investigating a bunch of thieves as well as smugglers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the Neo Nazi/Fascist problem is one that most fandoms have period. Pick a fandom and odds are there is a section of the fans that have co-opted it for their own. It's something creators and the rest of us fans have to deal with and warn new fans about so they don't fall down that awful rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> As for why including the real world nastiness of the Victorian Age in VAM because it's the WoD, our world but with supernatural things in the shadows. You can't really avoid it here like you could with a fictional Victorian setting.<br /> <br /> And also likely to try to avoid feeding the aforementioned Fascists and their ideology by making it clear that there were a lot of bad things going on during the Victorian Age.<br /> <br /> There also one other important thing to add, VAM takes the stance that the future doesn't have to be set in stone. If you want to the Victorian Luminaries back to their noble origins, you can. Obviously you can't undo the atrocities that have already happened but you can prevent ones in the future and shape the world into something different, possibly better even. One of the sidebars in the Order chapters talks about different outcomes of the Victorian Reforms and the most successful version has the future SoE and VA stay with the Order, leading to Ether becoming accepted by the Masses and thanks to the technology born of that, World War I doesn't happen. Which in turn means that World War II and all the violence and death caused by those wars don't happen.<br /> <br /> There nothing stopping you from having in your chronicles events leading to the Dalou\u2019laoshi or the Jidai (or even both of them together) sitting down with the Order and joining early them early in this era as equals. As a result their nations get time and support in modernizing. Those Luminaries already sympathetic to foreign Technomancers hold them up as examples for how they should treat other Technomancer Crafts. In time, said Crafts start joining, changing the demographics and ideology of the Order. Their racism starts to fade and they in turn start pushing the Masses away from those horrible ideas.<br /> <br /> And from there? Well that's up to you and your table.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T16:54:32-08:00","id":1439320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439315#post1439315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note how the Chorus never, ever, it's to blame about any kind of fundamentalism. It's the fault of the Gabrielites (OoR)...how convinient Technocracy tolerates mystical christians just in the era when christians did some really, really, bad things.<br /> <br /> But then, there's no other choice because &quot;realistic&quot; christian Awakened would hardly side with pagans and heretics - and that would *destroy* the premises of them as a Tradition.<br /> <br /> Which makes many players rigthfully ask: With Belief/Paradigm working as it does, where are the fundamentalist christian mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm a religious Christian and married to a witch. The weird thing about the Chorus is that it isn't a Christian sect, it's a pantheistic multi-religious sect that basically functions as a BIG TENT PARTY for all religious people. So there's no problem with the Choirsters NEVER being fundamentalists because their ideology is fundamentally pretty close to Hinduism.<br /> <br /> &quot;All gods are just parts of the bigger God.&quot;<br /> <br /> But that means that if you ever DO want a witch hunting psychopathic fundamentalist, you need to look elsewhere. It's why I actually liked the Knights Templar as their own separate Craft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\">AkatsukiLeader13</a>[/B]]<br /> And that's really a big point of the Modern Technocracy. That in what should be their time, their Golden Age where they lead the Masses into their Enlightened Future and instead they're being forced more and more to putting out all the fires the Sleepers keep causing in their willfull stupidity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure that was a wise artistic decision.<br /> <br /> &quot;The group involved in genocide of supernaturals, brainwashing, and the Military Industrial Complex is TOTALLY innocent of all the crap the Far Right is doing. They are against climate change!&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Technocracy would never be science deniars either.<br /> <br /> Tough call.<br /> <br /> Maybe we should officially make THREAT NULL into the EVIL Technocracy and a pseudo-Seers of the Throne in-universe when there's a M5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T17:24:26-08:00","id":1439322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439320#post1439320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'm a religious Christian and married to a witch. The weird thing about the Chorus is that it isn't a Christian sect, it's a pantheistic multi-religious sect that basically functions as a BIG TENT PARTY for all religious people. So there's no problem with the Choirsters NEVER being fundamentalists because their ideology is fundamentally pretty close to Hinduism.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;All gods are just parts of the bigger God.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But that means that if you ever DO want a witch hunting psychopathic fundamentalist, you need to look elsewhere. It's why I actually liked the Knights Templar as their own separate Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Victorian Mage text does not agree with you though. The Septarians are hunting heretics and pushing aggressive imperial missionary work.<br /> <br /> That being so contrary to the paradigm and organizing philosophy of the Chorus is why I suggest it may be necessary to establish the collapse of the Gabrielites is in play in reshaping the Chorus in this era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T17:35:16-08:00","id":1439323,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T17:47:02-08:00","id":1439326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439320#post1439320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not sure that was a wise artistic decision.<br /> <br /> &quot;The group involved in genocide of supernaturals, brainwashing, and the Military Industrial Complex is TOTALLY innocent of all the crap the Far Right is doing. They are against climate change!&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Technocracy would never be science deniars either.<br /> <br /> Tough call.<br /> <br /> Maybe we should officially make THREAT NULL into the EVIL Technocracy and a pseudo-Seers of the Throne in-universe when there's a M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well with Climate Change it's a simple thing, the Sleepers are a long away from moving beyond Earth. And that's without factoring in how the Avatar Storm has made a mess of things. So damage to Earth is a bad thing. Damage to Earth that makes the world less habitable for people is worse. Even the darkest iterations of the Technocracy would recognize that.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I think even the most space-obsessed Void Engineers would hate the idea of Earth becoming a lifeless rock even if they could get all of Humanity off it.<br /> <br /> As for Threat Null, that's hard thing given that they've become Spirits and utterly divorced from any shreds of Humanity. They're eldritch horrors, not twisted evil people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T17:49:08-08:00","id":1439327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439326#post1439326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Threat Null, that's hard thing given that they've become Spirits and utterly divorced from any shreds of Humanity. They're eldritch horrors, not twisted evil people.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the natural endpoint of Technocratic philosophy. The scary thing about Threat Null is they are not corrupted technocrats: They are their perfection.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I kind of like that sort of twist.<br /> <br /> Judge Dredd did several variants on it that the Judge system is WORSE than regular fascism. Not because it falls prey to corruption anymore but that its brainwashed leadership generally DOES follow its philosophy and spiirt.<br /> <br /> And that is what's rotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T18:21:11-08:00","id":1439330,"title":"","content":"I wanna be clear that I in no way have any dislike towards Technocracy players. Or Vampire or Hunter players. I simply can't see the appeal of playing the Technocrats (or Vampire, Hunter, Wraith, Promethean, Kult, etc.) because it's too dark for me. Like, I need kitten-video-brain-bleach after reading too much about those games. That's just me.<br /> <br /> I am confused how the guys who rule the world have supported clean energy all this time and not made one micron of actual difference with any Sleeper government? Because if any environmentalism in the Union predates the Avatar Storm.... that just makes no sense to me. Doesn't the Syndicate have the magic to create unlimited relative wealth for themselves, even more than Pentex? Don't they basically own all the Sleeper governments? Aren't the Progenitors the inventors and purveyors of all things pesticide? Despite having the magic to rewrite reality so pesticides aren't even necessary? Despite real-world science now having proven they were never necessary*? And yet... the WOD is still even worse environmentally than real life. Like, lots worse. Like, Deep Horizon wasn't a unique or even unusual spill. Likewise... genuine religious freedom and tolerance isn't doing great in real life or the WOD, so if the Technocrats aren't really all about forced conversion... what have they been up to this whole time? Maybe I'm overestimating how powerful they are. Are the Ventrue actually the real rulers of the WOD?<br /> <br /> Even back in the Victorian Age, solar energy was invented in the same year as the internal combustion engine. In real life, I think around 1901. Pentex didn't exist until 1915. So if the Technocrats weren't utterly enamored with coal and oil, despite the visually and odorously obvious problems, why didn't they ever promote solar panels or electric busses in their Time Table? They ought to at least have just as much influence as Pentex and the Camarilla. If they have any environmental interest, they ought to have <i>something</i> to show for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Not to mention generations of organic regenerative agriculture practiced by some Native Americans before they were conquered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T18:24:39-08:00","id":1439333,"title":"","content":"It strikes me also that the Chorus trying to heal of the rift of the Messianic Voice by welcoming Gabrielites fleeing the knives of the Ksirafai into their ranks, but that in turn reshaping them into hegemonic enforcers of (small-o) orthodoxy that push the non-Christians and many heterodox Christians from their ranks, does a good job making a statement about the paradox of tolerance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T18:33:24-08:00","id":1439336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, definitely. I was going to say something about that. Because I remember in The Fragile Path, the Chorus representative whose name I forgot B-something, gets sent to the First Cabal as a penance for having helped the Inquisition. The Celestial Chorus leadership of that time weren't <i>accepting</i> of other religions, but they weren't on board with religious persecution. So... then 350 years later, they embrace persecution of the same 'heretics&quot; who were their allies a few decades ago? Like, what?<br /> <br /> I know there are probably always elements of such intolerance among the Chorus, and I know that many times they've looked away while Native Americans, Africans, Australian Aborigines, South-Southeast Asians, etc. were massacred. But how are the leaders wholly participating in that at any time after the Grand Convocation?<br /> <br /> Glamourweaver, your explanation would make sense. &quot;We tried to help these people see that pluralism and compromise don't have to hurt them. We tried to reach out to them, to show them compassion, so they wouldn't support genocide out of knee-jerk fear. So they could become better people.<br /> <br /> Turns out, they were never motivated by fear. They're actually just sadistic maniacs because they like it. And now they've taken over. Oh God OH GOD, what do we do now?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:06:01-08:00","id":1439342,"title":"","content":"<b>How I run Technocracy games</b><br /> <br /> I always run Technocracy games with generally the appeal of being government agents crossed with Vampire the Masquerade. You are part of a secret government agency like SHIELD and are either one of its scientists or field operatives. However, the fact is your superiors are evil. They will often try to get you to do things that are blatantly immoral or that benefit them personally. It's a bit like working for a cyberpunk megacorporation where if you're LUCKY then they won't sell you out after asking you to kill a rival superior.<br /> <br /> However, the Technocracy is not an organization that you can just quit. You have credit cards, social security numbers, mortal relatives, and friends. If you defect from the Union then you will find yourself wanted as a pedophile, your family will be brainwashed into believing it, maybe your girlfriend will be replaced by a clone with orders to kill you when you pick her up, and that's assuming you can physically defect in the first place without them activating the microbomb in your brain that you never even knew was there.<br /> <br /> But maybe you can do some good in the Union if you're not a monster. The Technocracy does oppose the Nephandi, Marauders, renegade Umbrood, and a lot of Traditionalists who think they're heroic freedom fighters but blow up computer factories that are only tangentially associated with the Union. Also, how would you even know if they were lying that the Order of Hermes member doesn't sacrifice babies. I mean, it says he does right here in his file.<br /> <br /> Plus, you can be a moderating influence a lot of times. Sure, it says to gas the church with nerve gas because they believe in the faith healer! However, maybe you can figure out a way to convince them that it was all placebos as well as mind-control! That's, in a way, saving dozens of lives! Imagine if you weren't there.<br /> <br /> And, at one point, you realize that you can just go over your superior's head and get him cancelled.<br /> <br /> Then YOU'RE making the decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:14:29-08:00","id":1439344,"title":"","content":"So since it\u2019s come up, how I\u2019ve wrestled with climate change in the context of MtA, since it\u2019s an objective reality that seems resistant to whatever the Consensus believes, is that the Union interprets it as Paradox fallout from the industrial revolution. The Syndicate in particular views it as a \u201cmarket correction\u201d as the Consensus adjusts to accept post-industrialization levels of consumption. Having it firmly take root as part of the consensus would be the worse thing possible because then it will stay after the correction runs it\u2019s course - so they fund and support climate change denial. Environmentalists in ItX and the Progenitors are trying desperately to push real environmental reforms, but the Syndicate keeps blocking them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:22:47-08:00","id":1439347,"title":"","content":"But the Iteration X and Progenitors have precisely zero influence in any WoD government anywhere?<br /> <br /> And, long before climate change was discovered, there were these things called pollution and sacrifice zones and stolen land.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *off-topic silliness deleted*<br /> <br /> <br /> But I realize we may be veering away from the topic of Victorian Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:29:58-08:00","id":1439350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439347#post1439347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Iteration X and Progenitors have precisely zero influence in any WoD government anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that much on their own no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:35:52-08:00","id":1439352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439347#post1439347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Iteration X and Progenitors have precisely zero influence in any WoD government anywhere?<br /> <br /> And, long before climate change was discovered, there were these things called pollution and sacrifice zones and stolen land.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *off-topic silliness deleted*<br /> <br /> <br /> But I realize we may be veering away from the topic of Victorian Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think you\u2019ll find me arguing the Union is not and has not been consistently imperialist. Climate change denial takes special addressing because it\u2019s fucking up their own self interest and time tables for civilization.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t try to use WoD to do Star Trek at all. Main relatively recent media influence for Void Engineer aesthetic is BSG. Maybe some Expanse, haven\u2019t really seen enough to comment.<br /> <br /> No Revised edition makes clear that while the Gauntlet is very very thin in outer space, physical space still exists separately from the Deep Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T19:51:14-08:00","id":1439354,"title":"","content":"The denialism I actually can understand. Within Mage cosmology, it's horrifically defensible. But... why use fossil fuels in the first place when solar energy is so easy? When both of these technologies required equal effort to add them to the consensus, when the Sun was part of the consensus already but the fossil fuels didn't even exist in some cases until the Web of Faith was mutilated.... why bother with that gunk at all?<br /> <br /> Am I mistaken and fossil fuels were part of the consensus for centuries before the Victorian Age?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And even on top of the imperialism... even with the Enclosure Movement as a weapon against rural religion and pagan survivors.... in the Victorian Age, industrialization simply isn't a good thing even for the <i>white</i> Masses. This is the era when the air of London is not really breatheable for humans, when the Thames has been sterilized of all life, when factories and mines produce piles of mutilated and dead white children (and orgies of Banes in the Penumbra), when cholera and typhoid run rampant in the overcrowded cities created by rapid urbanization. It's not &quot;just&quot; imperialism, it's robber-baron betrayal and massacre of &quot;their own kind&quot;. It's when the bankers realize they can monetize human lives in a way goes way beyond slavery, and use that as a weapon against the very concept of humanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:09:54-08:00","id":1439355,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy is a group that probably has undergone numerous revisions to its paradigms. They originally used steam then they moved to nuclear and NOW they're thinking about solar energy because the others had side effects.<br /> <br /> Yes, PARADOX!<br /> <br /> Like global warming and Hulks and Spider-Men!<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> It's also not confirmed but pretty heavily implied that the Union often chases Sleeper trends, which makes the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts' meddling with the paradigm more useful. The Technocracy may have originally had plans to have the world look like one enormous coal powered universe with artificial coal and steam powered turbines everywhere. However, then some guy discovered something better that the Sleepers latched onto. Maybe Einstein was Awakened, maybe not.<br /> <br /> Then the Union readjusts their predictions for the future, possibly with scientists very annoyed by having to throw out all their models.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:16:17-08:00","id":1439356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439330#post1439330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna be clear that I in no way have any dislike towards Technocracy players. Or Vampire or Hunter players. I simply can't see the appeal of playing the Technocrats (or Vampire, Hunter, Wraith, Promethean, Kult, etc.) because it's too dark for me. Like, I need kitten-video-brain-bleach after reading too much about those games. That's just me.<br /> <br /> I am confused how the guys who rule the world have supported clean energy all this time and not made one micron of actual difference with any Sleeper government? Because if any environmentalism in the Union predates the Avatar Storm.... that just makes no sense to me. Doesn't the Syndicate have the magic to create unlimited relative wealth for themselves, even more than Pentex? Don't they basically own all the Sleeper governments? Aren't the Progenitors the inventors and purveyors of all things pesticide? Despite having the magic to rewrite reality so pesticides aren't even necessary? Despite real-world science now having proven they were never necessary*? And yet... the WOD is still even worse environmentally than real life. Like, lots worse. Like, Deep Horizon wasn't a unique or even unusual spill. Likewise... genuine religious freedom and tolerance isn't doing great in real life or the WOD, so if the Technocrats aren't really all about forced conversion... what have they been up to this whole time? Maybe I'm overestimating how powerful they are. Are the Ventrue actually the real rulers of the WOD?<br /> <br /> Even back in the Victorian Age, solar energy was invented in the same year as the internal combustion engine. In real life, I think around 1901. Pentex didn't exist until 1915. So if the Technocrats weren't utterly enamored with coal and oil, despite the visually and odorously obvious problems, why didn't they ever promote solar panels or electric busses in their Time Table? They ought to at least have just as much influence as Pentex and the Camarilla. If they have any environmental interest, they ought to have <i>something</i> to show for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Not to mention generations of organic regenerative agriculture practiced by some Native Americans before they were conquered.</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of factors, some of which I've touch upon already. The Technocrat control over the world, much like their internal unity, is greatly over exaggerated especially from the outside. The Traditions, our main viewpoint in MtAs, sees the Technocracy as this great monolith that dominates the world and certainly the Union likes to present that image but the truth is far from that. While they do have a great deal of influence over the world it's nowhere near as strong as they play it up. Worse, the Masses are increasingly rebelling against them and the Belief they're trying to push. Of course they're not rushing off to the Traditions either. Instead the Masses are embracing a self-destructive spiral of apathy and irrationality.<br /> <br /> It's telling that M20 Technocracy Reloaded starts with a Technocrat straight up saying:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We\u2019re losing.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know what you\u2019ve been told, kiddies: Our magnificent Union cornered the market on Consensus. Mankind\u2019s curled up with their smart phones, everyone loves technology, and cybernetic monkeys fly out my ass on command, raining fire on the poor little sorcerers cowering in the shadows of our magnificent Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I ask you this: Does it look like we are winning?<br /> <br /> Irrationality rules the day. Our world unravels at the seams. If our sad-sack species has formed any kind of consensus, it\u2019s that cutting off your nose to spite your face is much more fun when you use a chainsaw in public to do it.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re partly to blame for this, you know. We got stupid, careless, so caught up in our own propaganda that we refused to see the infection eating us alive.<br /> <br /> Worst of all, we got complacent. We believed it would only take a few surgical strikes on the worst offenders, and a wealth of luxuries for the Masses, before humanity would come around and enter a grand age of civil stability.<br /> <br /> We were wrong.<br /> <br /> Man is fundamentally irrational. He wants ghosts and vampires and boy wizards with English accents. He wants to believe that genital configurations or melanin production define him as blessed in the eyes of nonexistent gods. He doesn\u2019t fear Apocalypse \u2014 he craves it, so long as he doesn\u2019t have to live personally with the results. He\u2019s more fascinated with wanking off in the mirror than with looking toward the horizon of what he could be if he\u2019d just get his hand off his cock.<br /> <br /> Man cannot be trusted with the future. If we are to have a future, that future must belong to us. </div> </div> </div>They're not just fighting to protect the Consensus they've built from Realty Deviants that want to tear it down, they're fighting against the apathy of Masses that's causing it to rot from within.<br /> <br /> As for introducing technologies that could overcome climate change there's a problem with that, Paradox. While Enlightened Science and Hypertechnology can evade Paradox more easily than Magick can, it is still subject to Paradox. In fact, some speculate that Climate Change is a Paradox reaction in and of itself.<br /> <br /> The opening and closing fiction of the Rev Ed Syndicate book is a great example of this. The story revolves around a Syndicate agent sent to investigate a Sleeper medical research lab that is getting very promising results in a cure for cancer, very sudden results. As it turns out that's because a group of Progenitors are covertly helping the Sleepers with Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> The agent shuts them down, hating herself for doing so. Not because of some nefarious Technocrat scheme these Progenitors were disrupting but because it wouldn't work. If if can't be done through mundane science and technology it will cause Paradox and people will die because of it. To paraphrase the agent, the Masses dream of a world without cancer but they don't actually believe it. So the Technocracy cannot make a world without cancer. They need to slowly feed to slowly feed breadcrumbs to get them there so that they can have a cure for cancer by their own hands. That's the only way the Consensus would accept it.<br /> <br /> Climate Change is of that vein as well. The Technocracy could fix it with their Hyper Technology and Enlightened Science in a relative short order but the Consensus would not except it and the world would be hit with Paradox on a massive scale which would likely make things a thousand times worse.<br /> <br /> Which is also a factor in their frustration at the growing apathy and irrationality of the Masses. They're trying to put out dozens of the growing fires as the Sleepers are running around and throwing gasoline all over the place.<br /> <br /> As for solar energy vs. fossil fuels, it's again a matter of what will the Consensus accept and what it won't, what it will accept more easily and what will struggle to be accepted. More importantly what could be done most efficiently with the mundane science and technology of that time. Then of course you have hope that it catches on with the Sleepers.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Technocrats and their Time Tables are not perfect. They are regularly revising the Time Tables all the time because even with their Enlightened Science they cannot predict every variable that could affect their predictions.<br /> <br /> Again, the Technocracy likes to present itself as this All-Seeing, All-Powerful Monolith that rules the world from the shadows when in reality while they are powerful, they are no where near as powerful as they claim. Doubly so in a post-Avatar Storm world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:21:47-08:00","id":1439357,"title":"","content":"But why centuries of effort to repeatedly suppress solar energy, wind energy, and electric cars? What did they have against those concepts? It's not like those were tools of the Traditions or Werewolves or Vampires. I suppose they were invented by underfunded Sleeper geniuses.<br /> <br /> In the real world, we ask Who Killed the Electric Car?<br /> <br /> In the WOD, we ask Who Killed 500 Electric Car and Solar Energy Scientists and What Happened to Their Bodies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:34:15-08:00","id":1439359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439357#post1439357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why centuries of effort to repeatedly suppress solar energy, wind energy, and electric cars? What did they have against those concepts? It's not like those were tools of the Traditions or Werewolves or Vampires. I suppose they were invented by underfunded Sleeper geniuses.<br /> <br /> In the real world, we ask Who Killed the Electric Car?<br /> <br /> In the WOD, we ask Who Killed 500 Electric Car and Solar Energy Scientists and What Happened to Their Bodies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Centuries? The earliest I've seen anyone present solar energy in a practical form was the late 1800s, not centuries ago. Same with electric cars.<br /> <br /> As for who 'killed' it, a number of people and factors. Some of it was rival Syndicate and other Union members that were pushing their own alternatives. And by that same token, some of it was mundane individuals and groups, and perhaps even other Supernaturals. Hell, I wouldn't put it past some spiteful SoE getting involved as payback for the Order tossing Ether out. But other factors were the Consensus just not ready to accept the technologies needed to make things electric cars efficient and worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:38:21-08:00","id":1439360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439357#post1439357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why centuries of effort to repeatedly suppress solar energy, wind energy, and electric cars? What did they have against those concepts? It's not like those were tools of the Traditions or Werewolves or Vampires. I suppose they were invented by underfunded Sleeper geniuses.<br /> <br /> In the real world, we ask Who Killed the Electric Car?<br /> <br /> In the WOD, we ask Who Killed 500 Electric Car and Solar Energy Scientists and What Happened to Their Bodies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the obvious answer SHOULD be that the Technocracy destroyed them because they were not things they wanted for their paradigm. That if the cure for cancer is made by a sleeper, they WILL kill the Sleeper and confiscate his research if it's not on the time table. Not that this is ALL Technocrats. Some would be, maybe even the majority, horrified. But the <u><b>leadership</b></u> of the Union should be people who are of the mind that the Union's control is not allowed to be subverted. The whole point is they are CONTROL THROUGH TECHNOLOGY and anything out of that control is a wildcard.<br /> <br /> And if you think this isn't the thing the Union would do. It is LITERALLY the entire motivation behind the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts defection.<br /> <br /> That the Union will not allow functional but too advanced science into the world.<br /> <br /> The Loyalist Union would say, &quot;There's a good reason! Like 'Man was not ready for the Internet!'&quot; (and maybe they were right).<br /> <br /> Others would go, &quot;Bullshit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T20:43:24-08:00","id":1439361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439359#post1439359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Centuries? The earliest I've seen anyone present solar energy in a practical form was the late 1800s, not centuries ago. Same with electric cars.<br /> <br /> As for who 'killed' it, a number of people and factors. Some of it was rival Syndicate and other Union members that were pushing their own alternatives. And by that same token, some of it was mundane individuals and groups, and perhaps even other Supernaturals. Hell, I wouldn't put it past some spiteful SoE getting involved as payback for the Order tossing Ether out. But other factors were the Consensus just not ready to accept the technologies needed to make things electric cars efficient and worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, 150 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's historical revisionism, concerning the reality of how &quot;plausible&quot; and functional early electric cars were relative to the first combustion engines. Not buying it. Again, electric cars and solar energy were invented <b>by Sleepers</b> at the same time as internal compustion engines. Pentex simply didn't exist in the Victorian Era. The Sons of Ether had not defected yet. No other supernatural group was motivated or even able to eliminate clean energy as a concept in the 1800s.<br /> <br /> So, again: why did they kill the electric car, the solar panel, and the windmill? Why did they waste effort putting fossil fuels into the consensus when the same degree of effort and funding would have produced Sleeper-ready clean energy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:20:34-08:00","id":1439363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439357#post1439357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why centuries of effort to repeatedly suppress solar energy, wind energy, and electric cars? What did they have against those concepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Control. Power people can harness themselves makes them less dependent on technological infrastructure that gives Technocrats avenues of power (be they private industry or governmental) to exert influence for their other work to shape the Consensus and move resources through.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same reason they removed Ether from the Consensus before Tesla could provide free flowing power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:54:10-08:00","id":1439371,"title":"","content":"OK, that is actually plausible.<br /> <br /> Of course, it brings them right back to mustache-twirling evil and oppressing the Masses just for the sake of oppression itself. And profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:55:58-08:00","id":1439372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439361#post1439361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, 150 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's historical revisionism, concerning the reality of how &quot;plausible&quot; and functional early electric cars were relative to the first combustion engines. Not buying it. Again, electric cars and solar energy were invented <b>by Sleepers</b> at the same time as internal compustion engines. Pentex simply didn't exist in the Victorian Era. The Sons of Ether had not defected yet. No other supernatural group was motivated or even able to eliminate clean energy as a concept in the 1800s.<br /> <br /> So, again: why did they kill the electric car, the solar panel, and the windmill? Why did they waste effort putting fossil fuels into the consensus when the same degree of effort and funding would have produced Sleeper-ready clean energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about a fictional setting where Belief rewrites Reality who authors didn't have a perfect knowledge of the history of Science and Technology. Further we're talking about the World of Darkness here. You know a setting like our world but darker and with the Supernatural.<br /> <br /> If we didn't have clean energy back then, why would it exist in a setting that again, is our world but darker and with the Supernatural?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439363#post1439363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Control. Power people can harness themselves making them less dependent on technological infrastructure that give Technocrats avenues of power (be they private industry or governmental) to exert influence for their other work to shape the Consensus and move resources through.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same reason they removed Ether from the Consensus before Tesla could provide free flowing power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed when you're trying to shape the Consensus to your Belief, having as much Control and Influence as you can is vital. And it's a factor in why the Order became what it is. All that power went to their heads and their ideals slid further and further away.<br /> <br /> Had the Traditions gained upper hand in the Ascension War instead of the Order, they would have become just like the Order/Union, just with a Magical bent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:51:27-08:00","id":1439384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439371#post1439371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, that is actually plausible.<br /> <br /> Of course, it brings them right back to mustache-twirling evil and oppressing the Masses just for the sake of oppression itself. And profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about that being that such things aren't remotely unbelievable. We're in an age where people defunded the EPA and tried to sell national parks while opening up public places during a pandemic. All for comparative pennies on the dollar.<br /> <br /> For me, the best answer is the Union's leadership should be evil and that good Technocrats should be fighting to reform it or overthrow its leadership.<br /> <br /> But the organization itself should be hopelessly corrupted at the top levels as long as it represents the leadership of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T23:34:53-08:00","id":1439392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439190#post1439190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this supposed to be a horror game where you play monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the text as is in VM? Apparently not.<br /> <br /> The text of VM as is is saying that only one group of mages is Evil Enough to be singled out, and that the other two major factions are Mostly Good. That doesn't really strike me as a game that's about playing monsters at all if it's not treating them all as monsters equally.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that &quot;be a monster&quot; =/= &quot;always do evil Things&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439190#post1439190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like you can play the Victorian equivalent of Oppenheimer, but the consequences don't change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you grossly misunderstand Oppenheimer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439193#post1439193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously you think the Players Guide to the Sabbat fails as a game sourcebook, as they're portrayed as proud monsters playing football with the heads of innocents...Since we're at it: Can you really say the Camarilla, as an institution, isn't evil for any other reason than &quot;well, they're better than the Sabbat&quot;?.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, don't put words in my mouth. That's rude.<br /> <br /> Second...no.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the Camarilla is about the same degrees of evil as the Sabbat, just in different ways. Camarilla at least encourages vampires to try to be Human and to not give into the Beast and accidentally kill or be killed...at the cost of expecting everyone to follow and confirm to a constricting Masquerade and don't take seriously the threat of Gehenna, even though more and more signs are showing that it's true. The Sabbat gives you a bit more freedom to do what you want and not chaining to you as restricting as the Masquerade, not to mention does take Gehenna seriously on taking the fight to the Antediluvians...but that it also means not giving a shit about how monstrous you are and valuing human lives less.<br /> <br /> Both have the issue of elders who like their comfy positions of power and are reluctant to give them up to the younger vampires. Both surrounded by other vampires who will do whatever it takes to get ahead.<br /> <br /> (and no, no I'm not going to hear it on &quot;Camarilla covering up the threat of Gehenna&quot; as being comparable to &quot;the Technocracy covering up the existence of supernaturals&quot;)<br /> <br /> Although the Sabbat is actually a good example to compare to the Technocracy...because they ALSO changed drastically between editions.<br /> <br /> (and hence, from my understanding, grumbling on Sabbat fans with the direction of V5 on how it strongly suggests that the Sabbat are going to return to being their V1e versions)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439282#post1439282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant as a whole, to be fair I never got to read Dark Eras 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's there and lines up more in Victorian Era then it does with this depiction of the OoR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439285#post1439285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seers are more consciously selfish, but no less realistic, in that their motives are pure self interest. If Mage factions in Awakening are divided by &quot;what is magic for&quot; rather than Ascension's &quot;how does magic work&quot;, the Seers are the Mages who checked the &quot;absolutely comfort, power, wealth, luxury&quot; box, and that comes with required complicity in upholding the pyramid that lets them sit at the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point being that the Seers as you described makes more sense with the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar, not with the OoR/Union.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439262#post1439262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I had with the Convention books was that they were all about whitewashing (in the context of making them more moral and justified not racially) the Union so much so that the ITERATION X Revised Convention book removed all morally repugnant elements that the Guide to the Union left in (that everyone was &quot;Conditioned&quot;/brainwashed and terrorism as a Skill). Making them better because of the Avatar Storm is fine.<br /> <br /> BUTTTttt...<br /> <br /> Now is not the time to believe that the Establishment, Corporate rule, government, politicians, and militaristic idealogues to be the Good GuysTM. My big problem with the M20 guide to the Union is, &quot;Uh, where are the racist assholes?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't mind them being opposed by globalist progressives in the Union but they ABSOLUTELY would still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold up...are you saying your prefer 1e WoD?<br /> <br /> Otherwise...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439299#post1439299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;At what point is including the nastiness of RL fascism, racism, imperialism, and so on a good thing as game material?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>...and there is my problem right there regarding the &quot;Are we the Baddies?&quot; sidebar and select passages regarding the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> If it gets to the point that a book's adherence to tone and theme actively starts to disrupt the game at play, especially if it means actively pushing players away from playable options if they<br /> <br /> The book can't have its cake and eat it by wagging its finger about how awful one playable group is but then provide them as a playable option anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439177#post1439177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disclaimer, I don't own any Mage corebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439308#post1439308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm no Mage expert but...</div> </div> </div> </div>...then why are you talking about Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T23:46:08-08:00","id":1439393,"title":"","content":"Nvm that I should also note that the latest manuscript has this sidebar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Of Atrocities and \u201cProgress\u201d</b></i><br /> <br /> Note that helping European empires commit genocide is a really shitty thing to do. Troupes that favor a Luminary chronicle have their work cut out for them if they want to remain good guys during this period. Slavery, racist institutions, and cultural extermination are the historical tactics of this era\u2019s empires, and those methods enable the Technocracy\u2019s domination in the following centuries. Players who wish to remain on the better side of history would benefit more from moderating their Order\u2019s extremities than from battling \u201chostile natives\u201d in the name of a Technocratic future. Intriguing moral questions can arise from the latter sort of chronicle, of course, but it\u2019s worth remembering that \u201cthe white man\u2019s burden\u201d has an appalling human cost to the people on the receiving side of it. </div> </div> </div>So...it claims that the OoR is lock and step with the British Empire ideals...but then also turns around and says &quot;don't run chronicles that involves your OoR PCs actually massacring brown people&quot;?<br /> <br /> What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T02:47:04-08:00","id":1439406,"title":"","content":"Woof that was something. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> what do you want? Because at one point the OoR was apparently being written as anti-vaxx propaganda that was too harsh but now they are also being given too much leeway by saying, &quot;hey not every colonial or metropole subject was actively murdering black and brown people so hey readers just do that despite how conquest has been baked into the myth of progress.&quot; <br /> <br /> I'm totally fine making them nonplayable if they really hammer home how the myth Western science really ain't shit, stole most things, and the rest it did create was in response to the need of the empire. Including vaccines--again I'm not saying vaccines are bad but they aren't apolitical and have been created as a reaction to or supporter of genocide more than not. Maybe settlers shouldn't have been so filthy or ya know interested in spreading disease and destroying entire ecosystems.<br /> <br /> Also who cares about equality when it comes to the Victorian Era. For the record one group was evil. One group will always be more monstrous and can never absolve that fact. I'm fine with people playing them because hey they still be colonizing and the world hasn't changed much. It would be like saying no one should ever play a white person or a cop or a doctor. I'm totally down with that but let's be realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T03:18:30-08:00","id":1439414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439392#post1439392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, don't put words in my mouth. That's rude.<br /> <br /> Second...no.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the Camarilla is about the same degrees of evil as the Sabbat, just in different ways. Camarilla at least encourages vampires to try to be Human and to not give into the Beast and accidentally kill or be killed...at the cost of expecting everyone to follow and confirm to a constricting Masquerade and don't take seriously the threat of Gehenna, even though more and more signs are showing that it's true. The Sabbat gives you a bit more freedom to do what you want and not chaining to you as restricting as the Masquerade, not to mention does take Gehenna seriously on taking the fight to the Antediluvians...but that it also means not giving a shit about how monstrous you are and valuing human lives less.<br /> <br /> Both have the issue of elders who like their comfy positions of power and are reluctant to give them up to the younger vampires. Both surrounded by other vampires who will do whatever it takes to get ahead.<br /> <br /> (and no, no I'm not going to hear it on &quot;Camarilla covering up the threat of Gehenna&quot; as being comparable to &quot;the Technocracy covering up the existence of supernaturals&quot;)<br /> <br /> Although the Sabbat is actually a good example to compare to the Technocracy...because they ALSO changed drastically between editions.<br /> <br /> (and hence, from my understanding, grumbling on Sabbat fans with the direction of V5 on how it strongly suggests that the Sabbat are going to return to being their V1e versions)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't think the Players Guide to The Sabbat it's about playing with bad guys?<br /> <br /> Because you said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439392#post1439392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it\u2019s bizarre that we have a sidebar that basically says \u201cdon\u2019t play these guys as anything other then EVIL\u201d.<br /> <br /> It restricts play options.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s not doing that, then it fails as a game sourcebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>which kinda does imply that the Players Guide to the Sabbat, which does say very much that these guys (the Sabbat) are EVIL - much worse than the Victorian Technocracy - would be restricting player options (playing a Good Samaritan Sabbat), hence it either fails as a sourcebook or should forbbid playing with the Sabbat altogether (obiously doesn't).<br /> <br /> And note that the Guide to the Sabbat paints them as a much worse monsters, much more inhuman, than Victorian Technocracy, or doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Or, as I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously you think the Players Guide to the Sabbat fails as a game sourcebook, as they're portrayed as proud monsters playing football with the heads of innocents... </div> </div> </div>Unless you think they weren't portrayed as inhuman mosters , which is way worse than how Victorian Technocracy it's being portrayed, that's what you said and not me putting words in your mouth<br /> <br /> BTW:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . The Sabbat gives you a bit more freedom to do what you want and not chaining to you as restricting as the Masquerade </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure being a colonialists overlord gives you a lot of those freedoms too...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> not to mention does take Gehenna seriously on taking the fight to the Antediluvians...but that it also means not giving a shit about how monstrous you are and valuing human lives less. </div> </div> </div>It's true that the book says this is what the Sabbat believes, but to avoid complicating this with metaplot, the point it's that they're Evil - not the justifications they invent for it, true or not.<br /> <br /> So.<br /> <br /> Should the book says European ARE indeed superior, and that they have to culture the savages even if that means enslaving them ... or is it enough with them believing this is true?<br /> <br /> Shouldn't the book, taking in count this is a real world issue, also take a stance and say this belief actually isn't true, and that thinking this means not giving a shit about how monstrous you are, and valuing human lives less?<br /> <br /> Exactly what do you expect the book to say about what OoR was doing overseas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iladas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> what do you want? Because at one point the OoR was apparently being written as anti-vaxx propaganda that was too harsh but now they are also being given too much leeway by saying, &quot;hey not every colonial or metropole subject was actively murdering black and brown people so hey readers just do that despite how conquest has been baked into the myth of progress.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2021, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T06:03:07-08:00","id":1439432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except I don't think that's what the text of VAM, or myself and Data are saying. We're not saying ignore the bad, focus on the good. We're saying that both need to be recognized and understood.<br /> <br /> To focus solely on the good or bad is wrong because it will paint a biased picture of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bias isn't automatically evil. It's pretty good to be biased against something so evil as this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we met one of our ancestors from the Victorian Era, we would be horrified by at least some of their beliefs and attitudes. Does that automatically make them bad people? No, it makes them just people from another time, just as complicated and flawed as us. </div> </div> </div>W/o entering in the merits and defects of moral relativism: As I pointed out earlier, Imperialism was only considered good by imperialist societies. This is not like being a &quot;murderer of man&quot; being a good thing for the mediterranean belicose greek and spartans, in an era where war was very common. We're talking about ppl that had nothing to do with it being invaded. There were clear victims here.<br /> <br /> Also, I get ppl it's complicated and flawed, a product of their time - Note that I always talk about the OoR as an evil <u>institution </u>- and ppl of that institution being bad insofar as they proffit from it, presumably support it in some fashion, and aren't figthing against it.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein as how I can say it's a very bad thing if you're affiliated to the Nazi party, regardless if you never violated any human rigths in person. I'm not saying you're AS bad as the SS, but surely you can see how <i>not reconsidering your allegiances can be quite problematic.</i> <hr /><br /> I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> notion of Soul Searching better.<br /> <br /> The implication (if I understand it rigth) would be that not all the OoR was on board with the obvious agenda of the OoR at that time, presumably fought against that agenda, but failed to stop it in any meaningful fashion.<br /> <br /> The only problem I have with that it's that the whole shit had been going on for centuries at 1885. Imperialism understood as a concept it's older than Victoria, similar tragedies were happening since Columbus found America arround 1500. Or was the Order not deeply involved with those *very defining* moments of western culture 'til now? - because I seem to remember that they were<br /> <br /> I think one has reasons to say the Soul Searching had been going for a while now. And losing.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the game, the cards of what the technocracy would become were already very much on the table in the Victorian Era:<br /> <br /> *At this point in time the largest Idealist faction known in the Order: The Craftmasons, were already purged. If a whole Convention can be murdered for being too idealist about peasants, then how can other Idealists feel safe?<br /> <br /> *Nobody will miss the Gabrielites, as they were among the worst of the Order - but If I remember correctly they weren't purged out of their brutality, they were purged as a sign of OoR not being tolerant with mystical practices anymore<br /> <br /> I think that Conditioning pays no place in the &quot;fall from grace&quot; of the Order. I mean, <i>can we really say they were involved in worse</i> <i>things</i>, at <i>any </i>time? Because I think this is, as represented by older books and everything I've read, very much their darkest time in history.<br /> <br /> I DO think, however, that the lack of Conditioning allows one to play with &quot;Milo''s , Idealistic people that would try to figth against the larger goals of the institution. But I don't think this, Lore Wise, is a time of Idealism. Rather<i>, this is the time where Idealism falls. </i>I don't think Idealists can opperate under these conditions w/o peril of ending like the Masons did, if their anti-imperialistic agenda shows too much. They're freer to <i>hide </i>this agenda, as there are presumably no Psi-Ops reading their minds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T06:28:03-08:00","id":1439433,"title":"","content":"The manuscript has a reference in it about the Etherites knowing that the Union will be gunning for them sooner or later and making preparations for that eventuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:10:16-08:00","id":1439436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439393#post1439393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nvm that I should also note that the latest manuscript has this sidebar:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So...it claims that the OoR is lock and step with the British Empire ideals...but then also turns around and says &quot;don't run chronicles that involves your OoR PCs actually massacring brown people&quot;?<br /> <br /> What?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not saying that at all. It's saying that if your table wants their Luminaries to be good guys than that kind of stuff is not the way you want to go. Because you know the last time I checked, massacring indigenous people for the British Empire was still a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Rather it says that if you want heroic Luminaries, you should be fighting against such things. Play the people that fought against those things in that era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:55:52-08:00","id":1439442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439406#post1439406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> what do you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>A consistent direction with what the OoR is supposed to be. <br /> <br /> Preferably to make them a viable, playable option because I think reverting back to Mage 1e\u2019s direction is a terrible idea for a game. And that in order to do the opposite and quadruple down on \u201cOoR is unambiguously Absolute Evil\u201d would require a Beast: the Primordial level rewrite, that I\u2019m pretty sure OPP would like to avoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439414#post1439414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you don't think the Players Guide to The Sabbat it's about playing with bad guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed the point of my whole post. <br /> <br /> My point was that the 1e/2e depiction of the Sabbat changed as editions went on, pulling them away to a more nuanced depiction and not just \u201cEvil-est vampires\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439436#post1439436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not saying that at all. It's saying that if your table wants their Luminaries to be good guys than that kind of stuff is not the way you want to go. Because you know the last time I checked, massacring indigenous people for the British Empire was still a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Rather it says that if you want heroic Luminaries, you should be fighting against such things. Play the people that fought against those things in that era.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except it has to be because the implication is if the PCs aren\u2019t doing it, then they are genociding not-whites which this sidebar is telling you to not actually play out.<br /> <br /> And if it doesn\u2019t, well, the point stands that the book\u2019s messaging on what to do with the OoR is unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:56:18-08:00","id":1439443,"title":"","content":"As well, I do think that in the Victorian Age, it's more a matter of being free to object then being free to hide. Between the destruction of the Cabal of Pure Thought and the induction of the Skeleton Keys, the Order didn't really have anything resembling a secret police to punish people who stepped out of line. That happened more on a convention by convention basis. And even when they did have \u201csecret police\u201d, it wasn't like the Ksirafai (who had disappeared shortly after the Craftmasons were purged) or the New World Order (which brought in the notion of \u201cthought crime\u201d \u2014 that you could and should be punished for what you <i>think</i>, not just what you <i>do</i>). <br /> <br /> And I believe that the standards of what constitutes a fitting punishment were different then than after the rise of the NWO. A Milo would face reprisals for interfering with the greater goals of the order; but those reprisals would not be Room 101, and likely wouldn't be anything comparably draconian, largely because his opposition wouldn't be as likely to be viewed as criminal or traitorous, but rather merely wrong headed.<br /> <br /> All that said, the Victorian age idealists are definitely losing. Not because of institutional punishment, but rather because their views are in the minority. Invoking a more recent concept, the Overton Window within the Order doesn't align with their views, so if they express them openly they tend to be mocked and shunned. <br /> <br /> As for the destruction of the Craftmasons: their destruction was 200 years earlier, and the Watsonian justification for it, as understood by the Order, is still unclear. Also unclear are the details as to <i>how</i> it happened: all we know is that it was carried out by an alliance between the Ksirafai, the Cabal of Pure Thought, and the High Guild; and by the start of the Victorian Age, two of those groups are <i>gone</i> \u2014 one has effectively been wiped from history; and the other, let's just say that many who think that the purge of the Craftmasons was wrong might take some small satisfaction in the Cabal of Pure Thought's demise. I don't see Victorian idealists hiding out because of the destruction of a convention that took place relative to them about as far back as the American Revolution is to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:59:48-08:00","id":1439444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439436#post1439436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's not saying that at all. It's saying that if your table wants their Luminaries to be good guys than that kind of stuff is not the way you want to go. Because you know the last time I checked, massacring indigenous people for the British Empire was still a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Rather it says that if you want heroic Luminaries, you should be fighting against such things. Play the people that fought against those things in that era.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. That's why my current thoughts on the subject lean more toward there being idealists within the order that are fighting against the evils that the order is perpetrating. Or they are in situations where said evils have no impact on them or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:59:56-08:00","id":1439445,"title":"","content":"And then there\u2019s the bigger issue: <br /> <br /> Why are so many of y\u2019all so eager to accept blaming the real world atrocities of the Victorian era on a fictional group of technowizards? Doesn\u2019t that whitewash and trivialize the actual perpetrators that happened in history by scapegoating a group that...never existed in the first place?<br /> <br /> How is this different from V5 Chechnya, where everyone agreed it was NOT ok to say that vampires were responsible from the real life atrocities in that region?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:03:24-08:00","id":1439446,"title":"","content":"The difference is that we're not actually blaming the actions on the order of reason. That is, we're not saying that if not for the order of Reason these things would not have happened. Rather, the issue is that the order of reason reflects these real world atrocities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:04:54-08:00","id":1439447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439445#post1439445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there\u2019s the bigger issue: <br /> <br /> Why are so many of y\u2019all so eager to accept blaming the real world atrocities of the Victorian era on a fictional group of technowizards? Doesn\u2019t that whitewash and trivialize the actual perpetrators that happened in history by scapegoating a group that...never existed in the first place?<br /> <br /> How is this different from V5 Chechnya, where everyone agreed it was NOT ok to say that vampires were responsible from the real life atrocities in that region?</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone said this? Or have they said that the ideals espoused by this fictional group are those held by the real world perpetrators so they can't be separated.<br /> <br /> I'm just at a loss. Are you asking for a fictional group of technowizards who espouse western science and modernity who were somehow not part of that system or agenda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 03-12-2021, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:12:49-08:00","id":1439448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439446#post1439446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that we're not actually blaming the actions on the order of reason. That is, we're not saying that if not for the order of Reason these things would not have happened. Rather, the issue is that the order of reason reflects these real world atrocities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they are.<br /> <br /> There's a bit that says that the Void Seekers were directly responsible for causing the Anglo-Zulu War and that the Syndicate directly caused the Opium War, among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:19:36-08:00","id":1439450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439448#post1439448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they are.<br /> <br /> There's a bit that says that the Void Seekers were directly responsible for causing the Anglo-Zulu War and that the Syndicate directly caused the Opium War, among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having read that part that is a fair critique. I dont think its outside the realm of the rewrite to highlight how they were collaborators or co-conspirators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:24:34-08:00","id":1439452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439445#post1439445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there\u2019s the bigger issue:<br /> <br /> Why are so many of y\u2019all so eager to accept blaming the real world atrocities of the Victorian era on a fictional group of technowizards? Doesn\u2019t that whitewash and trivialize the actual perpetrators that happened in history by scapegoating a group that...never existed in the first place?<br /> <br /> How is this different from V5 Chechnya, where everyone agreed it was NOT ok to say that vampires were responsible from the real life atrocities in that region?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you have a faction in a WW2 Mage game who represent the paradigm of Nazi Ideology, then obviously they're bad guys involved in supporting the results of that paradigm. While 1e made the Union cartoon villains without nuance, the point even when they were better written has ALWAYS been to represent the paradigm of Western secular imperialism (today neoimperialism) for the globe. In the Victorian Era that means genocide.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they can't be played, some of my favorite Exalted characters are Dynasts, but institutionally they're going to be inseperable from Empire..<br /> <br /> Edit: The issue with Chechnya was that it reduced an ongoing real world atrocity to a distraction for the REAL BAD THING the Vampires were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:25:38-08:00","id":1439453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439445#post1439445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there\u2019s the bigger issue:<br /> <br /> Why are so many of y\u2019all so eager to accept blaming the real world atrocities of the Victorian era on a fictional group of technowizards? Doesn\u2019t that whitewash and trivialize the actual perpetrators that happened in history by scapegoating a group that...never existed in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a fantasy game about a fictional bunch of technowizards that secretly rule the world? I also think there's also a fundamental difference between ongoing ones and ones that are over a century ago.<br /> <br /> Call me crazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is this different from V5 Chechnya, where everyone agreed it was NOT ok to say that vampires were responsible from the real life atrocities in that region? </div> </div> </div>Because the Union is a metaphor for the real life evils while Chechnya was about it being a cover for them.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between:<br /> <br /> 1. The vampires of Chechnya are making it illegal to be gay to feed on people.<br /> <br /> 2. A vampire in Chechnya is homophobic and fascist drawing attention to the RL atrocity.<br /> <br /> The author apparently wanted 2# and was edited to do 1#","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2021, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:40:27-08:00","id":1439456,"title":"","content":"Not wanting to share too much personal information I feel like talking about my dad is useful. My dad is from Puerto Rico and since the U.S. crippled its capacity to be financially stable the only real job he could find was joining the U.S. Army. He spent 22 years in the Army as a Combat Engineer and then as Nuclear, Biological, and Chemical Weapon Tech. He participated in the War in Afghanistan and Iraq. He is both a colonized subject and an imperial agent. That has never been lost on him or me. Hell he talks about the complexities and paradoxes of that all of the time. When I share his story with my son I cannot and will not separate the fact that while my dad might not have done explicitly terrible things (I really don't know) he chose to be participate and support truly heinous things in the name of feeding his family. Obviously no one's parents are from this time, but to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> point, the Technocracy is a pretty solid and clear metaphor for real world evils. Hell they don't even believe they are doing magic. So, it is not outside the realm of belief that you can roll up a character that is for OoR that doesn't actively kill brown people while also accepting that that doesn't really matter or change the fact that they are supporting it somewhere. Even if they are resisting it at the individual level. <br /> <br /> I would totally be down also for talking about the complexities and nuances of colonized and colonizer relations. The unification of Hawaii into a kingdom would probably not have happened without European support. So there is definitely a Mage story there where some ali'i Kopa Loei work with members of the Order of Reason to get weapons to help them out. But that complexity does not also mean they are the same or share equal responsibility with how the world is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:44:20-08:00","id":1439458,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> I think you can use fantasy and science fiction as a pretty solid tool to discuss real world issues without trivializing them. Also to draw from RL events for what is essentially a entertainment property.<br /> <br /> The best examples off the top of my head being Magneto's origins and the Black Panther movie being very heavy subject matter for superhero stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T09:44:58-08:00","id":1439465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439448#post1439448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they are.<br /> <br /> There's a bit that says that the Void Seekers were directly responsible for causing the Anglo-Zulu War and that the Syndicate directly caused the Opium War, among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That idea, w/o context, has a very 2\u00b0 edition vibe. I think it could be argued, like Revised did, that it is bad taste. That supernaturals should subtly influence humanity rather than control it's destiny.<br /> <br /> But, as has been explained by others above (and much better than I could ever hope to), that wouldn't really matter for the subject at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:09:08-08:00","id":1439468,"title":"","content":"Anyways... <br /> <br /> *skims through the \u201cVictorian Magick\u201d chapter...sees that it lists Nephandic Focus elements from \u201cBook of the Fallen\u201d in the \u201cVictorian Focus\u201d section* <br /> <br /> ...and right back to muddled creative intent regarding \u201cBook of the Fallen is NOT a Player\u2019s Guide to the Nephandi\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:18:19-08:00","id":1439471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439468#post1439468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways...<br /> <br /> *skims through the \u201cVictorian Magick\u201d chapter...sees that it lists Nephandic Focus elements from \u201cBook of the Fallen\u201d in the \u201cVictorian Focus\u201d section*<br /> <br /> ...and right back to muddled creative intent regarding \u201cBook of the Fallen is NOT a Player\u2019s Guide to the Nephandi\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, why not destroy reality?<br /> <br /> You can always make a better one.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:18:35-08:00","id":1439472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439468#post1439468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways... <br /> <br /> *skims through the \u201cVictorian Magick\u201d chapter...sees that it lists Nephandic Focus elements from \u201cBook of the Fallen\u201d in the \u201cVictorian Focus\u201d section* <br /> <br /> ...and right back to muddled creative intent regarding \u201cBook of the Fallen is NOT a Player\u2019s Guide to the Nephandi\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I wouldn't mind if they were to cut the book of the Fallen Focus elements. They really aren't meant for player characters, and their use as warnings of how the likes of the Nephandi operate are covered in that book \u2014 and <i>aren't</i> covered <i>here</i>. Nor should they be: to the extent that Victorian Mage is serving as a warning against something, it's imperialism that's its target, not the sadistic manipulation that the Nephandi represent. <br /> <br /> So yeah; I'd cut it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T11:42:56-08:00","id":1439484,"title":"","content":"Another \u201cwho gets credit for\u2026\u201d question, and it's a biggie: who gets credit for the formal end of slavery? Because that also happens smack dab in the middle of the Victorian age, starting in Britain and then followed up by the American Civil War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T11:46:35-08:00","id":1439486,"title":"","content":"I mean I think it's safe to say that slavery didn't functionally end in the United States during this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T11:47:51-08:00","id":1439487,"title":"","content":"That's why I said \u201cformally\u201d. 