ntainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439647#post1439647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok fair, but there\u2019s a big difference between the East India Company, or Leopold II trying to maintain the Congo as his private property to avoid oversight, and secret cabals of elites in groups that have no public existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a corporation miles away meeting in smoke-filled rooms making massive decisions that ruin your life and could easily involve ruining the lives of millions.<br /> <br /> It's not literally true for the Technocracy but it's exaggerated for superheroic effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:11:17-08:00","id":1439660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439634#post1439634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first of all the setting indeed doesn\u2019t make sense, but suspending the disbelief necessary, the Technocracy\u2019s position as \u201cthe Authority\u201d is necessary for it to make any sense at all because why would people have stopped believing in literal magic in a world where it objectively exists unless the people hiding it were in the positions of power to do so?<br /> <br /> The Union being \u201cthe Man\u201d as it were was also thematically necessary for the game\u2019s intended anti-authoritarian vibe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point being you can have the Technocracy be in *a* position of authority without being *the* position of Authority that would need making them be &quot;&quot;&quot;secret masters of the world&quot;&quot;&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise it kind of kills a Traditions/Crafts-only game if it keeps being interrupted by Union agents swooping in on the PCs.<br /> <br /> (nvm M20's position being &quot;no, no the Union's Paradigm has not completely dominated the entire world&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the games ignore each other where they\u2019d otherwise get in each other\u2019s way. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I would prefer if newer books tried to steer away from quadrupling down on the inconsistencies to the larger WoD setting.<br /> <br /> And because I know full well that the games are never going to take the official stance of &quot;each gameline is actually an alternate reality of each other&quot; to explain the inconsistencies with each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:19:36-08:00","id":1439664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439660#post1439660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And my point being you can have the Technocracy be in *a* position of authority without being *the* position of Authority that would need making them be &quot;&quot;&quot;secret masters of the world&quot;&quot;&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise it kind of kills a Traditions/Crafts-only game if it keeps being interrupted by Union agents swooping in on the PCs.<br /> <br /> (nvm M20's position being &quot;no, no the Union's Paradigm has not completely dominated the entire world&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2a/X-Men_v1_141.jpg/220px-X-Men_v1_141.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Original Recipe Mage</b> is heavily inspired by THE INVISIBLES by Grant Morrison and that also inspired THE MATRIX. The whole point is that mages are on the run. They are meeting in dirty warehouses and squatting in abandoned buildings because the Men in Black will kill you if you don't. It's very much like being one of the X-men in that chantries are hidden because literal robots will come to kill you and your family if you're identified as a dirty-dirty mutant.<br /> <br /> The reason the Technocracy was treated as absolutely monstrous was because the pogrom was deliberate invocation. It also had violent blowing up of Constructs and murder of Technocracy agents justified because it was a ASCENSION WAR and the point was not to achieve some arbitrary magical goal about Mass Ascension but out of survival.<br /> <br /> <b>Revised</b> Technocracy is too weak to hunt mages like animals and murder their families. These are very different takes on gameplay due to the fact the Technocracy is now a playable faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:42:46-08:00","id":1439670,"title":"","content":"Yes, and I prefer Rev\u2019s take over 1e\u2019s. <br /> <br /> On principle I don\u2019t care for games that go overboard on nailing a tone that\u2019s actively detrimental and toxic to playability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:55:39-08:00","id":1439671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439670#post1439670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and I prefer Rev\u2019s take over 1e\u2019s.<br /> <br /> On principle I don\u2019t care for games that go overboard on nailing a tone that\u2019s actively detrimental and toxic to playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure, &quot;Rebel Alliance&quot; is playable.<br /> <br /> But it's your game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T13:17:56-08:00","id":1439711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439670#post1439670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and I prefer Rev\u2019s take over 1e\u2019s.<br /> <br /> On principle I don\u2019t care for games that go overboard on nailing a tone that\u2019s actively detrimental and toxic to playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the &quot;Are We The Baddies?&quot; sidebar goes overboard or even does something against playability. What it does is to make something quite clear in order to be respectful to the cultures on the other side of imperialism and then even gives you the option to play a good person from the Order of Reason who actively fights or rebels against all of that. It's not really forcing you to play a bigot, it's the same idea as playing an idealist in the modern Technocracy that wants to end Room 101 and the Pogrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 03-13-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T16:36:14-08:00","id":1439737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439711#post1439711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;Are We The Baddies?&quot; sidebar goes overboard or even does something against playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it does, with some very explicit wording that's very hard top misinterpret as anything else. Such as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Are We The Baddies?</u><br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> There, we said it. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Luminaries believe in the supposed higher goals of the Order <b>but for plenty of magi, the brutality and conquest is the <i>point.</i></b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even among those magi who hold to lofty ideals of enlightening all of humanity, when presented with the monstrous evidence of what Order-backed imperialism looks like, they often choose to ignore it. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can play Order of Reason magi who are genuinely good people and who will really fight for humanity rather than trying to shackle and choke it beneath an oppressive regime; <b>but the Order fights against those tendencies.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ultimately, a chronicle featuring Luminary player characters is likely to be either the darkest kind of horror,</b> <b>witnessing the ravenous machine of imperialism from within, or a story of breaking loose from the Order\u2019s authority and rebelling against its monstrous excesses.</b> </div> </div> </div>So in summary:<br /> <br /> -The first couple of sentences lays it out with no ambiguity that &quot;yes, yes the Order of Reason is EVIL.&quot;<br /> <br /> -That most Luminaries don't believe in progressing things with science and reason, and that they do want ONLY control and &quot;oppressing brown people is KEWL!&quot; (nvm that that in of itself doesn't make sense, since that would mean they have no reason to go after white Hermetics, Christian Choristors, white Verbena, Siberian Dreamspeakers...)<br /> <br /> -The sidebar essentially dictates that if you do OoR chronicle in any other way that it describes, then STs and players are Choosing to play them wrong.<br /> <br /> -This sidebar actively contradicts the chapter, since a lot of the things the sidebar says the OoR are...aren't:<ul><li>It does list feats and ideology that the various Blocs and Conventions have done: from the Grand Faculty's contributions to sanitation and hygiene, the Golden Guild supporting labor unions, and the Brotherhood of Mechanicians specifically identifies with the working class on giving them the tools they need to make their lives better. (and no, the text is not explicit and clear enough to say &quot;oh this is all just IC, unreliable narrator propaganda the OoR tells itself&quot;, so I do not buy that as an excuse to directly dismiss their feats and ideologies)</li> <li>Or how the various Blocs/Conventions ARE aware of and acknowledge the atrocities the other groups do. It mentions how the Grand Faculty got pissed when the Void Seekers started the Anglo-Zulu War (although once again, claiming that a fictional group started an actual historical war is Squick as hell), or how the Skeleton Keys do operate with the Pinkertons and that, yes, that would have meant being involved with breaking up labor strikes, and that the BoM and EE were fucking pissed at them for doing that (although I'll note that it's weird that GG isn't referenced.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> -If the Table of Contents is anything to go by...no, no you are not required to have Victorian-era chronicles only be centered around the atrocities of the era:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chapter Seven: Storytelling the Victorian Fantastic provides suggestions and assistance for running campaigns and creating scenarios in the Victorian Era, including incorporating a wealth of ideas and tropes from popular Victorian fiction, <i><b>ranging from Westerns to early science fiction by Jules Verne or H. G. Wells, to strange tales of distant locales.</b></i> </div> </div> </div>Which...yeah I think guidance on running plots and chronicles that are more Fistful of Dollars, From the Earth to the Moon, Journey to the Center of the Earth, in addition to Drunken Master 2, League of Extraordinary Gentlemen-but-not-accidentally-problematic, or Once Upon a Time in the West.<br /> <br /> The sidebar is dictating One-True-Wayisms on how to play Order of Reason, and it contradicts this very chapter AND the rest of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T16:47:12-08:00","id":1439739,"title":"","content":"I admit my V:TM experience is influencing me. My general view is VAMPIREDOM is evil.<br /> <br /> However, you are often trying to do some good while involved in it.<br /> <br /> I think any Victorian Technocrat that is supervising the enslavement and conquest of Natives is evil and no one should be playing Syndicate Executive of the West Indies Company unless they're trying to bring it down from the inside. HOWEVER, I can also see a pair of Men in Black/Skeleton Keys based on Holmes and Watson solving occult murder in London.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason is a BIG organization even if it's effect on the world is pretty bad as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:04:48-08:00","id":1439742,"title":"","content":"So, just to lay my cards all out, since there is confusion on my stance regarding the Order of Reason:<br /> <br /> -Yes, I am fine with OoR's goal to be to try to stomp out mystic Paradigms and Paradigms not part of their organization. That's kind of the point of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> -I'm fine with them taking advantage of the reach the British Empire provides them to wage their side of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> -I am not saying you're not allowed to portray OoR as villains period...in a Traditions/Crafts game (hell I'm in the middle of a Mage game right now where the STs only allow Traditions and Crafts and no Technocracy PCs). I'm saying that it shouldn't be the ONLY option to portraying the OoR.<br /> <br /> -No, I am not ok with them saying that they're directly responsible for real-world atrocities because that DOES whitewash and oversimplify the actual history behind these real world events, and is as bad as V5 Chechnya, and goes against the stance the WoD has up until now, like what's stated in Wraith's Charnel Houses of Europe, ergo &quot;the Holocaust was not directly caused by a WoD splat, please don't do that&quot;.<br /> <br /> -No, I am not ok with them being completely lock-in step with ALL British Victorian ideology. The way how the entire gameline presents Enlightened Science, that they discover scientific innovations decades, if not centuries before Sleepers do, so they would have to know that all of the now-debunked Victorian science theories like &quot;&quot;&quot;scientific racism&quot;&quot;&quot; are inherently untrue. And that it contradicts Mage as a gameline with &quot;belief changes reality&quot;. Because if OoR logically doesn't believe these debunked theories, why would they promote them? If they did try to promote them, then their magick shouldn't work. So why would it?<br /> <br /> -And to lead into the above: in order for players to play and RP as OoR, their PCs have to believe their characters are doing the right thing. If they don't believe they're doing the right thing then they can't perform magick...you know, the Thing-That-You-Do-the-Most in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> -I prefer their mentality on waging the Ascension War to be less &quot;oppressing colored people is KEWL!!!&quot; and more &quot;I just want you to understand, that this is nothing personal. This is simply...business.&quot;<br /> <br /> -I also prefer, as mentioned above on Skeleton Keys vs BoM/EE regarding labor unions, I absolutely also prefer cases of &quot;the right hand not talking to the left hand&quot; because, yes, in-fighting between whole factions IS an interesting conflict to play out, and not just restricted to individual Luminaries against the entire Order.<br /> <br /> -And finally, yes I prefer if the leads at the top of the organization were corrupt and maneuver the organization to do questionable things, but not the rank and file members...aka the typical Luminary PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:16:31-08:00","id":1439745,"title":"","content":"I think there should be options to play a Technocrat/Reason member who isn't a white supremacist imperialist, a fascist, or a villain. They'll be treated barely better than the Tradition mages who are hunted &quot;like animals&quot; to quote another poster. But that's not so far from the reality for anyone who opposes white supremacy, even in the real world.<br /> <br /> I do NOT think there should be any options in any game to play an imperialist, fascist, or white supremacist without the game pointing out that this is utterly, irredeemably, inexcuseably evil. No matter what luxuries/hygiene items/medicine they sell to middle- and upper-class white people.<br /> <br /> Evil characters are playable in Vampire, so I don't see the problem here. I'm not sure it's even possible for a non-Nephandus to be as evil as the average Tzemisce. Tzimisce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-13-2021, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:19:24-08:00","id":1439746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439742#post1439742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-No, I am not ok with them saying that they're directly responsible for real-world atrocities because that DOES whitewash and oversimplify the actual history behind these real world events, and is as bad as V5 Chechnya, and goes against the stance the WoD has up until now, like what's stated in Wraith's Charnel Houses of Europe, ergo &quot;the Holocaust was not directly caused by a WoD splat, please don't do that&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best way to address this is basically to not do a bait and switch. If you're going to do, say, a V:TM game set in the Civil War or Reconstruction then you shouldn't have a vampire who is doing slavery as a cover for feeding. Unless you're doing a humor game and everyone understands it like ABRAHAM LINCOLN, VAMPIRE HUNTER. However, you can certainly have a vampire who is every bit as racist and vile as the beliefs of the time. That doesn't demean the larger atrocities.<br /> <br /> Which is basically what I think with the Order of Reason and Victorian Age. Most of the Technocracy in Victorian England are going to be lock step with British imperialism because they're a bunch of racist white British men that want to conquer the world.<br /> <br /> If you want to do non-imperialist OoR members then they should be feuding with these guys ala Captain Nemo or Five Metal Dragons members or even communists/socialists/anarchists out to overthrow the capitalist Order of Reason members. They might be considered enemies of the OoR but they might also supported by other factions in it.<br /> <br /> The Union and Traditions are full of infighting after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -No, I am not ok with them being completely lock-in step with ALL British Victorian ideology. The way how the entire gameline presents Enlightened Science, that they discover scientific innovations decades, if not centuries before Sleepers do, so they would have to know that all of the now-debunked Victorian science theories like &quot;&quot;&quot;scientific racism&quot;&quot;&quot; are inherently untrue. And that it contradicts Mage as a gameline with &quot;belief changes reality&quot;. Because if OoR logically doesn't believe these debunked theories, why would they promote them? If they did try to promote them, then their magick shouldn't work. So why would it? </div> </div> </div>I think that misunderstands how the Technocracy views science. They are IMPLEMENTING eugenics and Malthusian economics into the scientific paradigm. Even if they know they could do otherwise, they believe this is the way things should go.<br /> <br /> We know because it lasts until WW2 when the eugenicists get their ass kicked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-13-2021, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:35:18-08:00","id":1439747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439737#post1439737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidebar is dictating One-True-Wayisms on how to play Order of Reason, and it contradicts this very chapter AND the rest of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it's one-true-wayism when it's giving you the option you want too, the rank and file luminary who is trying to do good. And it's not even contradicting the rest of the book, it's just making a statement clear and then the rest of the book gives it more context and different sides. But even with all of that, the truth that it was horribad still stands.<br /> <br /> What it's talking about is a very common and extended way of act and thinking that your White Anglo-Saxon Protestants elites had in that era. And the Order of Reason in the Victorian era is mostly made up with those people and by design (and that is something true through all editions history), they were advocating it. The same can be said about the Hermetics. This is an actual historical situation that needs to be made clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:36:33-08:00","id":1439749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439739#post1439739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit my V:TM experience is influencing me. My general view is VAMPIREDOM is evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we're going to fundamentally disagree at how to look at the rest of the WoD, since I think trying to apply Vampire's themes and tone in any way to the other WoD gamelines fundamentally just...doesn't work.<br /> <br /> (...also Vampire is among my least favorite WoD gamelines sooo...)<br /> <br /> Not that Mage is devoid of horror at all, because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439495#post1439495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Sleepers surprised everyone by doing this themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439499#post1439499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm all in for humans being able to think for themselves, but I could see all of these going on - and I also imagine Disparate would likely be on board even if they can't do a whole lot to make it happen</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I think, is more representative of horror specific to Mage.<br /> <br /> The Sleepers.<br /> <br /> That Sleepers are ultimately the ones who dictate the Consensus, and thus whose magick is going to work or not. Like, there's stuff that even the Technocracy still hasn't gotten Sleepers to accept.<br /> <br /> My favorite being: Life Sphere lets you cure any and all injuries...and diseases. So for any mage that specializes in Life like the Verbena or the Progenitors curing any disease is a snap for them...like cancer or AIDS. And if you choose to run a game in modern times, where things are mostly the same as they are right now (with or without a COVID-19 pandemic) then this would be a time...where while there's a ton of treatments for the above diseases, there's still no cure for those diseases. Which begs the terrifying question:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why is the Consensus not accepting a cure for cancer or AIDS?&quot; </i><br /> <br /> It's less about &quot;whose Paradigm is Better?&quot; and more &quot;what Paradigm is the one that Sleepers want to accept?&quot; And what will mages do, regardless of faction, if they do all the work to try to change the Consensus and reality...but it's one that Sleepers reject.<br /> <br /> THAT is the real horror in Mage.<br /> <br /> (shock of all shocks, no I do not like the answer to be &quot;because the Progenitors/Technocracy is deliberately withdrawing the cure from Sleepers&quot; because that's squicky and awful)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:42:50-08:00","id":1439750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439749#post1439749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(shock of all shocks, no I do not like the answer to be &quot;because the Progenitors/Technocracy is deliberately withdrawing the cure from Sleepers&quot; because that's squicky and awful)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also something that many people in RL would do without being Nephandus or Pentex. Because we have plenty of powerful people who do hold back medicine and life saving resources as of 2021 in our first world democracy.<br /> <br /> I think the problem is, &quot;Are there evil Technocrats?&quot; and &quot;How evil is the Union leadership?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because it's okay to say, &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if they aren't evil, I think that should be Post-Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:06:12-08:00","id":1439754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439746#post1439746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that misunderstands how the Technocracy views science. They are IMPLEMENTING eugenics and Malthusian economics into the scientific paradigm. Even if they know they could do otherwise, they believe this is the way things should go.<br /> <br /> We know because it lasts until WW2 when the eugenicists get their ass kicked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it can't be, because that would suggest that the Technocracy would have to undo their own Consensus changes.<br /> <br /> And no, no I don't buy the idea of the Technocracy being idiots of their own accord that they implement a change to the Consensus that's false and then changing it later. I buy Sleepers being idiots and taking things the wrong way, but not the Technocracy themselves.<br /> <br /> (nvm that the Traditions also would have supported the Axis powers too)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439747#post1439747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it's one-true-wayism when it's giving you the option you want too, the rank and file luminary who is trying to do good. And it's not even contradicting the rest of the book, it's just making a statement clear and then the rest of the book gives it more context and different sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the sidebar on its doesn't seem to have any awareness that the chapter does describe more nuanced takes. The lines I quoted explicitly say that any Luminary that tries to go against the grain will automatically get smashed down, or inevitably ends with them quitting the OoR, which does not match how the OoR is depicted in the rest of the chapter.<br /> <br /> As I said...the impression I get is that the sidebar is written by someone who wasn't one of the actual writers of the chapter, and thus had no context to what was being written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:07:24-08:00","id":1439756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439750#post1439750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if they aren't evil, I think that should be Post-Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except M20 is post-Revised and Victorian Mage is an M20 book...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:08:12-08:00","id":1439757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439756#post1439756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...except M20 is post-Revised and Victorian Mage is an M20 book...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean literally they were evil in universe to the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439754#post1439754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it can't be, because that would suggest that the Technocracy would have to undo their own Consensus changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be rude but that's literally why the Technocracy drove out the Sons of Ether. They rewrote reality so the Ether was no longer accepted science despite being real.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty major plot point.<br /> <br /> We also know they murdered Alan Turning because he was creating the Internet (and I'm sure because some Technocrats were major homophobes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:37:20-08:00","id":1439759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439757#post1439757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean literally they were evil in universe to the Avatar Storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why the Avatar Storm is relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to be rude but that's literally why the Technocracy drove out the Sons of Ether. They rewrote reality so the Ether was no longer accepted science despite being real. </div> </div> </div>...except it's not?<br /> <br /> The Future Fates sidebar says that EE/SoE had a difficult time actually proving Ether exists in their experiments to the other Conventions, and thus was making it hard for them to make a case to make it part of the Consensus. And once again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439749#post1439749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less about &quot;whose Paradigm is Better?&quot; and more &quot;what Paradigm is the one that Sleepers want to accept?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>(also there's some bad writing present in the Ether Future Fates sidebar, but that's neither here nor there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We also know they murdered Alan Turning because he was creating the Internet (and I'm sure because some Technocrats were major homophobes). </div> </div> </div>Fair... although can we not make it about &quot;cause Technocracy hated gays&quot; or at least acknowledge it as bad writing?<br /> <br /> (and on a personal subjective level, I also think making actual historical figures mages is completely ridiculous and stretches credibility of Mage's setting...except for Wraith. That gameline is the only one where I will legitimately buy historical figures appearing in it, because everyone dies and statistically some of them would have had to become wraiths)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:38:28-08:00","id":1439760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439750#post1439750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also something that many people in RL would do without being Nephandus or Pentex. Because we have plenty of powerful people who do hold back medicine and life saving resources as of 2021 in our first world democracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding. Deliberately withholding life-saving medicine is a constant in the real world. It's done for money, for racism, for classism, for straight-up genocide. Just look around you. Millions of people are deliberately denied clean water, clean air, food, and medicine <i>deliberately to kill them</i> every day.<br /> <br /> Non-Nephandi Mages are capable of equal evil. Awakening is not a moral enlightenment. Maybe not even Ascension is a moral enlightenment (although I prefer to believe it is).<br /> <br /> Tasti man, I think you're looking at this as all or nothing. Either all Technocrats are evil, or none of them are. But there's no such thing as &quot;Everyone&quot; or &quot;Nobody&quot; with large groups of humans.<br /> <br /> You aren't prevented from playing a white, scientific Mage who is non-evil. The sidebar that you quote says those characters exist, explicitly. They're a minority, and they're not in charge, but they are playable.<br /> Mages are humans. Technocrats are humans. Whites are humans. All humans have free will. Non-Conditioned Victorian Era Technocrats have <b>unconstrained</b> free will. They can choose to stop committing atrocities <b>any time they want to.</b><br /> <br /> Inevitably, some of them will choose to stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> In real life during the height of chattel slavery and even during the triangle trade, there were white abolitionists on both sides of the Atlantic, risking their lives, facing down death threats and attempted murder to fight evil. My favorite example is William Lloyd Garrison. He spoke the truth plainly, fiercely, fearlessly, day after day after day, after death threats, after mobs attacked and almost killed him, after arson. Nothing stopped him. Nobody could shut him up. He was indomitable. He was a great hero, a man I look up to. And he was a white male, too.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Garrison specifically was a religious man whose moral convictions came from his interpretation of Christianity. But there was nothing stopping a transcendentalist or a secular humanist or a secretly religious Technocrat from coming to the same moral conclusions. There is nothing stopping you from playing one. If you don't want your PC persecuted for being anti-racist &quot;race traitor&quot;, hopefully you can go on gonzo adventures in the Umbra instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-13-2021, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:56:12-08:00","id":1439761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439760#post1439760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it so difficult to believe that Mages are capable of equal evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is not that evil mages don't exist, my point is that the sidebar paints the OoR as the Evil-est, but then still offers them as a playable option, which sends mixed messaging.<br /> <br /> If that was true I would have been criticizing the inclusion of the bits in the Choristor and Hermetic chapter saying that they ride the wave and allow for Victorian ideals to spread to buff up their Paradigms too.<br /> <br /> But I'm not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tasti man, I think you're looking at this as all or nothing. Either all Technocrats are evil, or none of them are </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> No I'm not.<br /> <br /> I'm saying the book is not consistent on what the OoR is. It's trying to say that Technocrats are the Evil-est while also saying they do...while listing all the good and progressive feats they DID contribute to. To rectify this the book would either have to: <br /> <br /> a.) If the book wants to be consistent on &quot;OoR is Evil and enabled Victorian Britain's ideal and power to spread as it did&quot;, in addition to not enabling and attracting bad faith players, then it needs to remove the OoR as a playable faction. Cut that chapter out, re-add them back into the Antagonists chapter with the other NPCs.<br /> <br /> b.) Rewrite the sidebar and select passages to tone back on &quot;OoR is the Evil-est group of mages&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm in support of option B, not because I think the atrocities of the Victorian Era aren't a problem and not worth discussing, but because that'd be the most practical course of action. Option A would require an extensive amount of rewriting and restructuring the whole book, something that I imagine is pretty expensive and time consuming that I would think OPP would rather not do. Option B is the overall better option since that requires a far less extensive amount of rewriting by comparison.<br /> <br /> And overall better for players and STs since it doesn't pigeonhole them into specific stories and characters or guilt-trip them if they attempt to do anything but what that sidebar currently says they should be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T18:58:41-08:00","id":1439762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439757#post1439757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be rude but that's literally why the Technocracy drove out the Sons of Ether. They rewrote reality so the Ether was no longer accepted science despite being real.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, this is another issue that I have with the manuscript. <br /> <br /> First off, I don't buy that the Order had the power to <i>do</i> that. The manuscript's talk about the Union's leadership declaring that the Ether is null and void and all of the sudden Ether Science becomes Catastrophic (or, at best, Uncanny). That's a <i>lot</i> of mojo in a simple decree. If they can do <i>that</i>, what <i>else</i> can they make Catastrophic through a simple \u201cmake it so\u201d? <br /> <br /> It runs counter to everything we've seen in M20 about how much time and effort is needed to alter a single Reality Zone, let alone making a global \u2014 nay, <i>interplanetary</i> \u2014 change. <br /> <br /> I could see that scenario playing out as the Union making a statement of <i>intent</i>, that the future plans for the Union no longer involve Ether and that the Etherites should sit down and shut up. That would still be plenty to outrage the Etherites and lead to them abandoning the Technocracy, especially since they had been growing increasingly dissatisfied with the Union anyway. <br /> <br /> And while I'm on the subject, there are a few other things about the treatment of the Etherites in this book that I take issue with. I've always had it as a bit of head-canon that the issue that drive the Etherites or of the Union wasn't <i>actually</i> the Union's rejection of the Lumineferous Ether; that was merely the straw that broke the camel's back, and the standard that they rallied around. The <i>actual</i> bone of contention was the Technocracy's adoption of Reductionism \u2014 or, phrased another way, \u201cOne True Way-ism\u201d \u2014 as its official policy. And rather than the trigger being the Lumineferous Ether, per se, the real trigger was the introduction of Tychoidean Cosmology and the beginning of the Void Engineers\u2019 efforts to isolate Etherspace from Conventional Space. Lumineferous Ether was merely the first step to the Electrodyne Engineers' plans to introduce the notion of Etherspace (and other related concepts) to the Masses, making space travel <i>easier</i>; and the Technocracy slammed the door on those plans. <br /> <br /> In comparison to that, the reason given for their parting in Victorian Mage feels\u2026 bland and uninspired. <br /> <br /> I'm also not terribly fond of the idea that they had been calling themselves the Society of Ether all along; I rather like the idea of them choosing to rename themselves as a reminder of what the Technocracy attempted to take away from them. <br /> <br /> *ahem* Sorry about that. It's something that's a bit of a pet peeve for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:05:43-08:00","id":1439763,"title":"","content":"Oh, the Ether Future Fates sidebar has some questionable writing in general.<br /> <br /> And your point also standing on: \u201cIf the Technocracy has that much power over the Consensus to purge Ether from it ... why haven\u2019t they already won the Ascension War?\u201d <br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me started on the Fate that talks about the Kopa Loei taking the Seat of Matter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:14:08-08:00","id":1439764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439759#post1439759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why the Avatar Storm is relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking in Doylean terms: before and after MRev was published. CTPhipps is presenting it in Watsonian terms: before and after the Avatar Storm isolated the Union from Control and gave the rank and file a shot at reforming the Union. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439759#post1439759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and on a personal subjective level, I also think making actual historical figures mages is completely ridiculous and stretches credibility of Mage's setting...except for Wraith. That gameline is the only one where I will legitimately buy historical figures appearing in it, because everyone dies and statistically some of them would have had to become wraiths)</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree with this \u2014 though it's too late in a handful of cases, as Alan Turing has been established as having been not just a Virtual Adept, but also <i>the</i> Virtual Adept who discovered (some say created) the Digital Web, as far back as the original VA Tradbook back in the early 90s. <br /> <br /> That said, Mage has been surprisingly good about this: Einstein wasn't a mage, despite his two biggest innovations being pivotal to Mage history (specifically, Special Relativity and Quantum Physics). Prince Albert and Queen Victoria play key and active roles in the formation of the Technocratic Union; but neither of them is Awakened. The book doesn't say that Babbage or Lovelace were Awakened; but they were central to bringing the Difference Engineers into existence. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:18:40-08:00","id":1439765,"title":"","content":"Mind you, Mage is the one game where brilliant inventors and artists being supernaturals wouldn't necessarily change them the way being vampires or shifters would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:19:12-08:00","id":1439766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439763#post1439763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t get me started on the Fate that talks about the Kopa Loei taking the Seat of Matter...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, please do. There are several other Crafts that would be <i>far</i> better suited to take the Seat of Matter than the Kopa Loei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:58:25-08:00","id":1439771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439766#post1439766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, please do. There are several other Crafts that would be <i>far</i> better suited to take the Seat of Matter than the Kopa Loei.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty-then, SO<br /> <br /> So naturally one of the Future Fates discussed is &quot;What if the Technocracy DID accept Ether and thus the SoE stayed with the Technocracy?&quot; One of the knock on effects being &quot;ok, then what Craft steps up to take the Seat of Matter on the Traditions if the SoE takes it?&quot; This Fate's answer...is the Kopa Loei. And that it goes on to say that with a bunch of Etherships in the Technocracy's battle fleet, that they're able to crush the Kopa Loei enough in the Pacific that they're forced to flee into the security of the Traditions and accept the Seat.<br /> <br /> There are several issues with this:<br /> <br /> 1.<b> Kopa Loei don't have an Affinity Sphere.</b> Or at least, not one that the whole group agrees upon. This is backed up by not just their M20 core write up, but also their VM write-up they get in the next chapter. So why would they even take one of the Tradition Seats in the first place, let alone the Seat of Matter?<br /> <br /> 2. Canonically speaking...<b>IC the Kopa Loei reject the concept of Spheres</b>. They dismiss it as Hermetic nonsense and refuse to entertain anyone who brings it up. So why would they accept something they <i>definitely</i> do not believe in?<br /> <br /> 3. The Fate is trying to insinuate when it comes to Etherites staying on...<b>that Etherships were apparently the decisive factor in razing the Kopa Loei</b>? Like...was it really just about having more or a different kind of airships to fight them with? Because if it's about fighting in mundane reality...the OoR already has Voidships. Nothing strikes me as Etherships being easier to adapt to flying around in mundane skies over Voidships. I'm not sure if it's trying to imply that the Kopa Loei tried to flee into Etherspace/Deep Umbra and only the Etherships could chase them there but, that's not made clear in the text at all. And even if it was, again...they already have Voidships. So Etherships still shouldn't matter.<br /> <br /> Nvm that in the canonical timeline, KL still would have had to have colonial violence happen to them, so logically they would have been put in a similar place, and it's weird that this Fate singles out the KL specifically and not the...other Crafts?<br /> <br /> And, this is admittedly my personal interpretation: to me, the Kopa Loei were always characterized as being very isolationist and stubborn. That they would rather die then to ever allow themselves to be shackled or owed to a larger magickal organization. So to me, them throwing in the towel and seeking safety with the Traditions is OOC from them.<br /> <br /> (and yes, I know them being in the Disparates is a Thing, but I also think the Disparates as a concept makes no sense, so my point still stands. but that's neither here nor there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-13-2021, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:09:12-08:00","id":1439772,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that in MRev, they <i>did</i> die rather than seek refuge in the Traditions: you got a House Solificati in the Order of Hermes, a Templar faction in the Celestial Chorus, a Sisters of Hypollyta faction in the Verbenae (IIRC), and so on; but the Kopa Loei? They got wiped out. Their existence in M20 is a retcon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:15:38-08:00","id":1439773,"title":"","content":"Did they? Didn't the survivors end up just joining the Dreamspeakers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:16:12-08:00","id":1439774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439762#post1439762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, this is another issue that I have with the manuscript.<br /> <br /> First off, I don't buy that the Order had the power to <i>do</i> that. The manuscript's talk about the Union's leadership declaring that the Ether is null and void and all of the sudden Ether Science becomes Catastrophic (or, at best, Uncanny). That's a <i>lot</i> of mojo in a simple decree. If they can do <i>that</i>, what <i>else</i> can they make Catastrophic through a simple \u201cmake it so\u201d?<br /> <br /> It runs counter to everything we've seen in M20 about how much time and effort is needed to alter a single Reality Zone, let alone making a global \u2014 nay, <i>interplanetary</i> \u2014 change.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's always been a problem with synergizing Mage history with real history: the Technocracy is wildly successful whenever history turns the page, so to speak, about some theory or way of thinking, and a miserable failure when it doesn't, and the result is a wild inconsistancy about the power of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The reality is that ether was simply replaced with better science. People who clung to that theory were dismissed as kooks because there WERE, in fact, kooks.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, people have mostly clung to religion not because the Celestial Chorus are amazingly effective at fighting the Technocracy, but because people still die and want some pretty lies about the afterlife to comfort them, and because religious beliefs don't fundamentally prevent technological progress and so don't get darwinned out by technologically superior forces.<br /> <br /> Mage fictional history has to be written around these historical/sociological forces. So the Technocracy is godlike except when it's a miserable failure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:24:40-08:00","id":1439775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439774#post1439774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's always been a problem with synergizing Mage history with real history: the Technocracy is wildly successful whenever history turns the page, so to speak, about some theory or way of thinking, and a miserable failure when it doesn't, and the result is a wild inconsistancy about the power of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The reality is that ether was simply replaced with better science. People who clung to that theory were dismissed as kooks because there WERE, in fact, kooks.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, people have mostly clung to religion not because the Celestial Chorus are amazingly effective at fighting the Technocracy, but because people still die and want some pretty lies about the afterlife to comfort them, and because religious beliefs don't fundamentally prevent technological progress and so don't get darwinned out by technologically superior forces.<br /> <br /> Mage fictional history has to be written around these historical/sociological forces. So the Technocracy is godlike except when it's a miserable failure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> In order for the Technocracy to make sense it would have to be that they're NOT in complete control of things. They have some influence and power, just not so much that they can sweep the Ascension War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:30:03-08:00","id":1439776,"title":"","content":"If I was sitting down with a Mage ST for the first time and they asked me what mood I'd prefer, I'd ask for a somewhat more-hopeful-than-Revised-canon game where Mysticks aren't hunted like dogs and the Technocracy doesn't actually own the entire Earth. Then again I'd also ask for the Avatar Storm to let up finally, and for Horizon to keep existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T20:38:30-08:00","id":1439777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439774#post1439774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's always been a problem with synergizing Mage history with real history: the Technocracy is wildly successful whenever history turns the page, so to speak, about some theory or way of thinking, and a miserable failure when it doesn't, and the result is a wild inconsistancy about the power of the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this completely missed the point I was making. While there's some validity to asking that Mage at least present the <i>appearance</i> of being consistent with the real world, if only because the base conceit of the World of Darkness is \u201clike our world, but darker\u201d, the <i>real</i> issue here is a lack of internal consistency. Part 3 goes to great lengths to point out how difficult it is to turn a Territory Technocratic, with talk about how you need to convince the locals to adopt your views or you need to remove them; and then it turns around and makes a change on a much larger scale without doing <i>any</i> of that. <br /> <br /> Even my earlier talk about embedded Negation Men allowing the earliest victories of the Anglo-Zulu War et al don't entirely negate the need to put in the hard work of flipping the Territory; it merely provides a way to temporarily, and very locally, override the local Territory's Focus with the Technocratic Focus long enough for the shock and awe to set in. To suddenly wipe out the Ether the way the book describes would require something more akin to an organized and coordinated <i>army</i> of Negation Men. And I have never proposed that the Union has anything even remotely like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-09-2022, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:04:23-08:00","id":1439778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439777#post1439777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this completely missed the point I was making. While there's some validity to asking that Mage at least present the <i>appearance</i> of being consistent with the real world, if only because the base conceit of the World of Darkness is \u201clike our world, but darker\u201d, the <i>real</i> issue here is a lack of internal consistency..</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understood your point perfectly. I was merely explaining why that point can never, ever be resolved. It is a plothole in the game's conceit that is inherently unfixable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:12:27-08:00","id":1439779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439778#post1439778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I understood your point perfectly. I was merely explaining why that point can never, ever be resolved. It is a plothole in the game's conceit that is inherently unfixable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not completely, no. But that doesn't mean that we shouldn't <i>try</i>. And we can definitely do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:26:40-08:00","id":1439780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439775#post1439775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bingo.<br /> <br /> In order for the Technocracy to make sense it would have to be that they're NOT in complete control of things. They have some influence and power, just not so much that they can sweep the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I strongly disagree. The Technocracy is entirely consistent if it is used as a conquering enslaving embodiment of Western hegemony. The problem is if you want to make them more nuanced idealists like later books that are devoted to a higher ideal.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want to make them the good guys.<br /> <br /> The gameline created them with the idea that they are meant to be the Knights Templar from Assassins Creed and primarily antagonists. Writing them as misunderstood heroes is a VERY difficult prospect then but not impossible as you can have them fighting uphill the entire time.<br /> <br /> But you must make the decision before you start the game. One or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:44:34-08:00","id":1439782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439780#post1439780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I strongly disagree. The Technocracy is entirely consistent if it is used as a conquering enslaving embodiment of Western hegemony.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I strongly disagree with that notion is well and find that the gameline moving away from Mage 1e\u2019s direction was the right call to make. Aside from my already documented thoughts on the mistake of tying them to mainstream science, I don\u2019t think the game\u2019s setting and mechanics supports having Mage 1e and just blows open holes in the setting and the mechanics. <br /> <br /> Besides if I wanted to do a game about a supernatural war against an all seeing authoritarian force, I\u2019d play Demon: the Descent <br /> <br /> At least that game\u2019s consistent with how by RAW, bans playable angels as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T21:49:12-08:00","id":1439783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439782#post1439782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I strongly disagree with that notion is well and find that the gameline moving away from Mage 1e\u2019s direction was the right call to make. Aside from my already documented thoughts on the mistake of tying them to mainstream science, I don\u2019t think the game\u2019s setting and mechanics supports having Mage 1e and just blows open holes in the setting and the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Besides if I wanted to do a game about a supernatural war against an all seeing authoritarian force, I\u2019d play Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> At least that game\u2019s consistent with how by RAW, bans playable angels as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine but I've run many games about the plucky resistance against fascists. I do Revised games but I make Threat Null into the New Technocracy because we need fascists to fight.<br /> <br /> It's the purpose of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> YMMV but that's how I feel about my games. For me, it's about throwing lightning bolts at the worst of society. I feel Victorian Mage would be doubly so that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0NGtY2wPva4\" data-code=\"0NGtY2wPva4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0NGtY2wPva4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T07:36:48-07:00","id":1439809,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that Revised and M20 also have the Loyalists and the Panopticon if you want Big Brother Technocracy. They are there, they are still part of the Union (unlike Threat Null) and they still have a lot of power and influence inside it. And that's the Revised/M20 canon with a more nuanced Union.<br /> <br /> If anything I feel that Threat Null now represents the 1e Union, Loyalists/Panopticon represents the 2e Union and the Utopians/Friends of Courage are the new guys who want to clean house. And having all those options is what makes the modern Technocracy interesting. Because the Technocracy represents a lot of things and just making them suddenly go full good progressive kind of destroys the conflicts that actually make them interesting as a faction (Security vs Freedom, Utilitarianism vs Idealism).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 03-14-2021, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T08:31:26-07:00","id":1439813,"title":"","content":"Two new stretch goals have been added: expanding Unusual Characters, and creating assets for VTT play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T08:48:08-07:00","id":1439816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439809#post1439809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that Revised and M20 also have the Loyalists and the Panopticon if you want Big Brother Technocracy. They are there, they are still part of the Union (unlike Threat Null) and they still have a lot of power and influence inside it. And that's the Revised/M20 canon with a more nuanced Union.<br /> <br /> If anything I feel that Threat Null now represents the 1e Union, Loyalists/Panopticon represents the 2e Union and the Utopians/Friends of Courage are the new guys who want to clean house. And having all those options is what makes the modern Technocracy interesting. Because the Technocracy represents a lot of things and just making them suddenly go full good progressive kind of destroys the conflicts that actually make them interesting as a faction (Security vs Freedom, Utilitarianism vs Idealism).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; more options on different ways to play the Union are always a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T09:08:50-07:00","id":1439821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439813#post1439813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two new stretch goals have been added: expanding Unusual Characters, and creating assets for VTT play.</div> </div> </div> </div>...still underwhelming as hell as Stretch Goals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:01:29-07:00","id":1439829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439809#post1439809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that Revised and M20 also have the Loyalists and the Panopticon if you want Big Brother Technocracy. They are there, they are still part of the Union (unlike Threat Null) and they still have a lot of power and influence inside it. And that's the Revised/M20 canon with a more nuanced Union.<br /> <br /> If anything I feel that Threat Null now represents the 1e Union, Loyalists/Panopticon represents the 2e Union and the Utopians/Friends of Courage are the new guys who want to clean house. And having all those options is what makes the modern Technocracy interesting. Because the Technocracy represents a lot of things and just making them suddenly go full good progressive kind of destroys the conflicts that actually make them interesting as a faction (Security vs Freedom, Utilitarianism vs Idealism).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I see Threat Null as the worst of the Technocracy, completely divorced from their Humanity and everything cranked up to eleven, beyond even what 1E Technocracy was. Which is why they work better as the eldritch things beyond the Veil than as the Technocracy on Earth.<br /> <br /> The 2E saw Guide to the Technocracy which brought real nuance to the Union. The divide between the Utopians and the Loyalists/Panopticon embodies that. I say if you want to have Technocrats more in line with the 1E, I'd use the Nephandi infiltrators of the Union for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:15:38-07:00","id":1439831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439829#post1439829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I see Threat Null as the worst of the Technocracy, completely divorced from their Humanity and everything cranked up to eleven, beyond even what 1E Technocracy was. Which is why they work better as the eldritch things beyond the Veil than as the Technocracy on Earth.<br /> <br /> The 2E saw Guide to the Technocracy which brought real nuance to the Union. The divide between the Utopians and the Loyalists/Panopticon embodies that. I say if you want to have Technocrats more in line with the 1E, I'd use the Nephandi infiltrators of the Union for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nephandi believe in NothingTM. Not nothing but NothingTM.<br /> <br /> 1st Edition Technocrats believe in a boot on the face of humanity forever.<br /> <br /> You can't really combine them well.<br /> <br /> I'd like Threat Null to be expanded so the TOP are Eldrifch Abominations but the bottom are Technocrats EAGER to follow them. Which is the REAL reason that the VE haven't written in everyone.<br /> <br /> Because they know that plenty of the Union would happily accept slavery and fascism if it meant they were no longer the underdogs.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is just the Seers of the Throne but the Seers WORK in regular mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-14-2021, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:39:02-07:00","id":1439841,"title":"","content":"\u2026and as much as I enjoy discussions about Threat Null, would it be out of line to suggest that the \u201cTechnocracy in Star Trek\u201d thread might be a better place to do so? After all, Threat Null didn't come into existence until a full century after the end of the Victorian age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:41:11-07:00","id":1439843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439841#post1439841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and as much as I enjoy discussions about Threat Null, would it be out of line to suggest that the \u201cTechnocracy in Star Trek\u201d thread might be a better place to do so? After all, Threat Null didn't come into existence until a full century after the end of the Victorian age.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd like to see about the Victorian Era that may be too removed from reality is the Order of Reason(s) joining together.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Five Metal Dragons have been Technocrats and oppressive legalists for 3000 years. They predate the Order of Reason by millennia and probably have 3 members for every 1 of the Union. So the Order of Reason makes them an offer, &quot;You can control China. Just help us murder all these Reality Deviants.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Order of Reason Europe thinks they've fooled the locals into serving them.<br /> <br /> But the Chinese Technocrats realize the Europeans have joined THEM.<br /> <br /> Maybe something similar in Japan and India.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:59:01-07:00","id":1439848,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't consider that to be a Victorian age thing. It clearly happened sometime before the present, but in the Victorian age these various technomancer groups were very much at each other's throats.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see would be a look at the African technomancers. There's an implication that they didn't get wiped out, and very likely did not end up joining the Order of Reason. And as such, they potentially still exist in the present day as an overlooked Craft.<br /> <br /> They're mentioned in the manuscript already, under the race to Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T11:13:35-07:00","id":1439850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439848#post1439848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't consider that to be a Victorian age thing. It clearly happened sometime before the present, but in the Victorian age these various technomancer groups were very much at each other's throats.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see would be a look at the African technomancers. There's an implication that they didn't get wiped out, and very likely did not end up joining the Order of Reason. And as such, they potentially still exist in the present day as an overlooked Craft.<br /> <br /> They're mentioned in the manuscript already, under the race to Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is especially a damn shame since more African Crafts are great appreciated. And doubly so if they're a technomancer Craft.<br /> <br /> Since as is we still only have the Ngoma as an African Craft that's been given any sort of write-up and it's...awkward for them to be the only Craft representing an entire continent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T11:35:16-07:00","id":1439860,"title":"","content":"If it's not something that can be added to the manuscript, that would be a decent stretch goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:29:11-07:00","id":1439897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439843#post1439843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd like to see about the Victorian Era that may be too removed from reality is the Order of Reason(s) joining together.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Five Metal Dragons have been Technocrats and oppressive legalists for 3000 years. They predate the Order of Reason by millennia and probably have 3 members for every 1 of the Union. So the Order of Reason makes them an offer, &quot;You can control China. Just help us murder all these Reality Deviants.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Order of Reason Europe thinks they've fooled the locals into serving them.<br /> <br /> But the Chinese Technocrats realize the Europeans have joined THEM.<br /> <br /> Maybe something similar in Japan and India.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assimilation is implied by the text to be what the OoR using its imperial power position to do with the other techno/social order factions, with even those resisiting becoming more like them in order to resist (this is specifically what\u2019s happening with the Jidai, as is keeping with the spirit of the Meiji Restoration - becoming more like a Western power to resist the Western powers).<br /> <br /> I assume the Union will eat the MMM after WW1, and the Jidai after WW2. But yeah more on the uniting of the Dalou\u2019laoshi with the Union and whatever is going on with Indian technomancers would be great (I have some thoughts but I want to hear back from an Indian consult before I share them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:34:08-07:00","id":1439899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439782#post1439782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I strongly disagree with that notion is well and find that the gameline moving away from Mage 1e\u2019s direction was the right call to make. Aside from my already documented thoughts on the mistake of tying them to mainstream science, I don\u2019t think the game\u2019s setting and mechanics supports having Mage 1e and just blows open holes in the setting and the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Besides if I wanted to do a game about a supernatural war against an all seeing authoritarian force, I\u2019d play Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> At least that game\u2019s consistent with how by RAW, bans playable angels as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Them \u201cmoving away from that\u201d is framed as the Union changing in-universe though, the Victorian Union <b><i>already</i></b> being the Neo-Daedalen idealists that arise with the Earthside young agents who believe in the ideals they were fed in propaganda rather than Control\u2019s real agenda would contradict the established canon of the very shift you are referencing.<br /> <br /> the once idealistic Order of Reason\u2019s transition to the repressive authoritarian Technocratic Union is something that specifically happens in the context of Western imperialism corrupting the ideals of the Enlightenment. There\u2019s a reason the Craftmasons who were supporting those ideals got taken out in 1670.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-14-2021, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:27:44-07:00","id":1439904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439850#post1439850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is especially a damn shame since more African Crafts are great appreciated. And doubly so if they're a technomancer Craft.<br /> <br /> Since as is we still only have the Ngoma as an African Craft that's been given any sort of write-up and it's...awkward for them to be the only Craft representing an entire continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at least we have the Madzimbabwe, the Uzoma, the Baruti and the Izinyanga inside the Traditions. And we got a write-up for the Zulu Mechanists here in Victorian Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:52:46-07:00","id":1439910,"title":"","content":"Right. But they aren't the technomancers that were being referred to in the race to Africa section. Those ones pre-existed the Anglo Zulu War, whereas the Zulu mechanists were the result of said war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:59:46-07:00","id":1439912,"title":"","content":"Who are the Izinyanga (or Isinyanga?) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:15:42-07:00","id":1439917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439912#post1439912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the Izinyanga (or Isinyanga?) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Zulu Verbenae from Guide to the Traditions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:44:20-07:00","id":1439934,"title":"","content":"So there're three-four groups in southern Africa, a few groups in Egypt, and a few groups in West Africa... and really nobody in the rest of the continent?<br /> <br /> Wasn't there also a group of Technomancers who came from Timbuktu at some point?<br /> <br /> I'd expect the Swahili Coast communities to have produced a complex mixture of many different beliefs and practices - it's an intersection of coastal and inland East African, Somali, southeast African, Arab, Malagasy, and South Asian cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-14-2021, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T22:54:38-07:00","id":1439978,"title":"","content":"Something else that sticks out to me regarding the OoR chapter:<br /> <br /> I've pointedly noticed that this chapter has WAY more Future Fates then the Traditions chapter or the Crafts chapter. I point that out because the OoR FFs go into alternate structures for the Technocracy, and of course the FF that describes on what if Etherites stayed with the Union. And past texts have referenced &quot;what-if&quot; possibilities of different Crafts that join the Traditions instead of SoE and AR/VAs...but thus far those hunks of text are nowhere to be found in their respective chapters.<br /> <br /> Normally I would have dismissed this as those FFs being saved for the Storytelling chapter...but considering that the OoR has these FFs and not the Traditions and Crafts chapter it just seems...bizarre and not consistent.<br /> <br /> (also the Autochtonia FF is ridiculous in suggesting that the mega-computer that it is gets slower over time as it became more advanced because...that's not how computers work. the reverse should be happening)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T23:35:41-07:00","id":1439980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439934#post1439934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there're three-four groups in southern Africa, a few groups in Egypt, and a few groups in West Africa... and really nobody in the rest of the continent?<br /> <br /> Wasn't there also a group of Technomancers who came from Timbuktu at some point?<br /> <br /> I'd expect the Swahili Coast communities to have produced a complex mixture of many different beliefs and practices - it's an intersection of coastal and inland East African, Somali, southeast African, Arab, Malagasy, and South Asian cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the OoR chapter did mention the Void Seekers encountering two Central African confederations of Willworkers with Beliefs not entirely incompatible with the Order's, the Awalaye and Wamukamwami. Unfortunately the rest of the Order learned this after the Seekers attacked and pillaged several of these African Technomancers' chantries, preventing any future talks with them.<br /> <br /> Frankly with how big Africa is, it's one of those things that would at the bare minimum require an entire Chapter in a supplement if not an entire book dedicated to it. The three purely African Crafts we got were there for a reason. The Bata'a and the Ngoma will survive into the modern day and would become founding members of the Disparate Alliance* while the Zulu Mechanists were created to show that there were Technomancers besides the OoR.<br /> <br /> *Though it does raise the question of where the Solificati are as all the other future founders of the Alliance are present in VAM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439978#post1439978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else that sticks out to me regarding the OoR chapter:<br /> <br /> I've pointedly noticed that this chapter has WAY more Future Fates then the Traditions chapter or the Crafts chapter. I point that out because the OoR FFs go into alternate structures for the Technocracy, and of course the FF that describes on what if Etherites stayed with the Union. And past texts have referenced &quot;what-if&quot; possibilities of different Crafts that join the Traditions instead of SoE and AR/VAs...but thus far those hunks of text are nowhere to be found in their respective chapters.<br /> <br /> Normally I would have dismissed this as those FFs being saved for the Storytelling chapter...but considering that the OoR has these FFs and not the Traditions and Crafts chapter it just seems...bizarre and not consistent.<br /> <br /> (also the Autochtonia FF is ridiculous in suggesting that the mega-computer that it is gets slower over time as it became more advanced because...that's not how computers work. the reverse should be happening)</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely because there are several important variables for the future surrounding the Order that Traditions and Crafts don't have. Namely how successful the Reforms will be and what will be the status of it's future defectors. For the Traditions there's really only who's going to fill the missing Matter Seat and Correspondence Seat should the Batini leave, assuming the SoE and VA aren't available.<br /> <br /> I think the only reason the Boxer Rebellion gets the attention it does is that it's a notable conflict during the era that could be used for alt history without too much suspension of disbelief and gives a bit of attention to a place not under the thumb of the British Empire. Well not entirely anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T03:50:27-07:00","id":1439998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439980#post1439980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the OoR chapter did mention the Void Seekers encountering two Central African confederations of Willworkers with Beliefs not entirely incompatible with the Order's, the Awalaye and Wamukamwami. Unfortunately the rest of the Order learned this after the Seekers attacked and pillaged several of these African Technomancers' chantries, preventing any future talks with them.<br /> <br /> Frankly with how big Africa is, it's one of those things that would at the bare minimum require an entire Chapter in a supplement if not an entire book dedicated to it. The three purely African Crafts we got were there for a reason. The Bata'a and the Ngoma will survive into the modern day and would become founding members of the Disparate Alliance* while the Zulu Mechanists were created to show that there were Technomancers besides the OoR.<br /> <br /> *Though it does raise the question of where the Solificati are as all the other future founders of the Alliance are present in VAM.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Knights Templar (seeing as how they lost their ability to hide in the Order of Reason when the Cabal of Pure Thought was wiped out), and I don't recall seeing the Sisters of Hypollyta, either. The Solificati wouldn't be considered for the Seat of Matter despite being perfect for it, because Heylel. <br /> <br /> The Zulu mechanists are all well and good; but the interesting thing about the Awalaye and Wamukamwami is that they were technomancers, too; and not in reaction to the Order the way the Zulu mechanists were. One of them was described as knowing secrets about the Ether that the Electrodyne Engineers didn't know, and that being a be sufficient reason why the EEs were pissed that the Void Seekers attacked them. Central Africans, technomancers, and technomancers in their own right rather than as a response to the Union. I really don't see why they weren't given a write-up of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:13:38-07:00","id":1440018,"title":"","content":"Speculation towards chapter 8; any one think we will see anything of Dr Gull and his associates who form the body of Her Majesty's Agents, who work to protect the Queen from the supernatural? (or at least they do in <i>Victorian Age Vampire</i>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T06:32:49-07:00","id":1440021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439978#post1439978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(also the Autochtonia FF is ridiculous in suggesting that the mega-computer that it is gets slower over time as it became more advanced because...that's not how computers work. the reverse should be happening)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it says that at first it took longer for the increasingly more complex iterations, but ultimately the &quot;engine began generating and completing iterations faster than Al-Sharif was able to count&quot;. So by the end it was going faster and faster.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T07:35:48-07:00","id":1440028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439998#post1439998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Knights Templar (seeing as how they lost their ability to hide in the Order of Reason when the Cabal of Pure Thought was wiped out), and I don't recall seeing the Sisters of Hypollyta, either. The Solificati wouldn't be considered for the Seat of Matter despite being perfect for it, because Heylel.<br /> <br /> The Zulu mechanists are all well and good; but the interesting thing about the Awalaye and Wamukamwami is that they were technomancers, too; and not in reaction to the Order the way the Zulu mechanists were. One of them was described as knowing secrets about the Ether that the Electrodyne Engineers didn't know, and that being a be sufficient reason why the EEs were pissed that the Void Seekers attacked them. Central Africans, technomancers, and technomancers in their own right rather than as a response to the Union. I really don't see why they weren't given a write-up of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are five founding members of the Disparate Alliance, the Batini, the Bata'a, the Ngoma, the Hollow Ones and the Solificati. Everyone else joined afterwards. <br /> <br /> I wasn't referring to the Solificati for potential groups to fill the vacant seat, I was referring to them not being a playable option while the rest of the other Alliance Founders are playable in VAM. In fact, they and the Templars are the only M20 Crafts not in VAM.<br /> <br /> The Sisters of Hippolyta are in VAM, in the Wardens of a World of Magick section of the Craft Chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T08:49:45-07:00","id":1440360,"title":"","content":"Fourth manuscript excerpt now up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T11:18:26-07:00","id":1440365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440360#post1440360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth manuscript excerpt now up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there somewhere the public can see this, or is it only for donors?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T11:33:35-07:00","id":1440367,"title":"","content":"Like all their KS manuscripts, they're backers only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T14:58:16-07:00","id":1440388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440365#post1440365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there somewhere the public can see this, or is it only for donors?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some material is previewed on the various updates (visit the <a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/victorian-mage-ttrpg/x/7052323#/\" target=\"_blank\">Indiegogo</a> page and hit the Updates tab), but the full manuscripts are available only to project backers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T15:18:33-07:00","id":1440389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440028#post1440028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are five founding members of the Disparate Alliance, the Batini, the Bata'a, the Ngoma, the Hollow Ones and the Solificati. Everyone else joined afterwards. <br /> <br /> I wasn't referring to the Solificati for potential groups to fill the vacant seat, I was referring to them not being a playable option while the rest of the other Alliance Founders are playable in VAM. In fact, they and the Templars are the only M20 Crafts not in VAM.<br /> <br /> The Sisters of Hippolyta are in VAM, in the Wardens of a World of Magick section of the Craft Chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of Knowledge history portrays this as being one of their big blank spaces in their history including others knowledge of them. They may straight up not have any current practitioners, some later Orphans picking up the identity from past members paradigmatic theorem writings. Most Western alchemists are going to be Hermetics, with the mind bending experimenters also overlapping with the ecstatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T22:32:48-07:00","id":1440409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440389#post1440389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Children of Knowledge history portrays this as being one of their big blank spaces in their history including others knowledge of them. They may straight up not have any current practitioners, some later Orphans picking up the identity from past members paradigmatic theorem writings. Most Western alchemists are going to be Hermetics, with the mind bending experimenters also overlapping with the ecstatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually their original write-up in the Book of Crafts talks about how while they did go into decline following the Great Betrayal and them leaving the Traditions, becoming the Children of Knowledge, the Industrial Revolution, this era saw them beginning their return. The guilt over the Great Betrayal has not just past but members were realizing that there was more to Heylel's actions, a purpose to it. A notion that would lead to their theory of the Tenth Sphere, Unity.<br /> <br /> M20 doesn't actually contradict that. It talks about how they were around, that while many thought then gone like you suggested, the reality was that they had just gone underground until the 1950s. Which too lines up with the Book of Crafts.<br /> <br /> And admittedly that is the only reason I can think of for not including them, that they are keeping a low profile. But at the same time we're in the middle of their transition phase between the old Solificati of Sorcerer's Crusade to the modern Solificati/Children of Knowledge. Throw in Alchemy's last gasp, the rise of Chemistry and modern recreational drugs, and we have an interesting time for them.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a shame to exclude them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:49:35-07:00","id":1440562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439980#post1439980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likely because there are several important variables for the future surrounding the Order that Traditions and Crafts don't have. Namely how successful the Reforms will be and what will be the status of it's future defectors. For the Traditions there's really only who's going to fill the missing Matter Seat and Correspondence Seat should the Batini leave, assuming the SoE and VA aren't available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well TBH, even the OoR FFs that we do have don't have very well written &quot;variables&quot; to explain their courses of actions.<br /> <br /> -The FF for &quot;the OoR and Union split and exist as separate entities&quot; only explains the Grand Faculty and League of Constructors being opposed to each, but gives no context on why the other Blocs/Convention goes to one faction over the other.<br /> <br /> -There's these weird asides about WWI that aren't given any additional context. In &quot;the OoR and Union splits&quot; they mention that their bickering makes WWI worse and possibly start earlier. And in &quot;the Union is super united&quot; they talk about how &quot;improvements to communication and travel&quot; could have helped stop WWI from happening...but gives no further explanation how that works.<br /> <br /> At least it didn't quite go all the way and suggest &quot;if the Union was this united they could have stopped Archduke Ferdinand from being assassinated!&quot;<br /> <br /> -Nvm that we technically already have a bit explaining how the Kopa Loei could take the Seat of Matter (it being badly written aside).<br /> <br /> And even then...I don't think it would eat up that much wordcount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440021#post1440021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it says that at first it took longer for the increasingly more complex iterations, but ultimately the &quot;engine began generating and completing iterations faster than Al-Sharif was able to count&quot;. So by the end it was going faster and faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still shouldn't have taken a long time to process each iteration at all period. It should have been getting faster period, not get slower at first and THEN speed up.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Anyways, done with Crafts chapter.<br /> <br /> -The Hollow Ones write up is bizarre...because this has very little resemblance to the modern day Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> Retcons for why they're called &quot;Hollow Ones&quot; aside (like seriously, even the M20 core write-up implies them being formed out of the &quot;Lost Generation&quot;...a movement post-WWI, almost TWO DECADES after the Victorian era ended!) the write-up describes a group of working class and low-middle class peoples (which would ironically mean they'd get along with the Brotherhood of Mechanicians) split between Marxists and Theosophists. Which...yeah that's actually a really cool idea to have, essentially, a &quot;privileged ally&quot; Craft. They WANT to help marginalized folks, but they have a hard time seeing past their own inherent biases. But...I do not see the modern day Hollow Ones in this Craft at all.<br /> <br /> The weirdest thing is how much the write-up just...chooses not to say anything about the Romanticism or Gothic movements, two literature movements that were integral foundations to the whole Craft. It *hints* at Romanticism when it mentions how &quot;hollow&quot; they felt at the humdrumness brought about by living in the Industrial Revolution and wanted something more. But it just...doesn't want to put its foot down and actually call it Romanticism. And I...really can't think of any reason why the write-up wouldn't mention that.<br /> <br /> No mention at all of Gothic literature is incredibly weird since...the Victorian era produced some of the most influential Gothic writers of the time. The works of Charles Dickens. Mary Shelley and &quot;Frankenstein&quot;...and Edgar Allen freakin' Poe. So it's weird that this is glossed over in the Hollow One write-ups.<br /> <br /> Naturally the write-up does not say anything about how the Victorian Hollow Ones transitioned into the modern day incarnation.<br /> <br /> -The Sisters and Bata'a write-ups I do like how it acknowledges that bigotry and prejudice within progressive movements is a Thing that happens, and that it's an issue that they have to confront. That I can definitely dig on getting into the messy and complicated nuances of progressive movements. Way more then I can buy the idea of VM-Dreamspeakers being...unanimous and united at combating colonialism and don't see an issue with a bunch of them being of completely different races or cultures.<br /> <br /> -I mean, we have the Comanche Puha right there, as a Native American Craft, that specifically refused to join the DSs.<br /> <br /> -...yeah I can accept the Wulong being a victim of their own arrogance and not initially taking the intrusion of Western empires into China seriously, lol.<br /> <br /> -Conversely, while I'm glad &quot;Jidai&quot; (terrible name) is there...still annoyed we don't really have an officially written up mystical Japanese Craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-19-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:33:06-07:00","id":1440630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440562#post1440562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well TBH, even the OoR FFs that we do have don't have very well written &quot;variables&quot; to explain their courses of actions.<br /> <br /> -The FF for &quot;the OoR and Union split and exist as separate entities&quot; only explains the Grand Faculty and League of Constructors being opposed to each, but gives no context on why the other Blocs/Convention goes to one faction over the other.<br /> <br /> -There's these weird asides about WWI that aren't given any additional context. In &quot;the OoR and Union splits&quot; they mention that their bickering makes WWI worse and possibly start earlier. And in &quot;the Union is super united&quot; they talk about how &quot;improvements to communication and travel&quot; could have helped stop WWI from happening...but gives no further explanation how that works.<br /> <br /> At least it didn't quite go all the way and suggest &quot;if the Union was this united they could have stopped Archduke Ferdinand from being assassinated!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are side boxes, they're not meant to be a detailed explanation on how these things turn out, especially when we're dealing with <i>potential</i> alternate timelines that themselves will depend on the individual table playing. They left that stuff vague because they that with alternate timelines and histories, most Players and Storytellers are going to want to craft them on their own.<br /> <br /> As for the other Conventions in the divided Union outcome, they put the other rival factions against each other. Everyone who knows the Technocracy knows that the NWO and Syndicate have been rivals. Even in VM there's signs of that future rivalry. In a timeline where things got worse for the Order, it's not hard to see it emerge earlier. By that same token, while the Seekers and CM are close if we're dealing with a worse timeline it's not hard imagine that the growing divides in the other Conventions/Blocs would affect them.<br /> <br /> After all in the Rev Ed CBs, there's plenty of talk of a Technocratic Civil War born out of the NWO/Syn rivalry and which Conventions would side with who if it happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -The Hollow Ones write up is bizarre...because this has very little resemblance to the modern day Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> Retcons for why they're called &quot;Hollow Ones&quot; aside (like seriously, even the M20 core write-up implies them being formed out of the &quot;Lost Generation&quot;...a movement post-WWI, almost TWO DECADES after the Victorian era ended!) the write-up describes a group of working class and low-middle class peoples (which would ironically mean they'd get along with the Brotherhood of Mechanicians) split between Marxists and Theosophists. Which...yeah that's actually a really cool idea to have, essentially, a &quot;privileged ally&quot; Craft. They WANT to help marginalized folks, but they have a hard time seeing past their own inherent biases. But...I do not see the modern day Hollow Ones in this Craft at all.<br /> <br /> The weirdest thing is how much the write-up just...chooses not to say anything about the Romanticism or Gothic movements, two literature movements that were integral foundations to the whole Craft. It *hints* at Romanticism when it mentions how &quot;hollow&quot; they felt at the humdrumness brought about by living in the Industrial Revolution and wanted something more. But it just...doesn't want to put its foot down and actually call it Romanticism. And I...really can't think of any reason why the write-up wouldn't mention that. </div> </div> </div>Honestly the idea that modern Hollow Ones are wrong about their origins doesn't affect me. They've always been a disorganized, mercurial Craft, ever changing with the times. Same with them being different in their beliefs from their modern kin. We're dealing with an era of dramatic change, for Sleepers and Awakened alike. A number of Awakened groups are not going to be the same at the end of the age as they were at the start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No mention at all of Gothic literature is incredibly weird since...the Victorian era produced some of the most influential Gothic writers of the time. The works of Charles Dickens. Mary Shelley and &quot;Frankenstein&quot;...and Edgar Allen freakin' Poe. So it's weird that this is glossed over in the Hollow One write-ups.<br /> <br /> Naturally the write-up does not say anything about how the Victorian Hollow Ones transitioned into the modern day incarnation. </div> </div> </div>While I do somewhat agree with you on these points, I also think that it's because those are in line with the modern Hollow Ones we know and they're trying to flesh other factions of the era that we wouldn't really know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 03-19-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:39:39-07:00","id":1440632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440630#post1440630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly the idea that modern Hollow Ones are wrong about their origins doesn't affect.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, but why? What does making these groups the \u201cHollow Ones\u201d instead of keeping that name an Elliot reference and having Victorian era original groups add?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T14:35:13-07:00","id":1440636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440632#post1440632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ok, but why? What does making these groups the \u201cHollow Ones\u201d instead of keeping that name an Elliot reference and having Victorian era original groups add?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for starters it's purely personal for me as like I said, the modern Hollow Ones being mistaken about their origins doesn't affect me. Again, they're a disorganized, mercurial Craft, changing with the times.<br /> <br /> Second, the Victorian Hollow Ones still fill a lot of the same niches as their modern counterparts. Bored, jaded, dissatisfied or nihilistic people, DIY Occultists, Counter Culture, etc. Even the reframing of Hollow One name to refer to the dissatisfaction and emptiness felt by lower class people in this changing, industrializing world is in keeping with themes of the modern Craft, at least for me anyway.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they did strangely downplay the Gothic and Romantic ideas born of the era that would go on to influence them but the stuff they did focus on are other things that also would be completely up the Hollow Ones alley and are consistent things across the Victorian Age.<br /> <br /> Plus it gives Hollow One players a bit more to work with by adding things like the occult societies of the age and Worker and Socialist aspects to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T22:59:41-07:00","id":1440688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440630#post1440630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are side boxes, they're not meant to be a detailed explanation on how these things turn out, especially when we're dealing with <i>potential</i> alternate timelines that themselves will depend on the individual table playing. They left that stuff vague because they that with alternate timelines and histories, most Players and Storytellers are going to want to craft them on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except some of them DO give out detailed information.<br /> <br /> The FF that talks about Etherites staying with the Union lists out the steps that lead to the series of events that leads to the Kopa Loei taking the Seat of Matter. The actual content of the writing isn't very good, but in terms of structure and wordcount that can be realistically devoted to a sidebar leaves me inclined to think they could have gone into more detail and still be concise.<br /> <br /> As is, we're left with a half-written FF that's not really that useful on its own.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the other Conventions in the divided Union outcome, they put the other rival factions against each other. Everyone who knows the Technocracy knows that the NWO and Syndicate have been rivals. Even in VM there's signs of that future rivalry. In a timeline where things got worse for the Order, it's not hard to see it emerge earlier. By that same token, while the Seekers and CM are close if we're dealing with a worse timeline it's not hard imagine that the growing divides in the other Conventions/Blocs would affect them.<br /> <br /> After all in the Rev Ed CBs, there's plenty of talk of a Technocratic Civil War born out of the NWO/Syn rivalry and which Conventions would side with who if it happened. </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that from? Because within the VM text itself, I'm not getting that.<br /> <br /> So far I've found: Lightkeepers getting annoyed at the Invisible Exchequers for taking credit of the US transcontinental railroad...then them having begrudging respect for the IE on how they handle finances. And we also have the Syndicate described as being happy to employ Skeleton Keys on debt collection and thief-catching. If anything, of the Conventions/Blocs they do have an issue with includes: LKs thinking the CM and EE is wasting time and money on frivolous projects, or the SKs pissing off the BoM and EEs for their involvement in worker strike busts.<br /> <br /> I at least broadly understand Grand Faculty vs League of Constructors being disagreeing on Theory vs Application. But Syndicate vs IT/NWO? Not seeing it here. And while I'll concede that going back to the text, that it does have context on CMs siding with the Syndicate: that due to IT/NWO not taking their ventures seriously but Syndicate does...but that through line is not referenced in the sidebar itself. I had to play detective just to find that connection. And frankly, your book is not laid out well if you need to flip back and forth between pages because the information and context is not where it should be.<br /> <br /> Even then...that's bad form to expect incoming players and STs picking up this book, especially if they're brand new to Mage, to just...know the context delivered in past books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly the idea that modern Hollow Ones are wrong about their origins doesn't affect me. They've always been a disorganized, mercurial Craft, ever changing with the times. Same with them being different in their beliefs from their modern kin. We're dealing with an era of dramatic change, for Sleepers and Awakened alike. A number of Awakened groups are not going to be the same at the end of the age as they were at the start.<br /> <br /> While I do somewhat agree with you on these points, I also think that it's because those are in line with the modern Hollow Ones we know and they're trying to flesh other factions of the era that we wouldn't really know about. </div> </div> </div>I don't buy that, simply because the writing of the Hollow Ones write-up isn't really explicit that it's an in-character, unreliable narrator. And again, their write-up making no reference to how they transition into their modern day form doesn't help this. I do appreciate VM fleshing out other factions...but I do not prefer them muddying the waters with past factions in a way that I honestly don't think anyone really asked for. <br /> <br /> If this was Changeling I'd be more accepting of it via &quot;the Mists did it!&quot;, but it's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T23:33:04-07:00","id":1440689,"title":"","content":"Anyways more Stretch goals.<br /> <br /> $90k: Art budget increase<br /> <br /> $95k: ...more VTT tokens and assets. <br /> <br /> Ok is there some wider context that I'm missing? Is VTT really that hugely popular right now to justify having Stretch Goals this late into the campaign for? Especially with Mage/WoD, with my read being that they're the games that are...not exactly my first choice when it comes to tactical combat simulation, at least on par with D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Because...speaking for myself, I don't ever see myself using VTT at all with Mage/WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T06:30:43-07:00","id":1440709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440689#post1440689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok is there some wider context that I'm missing? Is VTT really that hugely popular right now to justify having Stretch Goals this late into the campaign for? Especially with Mage/WoD, with my read being that they're the games that are...not exactly my first choice when it comes to tactical combat simulation, at least on par with D&amp;D?</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD was the 7th most popular setting/rules set on Roll20 in quarter 4 of 2020, and the 9th largest for growth, according to the stats <a href=\"https://blog.roll20.net/posts/the-orr-group-industry-report-q4-2020-8-million-users-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">Roll20</a> released. So suggest that VTT is popular and growing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T07:48:03-07:00","id":1440717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440689#post1440689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok is there some wider context that I'm missing? Is VTT really that hugely popular right now to justify having Stretch Goals this late into the campaign for? Especially with Mage/WoD, with my read being that they're the games that are...not exactly my first choice when it comes to tactical combat simulation, at least on par with D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Because...speaking for myself, I don't ever see myself using VTT at all with Mage/WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nearly all gaming people have done in the past year has been virtual, so it's a good idea for us to support that play style.<br /> <br /> It might not be your thing in particular, and that's fine, but it would be foolish of us not to be aware of the general trend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T10:35:57-07:00","id":1440734,"title":"","content":"I just really hope we\u2019re getting more Mage group info woven into the Gazateer chapter, because as it stands, House Tharsis for example is spoken of in terms of being significant to the plot of the era and we know literally nothing about them (or very very little if you have the Revised Order of Hermes book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T20:54:43-07:00","id":1440803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440717#post1440717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nearly all gaming people have done in the past year has been virtual, so it's a good idea for us to support that play style.<br /> <br /> It might not be your thing in particular, and that's fine, but it would be foolish of us not to be aware of the general trend.</div> </div> </div> </div>But will it still be a thing when the book comes out in what 2 years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T03:32:47-07:00","id":1440821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440803#post1440803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But will it still be a thing when the book comes out in what 2 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly presume that not a small amount of people actually found new groups and friends online over the last year or so - not just connecting to their RL friends.<br /> So yeah, I personally think the overall amount of online RP happening will have increased.<br /> But I might be biased. I've been RPing online since the early 2000's <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T13:42:40-07:00","id":1440855,"title":"","content":"Finished reading Chapter 5 and considering this and some things I've skimmed from reading ahead...<br /> <br /> I get the distinct impression that at some point, VM WAS intended to be a standalone corebook comparable to DAV20. But then the decision was made to turn it into just a historical setting book...but they didn't remove all the artifacts of being a standalone corebook all the way.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to break down how the various Traits like Abilities and Backgrounds operate differently in this time period (which, yeah I'm fine with that). But to go as far as...explaining how to make a character concept? Or a deep dive in the Spark of Life section? That seems unnecessary with a book that's supposed to be <i>just</i> a historical era supplement. And of the stuff in the Character Concept and Spark of Life devotes way too much wordcount to explaining it in its most basic sense: either retreading how M20 core explains it, or as something that players and STs could have deduced themselves, and too little wordcount to explain how the Character Concept or Spark of Life would be different in Victorian era versus modern day M20. It'd be one thing if this was a standalone corebook and be understandable if the expectation was to only run a VM chronicle using just this book...but it isn't.<br /> <br /> Another glaring element being that it even does structure <i>a</i> character creation process, step by step, and yet with the Attributes and Abilities steps, just points you towards M20 core.<br /> <br /> And in general I am disappointed that there isn't anything in the way of brand new Abilities, Backgrounds, Merits, or Flaws.<br /> <br /> (no, no I do not count the &quot;Well-Rounded&quot; Merit, because all that does is provide an alternative to the regular &quot;Well-Skilled Craftsmen&quot; rule)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T02:07:53-07:00","id":1440915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1439998#post1439998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Zulu mechanists are all well and good; but the interesting thing about the Awalaye and Wamukamwami is that they were technomancers, too; and not in reaction to the Order the way the Zulu mechanists were. One of them was described as knowing secrets about the Ether that the Electrodyne Engineers didn't know, and that being a be sufficient reason why the EEs were pissed that the Void Seekers attacked them. Central Africans, technomancers, and technomancers in their own right rather than as a response to the Union. I really don't see why they weren't given a write-up of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sources on the Awalaye and Wamukamwami?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T02:10:43-07:00","id":1440916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1440855#post1440855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in general I am disappointed that there isn't anything in the way of brand new Abilities, Backgrounds, Merits, or Flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there era appropriate concepts you feel are I represented and need new mechanics?<br /> <br /> Because I\u2019m definitely in favor of not wasting word count on new mechanics created for the sake of new mechanics that don\u2019t add something needed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T12:02:39-07:00","id":1441278,"title":"","content":"And of course only NOW I get teased with a stretch goal supplement I actually want to get built..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T15:21:19-07:00","id":1441311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1441278#post1441278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course only NOW I get teased with a stretch goal supplement I actually want to get built..</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. <br /> <br /> Time period-specific rotes and Wonders are FAR more useful to know versus plot hooks and NPCs. <br /> <br /> Not even from a KEWL powers perspective, but just from a \u201chey, can you show me an example in action of what Victorian magick looks like versus modern day magick?\u201d perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T07:37:15-07:00","id":1442837,"title":"","content":"Reading through it I find the Victorian era far better for play than the modern era. One of my biggest struggles with getting my head around what to di with mage has always been that the order of reason have essentially won the war already, and magic (the whole reason for playing mage) is difficult to pull off as a result. Even the idea of reality being malleable is only a technicality in the modern era. <br /> the Victorian era, with the ascension war still raging and the world split into a rich tapestry of reality zones where different kinds of magic hold away, really seems to shine. Here mages can genuinely shape reality, and can impact the setting in epically meaningful ways while doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T14:00:07-07:00","id":1442881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1435611-victorian-mage-will-be-crowdfunded-by-opp-on-indiegogo-instead-of-ks?p=1442837#post1442837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through it I find the Victorian era far better for play than the modern era. One of my biggest struggles with getting my head around what to di with mage has always been that the order of reason have essentially won the war already, and magic (the whole reason for playing mage) is difficult to pull off as a result. Even the idea of reality being malleable is only a technicality in the modern era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...not really?<br /> <br /> M20 stresses the idea that no, even in modern day, the Technocratic paradigm isn't really that dominant and that there's a mix of mystic and technological beliefs in play (Rise of the Extraordinary Citizen, M20 p. 133)<br /> <br /> And Paradox in M20...is really not that big of a deal. Successful vulgar magick only gets you 1 Paradox point. You only get a lot of Paradox if you botch a vulgar magick roll. So unless if your character is doing nothing but throwing out vulgar magick and not taking measures to at least reduce the Difficulty of the rolls down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T02:02:51-07:00","id":1442943,"title":"","content":"Agreed... to an excellent, but that is a far cry from witches flying broomsticks over the English moors because that is still the paradigm there. <br /> in Victoria mage I can quickly see the story potential of mages defending a territory from corrupting influences, or trying to &quot;terraform&quot; an enemy stronghold to be more hospitable, or even to take it away. Maybe 20 attempted to go down those lines, but with the weight of the modern technocratic paradigm it just doesn't play out as easily. <br /> it also helps that we know ho history &quot;should&quot; play out, so it is easy to see how epic and far reaching changes to the setting are by showing history diverging from what it should be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T01:22:17-07:00","id":1443096,"title":"","content":"Victorian Mage is now available for preorder from BackerKit, and we'll be counting preorders for the next ~60 days towards stretch goals.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://victorian-mage-ttrpg.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">https://victorian-mage-ttrpg.backerk...sted_preorders</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}